"811fecc11972730811d0d6dda9f13a21ac8a5771"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"martmull","providerType":"User"},"email":"martmull@hotmail.fr","name":"martmull"},"authoredDate":"2026-06-24T18:00:59Z","committedDate":"2026-06-24T18:00:59Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:32:32.988Z","repositoryId":1282265539,"sha":"14e4656fe3b00268a1431436a7de5a917fde35f1"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"Bonapara","providerType":"User"},"email":"tdesfrancs@gmail.com","name":"Thomas des Francs"},"authoredDate":"2026-06-24T17:15:01Z","committedDate":"2026-06-24T17:15:01Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:32:32.988Z","repositoryId":1282265539,"sha":"e22d31c55389cb61de5e46604706f50269f891da"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"charlesBochet","providerType":"User"},"email":"charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Bochet"},"authoredDate":"2026-06-24T17:14:19Z","committedDate":"2026-06-24T17:14:19Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:32:32.988Z","repositoryId":1282265539,"sha":"ad61d6d8a3d8105fb747ec7766dd1027699cd09a"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"bosiraphael","providerType":"User"},"email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"authoredDate":"2026-06-24T17:13:20Z","committedDate":"2026-06-24T17:13:20Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:32:32.988Z","repositoryId":1282265539,"sha":"02120aac42a65ce2db85ab5b904d7c2109dd1b06"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","providerType":"Bot"},"email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"authoredDate":"2026-06-24T17:09:14Z","committedDate":"2026-06-24T17:09:14Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:32:32.988Z","repositoryId":1282265539,"sha":"fdea2d6e1e27a5f349d08df4f49d3062f94ece57"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:32:32.988Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/2a21eb46c09cbacb913abf79870b127544462d97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T13:12:43Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T13:12:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: cap to-many relation records per parent and inline chips in table (#22206)\n\n## Problem\n\nRecord table views that show a to-many relation column (e.g. Workflows\nwith a \"Runs\" column) get slow and janky to scroll when some records\nhave many related records.\n\nTwo root causes, found by profiling the page live:\n\n1. **Backend over-fetch + unfairness.** Nested one-to-many relations\nwere loaded with a single flat limit of `QUERY_MAX_RECORDS_FROM_RELATION\n* parentCount` shared across *all* parents in the page (`WHERE\nparentColumn IN (ids) LIMIT 60*N`, no per-parent cap). A single hot\nparent can consume the entire budget — returning thousands of rows for\none cell, and potentially starving sibling parents of records they\nactually have. The `limit * parentCount` shape shows the original intent\n*was* a per-parent budget; it was just implemented as a global limit.\n\n2. **Frontend DOM explosion.** `ExpandableList` mounts the *entire*\nchild array inline (clipped with `overflow: hidden`) when unfocused, and\nmounts all children for measurement when focused. A cell with 2,000+\nrelation chips mounts ~14k DOM nodes — one observed page reached ~55k\nnodes for 43 rows, producing 100–300 ms main-thread long tasks on every\nscroll.\n\n## Fix\n\n- **Backend:** load one-to-many relations with a true **per-parent** cap\nvia a `LATERAL` join — each parent runs its own indexed, `LIMIT`-ed scan\nthat stops after the per-parent budget. This is `O(perParentLimit ×\nparentCount)` and never reads or sorts a parent''s full relation set. The\nper-parent query is built through the workspace query builder (so it\nstays schema-qualified and keeps the soft-delete predicate) and wrapped\nas a `FROM` subquery; read/row-level permissions are enforced when\nrecords are hydrated by id, as elsewhere in the relation loader.\nMany-to-one is unchanged.\n- **Frontend:** add an opt-in `maxInlineCount` to `ExpandableList` so\nto-many relation cells mount only a small inline preview; the expand\ndropdown still renders the full fetched set. Fully backward compatible\n(no cap → identical behavior).\n\n## Why LATERAL over a window function\n\nA windowed `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY parent) <= limit` is correct\nand fair too, but a window function **cannot stop early within a\npartition** — it must read every matching row (and sort it). Measured on\nskewed data (one parent with ~4k children, on the existing single-column\njoin index, PG16):\n\n| Approach | Time | Buffers | Rows read from the hot partition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Pre-PR (`LIMIT 60×N`) | 1.6 ms | 91 | ~180 total, early-stops, but\n**unfair** (starves siblings) |\n| Window (`ROW_NUMBER`) | 3.7 ms | 128 | **all ~4k + sort** |\n| **LATERAL (`per-parent LIMIT`)** | **0.5 ms** | **57** | **~60, index\nearly-stop** |\n\nLATERAL matches the pre-PR read cost while being fair, needs no new\nindex, and scales independently of how large any single relation is.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Backend integration test (`nested-relation-per-parent-limit`): a\nparent with 65 children is capped at 60 while a sibling with 3 keeps all\n3 — passes.\n- `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` on the generated SQL: Index Scan with the `LIMIT`\npushed into the per-parent lateral (early-stop).\n- Frontend unit test for the `ExpandableList` cap.\n- Manual check on a table cell with 40 related records: exactly 10 chips\nmount inline (down from 40), no console errors, chips still clickable\nand the overflow count reflects the true total.","tree":{"sha":"1efd263f81c0b1918d9d2ae66c5beb41e77a69e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/1efd263f81c0b1918d9d2ae66c5beb41e77a69e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/2a21eb46c09cbacb913abf79870b127544462d97","verification":{"payload":"tree 1efd263f81c0b1918d9d2ae66c5beb41e77a69e0\nparent 4840233a1cddf1f3c06867a820a95955be965381\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1782565963 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782565963 +0200\n\nperf: cap to-many relation records per parent and inline chips in table (#22206)\n\n## Problem\n\nRecord table views that show a to-many relation column (e.g. Workflows\nwith a \"Runs\" column) get slow and janky to scroll when some records\nhave many related records.\n\nTwo root causes, found by profiling the page live:\n\n1. **Backend over-fetch + unfairness.** Nested one-to-many relations\nwere loaded with a single flat limit of `QUERY_MAX_RECORDS_FROM_RELATION\n* parentCount` shared across *all* parents in the page (`WHERE\nparentColumn IN (ids) LIMIT 60*N`, no per-parent cap). A single hot\nparent can consume the entire budget — returning thousands of rows for\none cell, and potentially starving sibling parents of records they\nactually have. The `limit * parentCount` shape shows the original intent\n*was* a per-parent budget; it was just implemented as a global limit.\n\n2. **Frontend DOM explosion.** `ExpandableList` mounts the *entire*\nchild array inline (clipped with `overflow: hidden`) when unfocused, and\nmounts all children for measurement when focused. A cell with 2,000+\nrelation chips mounts ~14k DOM nodes — one observed page reached ~55k\nnodes for 43 rows, producing 100–300 ms main-thread long tasks on every\nscroll.\n\n## Fix\n\n- **Backend:** load one-to-many relations with a true **per-parent** cap\nvia a `LATERAL` join — each parent runs its own indexed, `LIMIT`-ed scan\nthat stops after the per-parent budget. This is `O(perParentLimit ×\nparentCount)` and never reads or sorts a parent''s full relation set. The\nper-parent query is built through the workspace query builder (so it\nstays schema-qualified and keeps the soft-delete predicate) and wrapped\nas a `FROM` subquery; read/row-level permissions are enforced when\nrecords are hydrated by id, as elsewhere in the relation loader.\nMany-to-one is unchanged.\n- **Frontend:** add an opt-in `maxInlineCount` to `ExpandableList` so\nto-many relation cells mount only a small inline preview; the expand\ndropdown still renders the full fetched set. Fully backward compatible\n(no cap → identical behavior).\n\n## Why LATERAL over a window function\n\nA windowed `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY parent) <= limit` is correct\nand fair too, but a window function **cannot stop early within a\npartition** — it must read every matching row (and sort it). Measured on\nskewed data (one parent with ~4k children, on the existing single-column\njoin index, PG16):\n\n| Approach | Time | Buffers | Rows read from the hot partition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Pre-PR (`LIMIT 60×N`) | 1.6 ms | 91 | ~180 total, early-stops, but\n**unfair** (starves siblings) |\n| Window (`ROW_NUMBER`) | 3.7 ms | 128 | **all ~4k + sort** |\n| **LATERAL (`per-parent LIMIT`)** | **0.5 ms** | **57** | **~60, index\nearly-stop** |\n\nLATERAL matches the pre-PR read cost while being fair, needs no new\nindex, and scales independently of how large any single relation is.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Backend integration test (`nested-relation-per-parent-limit`): a\nparent with 65 children is capped at 60 while a sibling with 3 keeps all\n3 — passes.\n- `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` on the generated SQL: Index Scan with the `LIMIT`\npushed into the per-parent lateral (early-stop).\n- Frontend unit test for the `ExpandableList` cap.\n- Manual check on a table cell with 40 related records: exactly 10 chips\nmount inline (down from 40), no console errors, chips still clickable\nand the overflow count reflects the true total.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqP8xLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7CAQAD/REaa5BcxGAKY9GfcOp6y0\n6qX3Stqk8dbVgBtPmTItKLMaBkwFFLSuSVVIkdVkwERtnDe46lfqP7y1oSEU7VMM\nZbLIUB6Zd119u0HBgXtDErrJjzg/s5GL/sUPXsrTJwMgKQd8NNqBBynoCj5ZQSJY\nZJ+++MriEq2Qro7LWF1IMpOh3skeqINwCnchvjafrEkZE1HoIe4uLkXKQbnCtN7x\nr/tC69LyXGt0MDXIGmUuULzsbqBOF2Toe+vQQyrOK6iXjAHRT6c9PsvbvdZUX5or\npwoJhAkee8Lf3JlvkhBDuyWEB+p3/oQ8CUoNxvjplPv5xMl9vMVJ/U/cHUTNgHsJ\nmkKakXMz5/+r1Ew4JDvdyAHikReQ3HfIOma9DEUVT7XSOmBPmjqXcZh7+LkO3jkB\nC4weEFV69fBcQXj5kO3AiMYptctF7QVViDv31wL6iTHYEUeZrd9QfCVjA4kEz1bT\nqeX/tw/rYcuq8xwZ9fjzNbHnlEYnqghimsDPc7u1tDYGZAwF8Ums//N6zzBRTl1D\nxJxG/T2zY6Z1QR0qkPxPSm1Oc8ytYDyLJ3m+qbDrQtmUydrueCqV2eGDT5F7Owbr\n892ENh3Z3sf4lWCV38cv8QTkQykplwwI5dO9CyFIDyz4UDhL9DoOEcassuhEp/ia\nT818mtb61Z6G0SoOmJiA\n=hAGo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","