gin":"mabdullahabaid","node_id":"U_kgDOB3UeMQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/d58ec64e10b407ceef012b581e6100f73da6928c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-26T16:45:39Z","email":"125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdullah."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T16:45:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(website): swap product Demo for a register Signoff; make signoff headings width-driven (#22232)\n\n## Summary\n\nReworks the product page''s closing section, and in doing so makes every\nsignoff closer width-driven.\n\n### 1. Replace the Demo section with a register Signoff (`6a5f0c34bf`)\n\nThe product page ended on a static `AppPreview` mockup (\"Try it live\").\nSwap it for the shared `Signoff` closer — a focused register CTA, the\nsame component the customers / why-twenty / partners pages use — so the\npage ends by driving sign-ups instead of re-showing the product.\n\n- New `ProductSignoff`: heading \"Start moving faster today.\", a\nsupporting line, and the **Get started + Talk to us** pair (matching\n`CustomersCatalogSignoff`). Uses `SITE_URLS.appWelcome` per the\nsite-urls rule rather than inlining the URL.\n- Removes the now-unused `product-demo` section and its 192KB background\nasset.\n\n### 2. Make Signoff headings width-driven (`0365c0d2ea`)\n\nThe signoff headings forced their two-line break with a literal `\\n` in\nthe translated string — against the site''s typography principle (fluid\ntype + `text-wrap: balance`, no `<br>`).\n\n- `Signoff` now carries one default **`615px`** heading measure; all\nfive closers drop `\\n`.\n- The width was **measured, not guessed**: each heading was rendered\nheadlessly in the real production fonts (Aleo 300 body, Host Grotesk 300\naccent — each heading mixes both) at the desktop size with `text-wrap:\nbalance`, then I found the common window where every heading breaks\nidentically: whyTwenty `[565–820]`, customers `[425–800]`, partner\n`[380–730]`, product `[380–660]` — `615` sits in all of them. Each was\nthen verified to reproduce its exact current break at 615px.\n- **Affects 4 other pages** (why-twenty, customers, customers/[slug],\npartners) — all verified to render identically, and headings now reflow\non narrow viewports instead of being pinned by `\\n`.\n- Drops the one-off `headingMaxWidth` prop (now unused).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- oxfmt, oxlint, check-conventions, typecheck — all green.\n- Headless measurement confirms all five signoff headings reproduce\ntheir current desktop break at 615px (no visual regression).\n- Visually confirmed the product closer and the four sibling signoffs.","tree":{"sha":"23fa9278137261d2e40c47b2d6da6dd3f133d3fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/23fa9278137261d2e40c47b2d6da6dd3f133d3fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/d58ec64e10b407ceef012b581e6100f73da6928c","verification":{"payload":"tree 23fa9278137261d2e40c47b2d6da6dd3f133d3fb\nparent e747bc3e4271f79605b695b4504b6ab4a659eb6e\nauthor Abdullah. <125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com> 1782492339 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782492339 +0200\n\nfeat(website): swap product Demo for a register Signoff; make signoff headings width-driven (#22232)\n\n## Summary\n\nReworks the product page''s closing section, and in doing so makes every\nsignoff closer width-driven.\n\n### 1. Replace the Demo section with a register Signoff (`6a5f0c34bf`)\n\nThe product page ended on a static `AppPreview` mockup (\"Try it live\").\nSwap it for the shared `Signoff` closer — a focused register CTA, the\nsame component the customers / why-twenty / partners pages use — so the\npage ends by driving sign-ups instead of re-showing the product.\n\n- New `ProductSignoff`: heading \"Start moving faster today.\", a\nsupporting line, and the **Get started + Talk to us** pair (matching\n`CustomersCatalogSignoff`). Uses `SITE_URLS.appWelcome` per the\nsite-urls rule rather than inlining the URL.\n- Removes the now-unused `product-demo` section and its 192KB background\nasset.\n\n### 2. Make Signoff headings width-driven (`0365c0d2ea`)\n\nThe signoff headings forced their two-line break with a literal `\\n` in\nthe translated string — against the site''s typography principle (fluid\ntype + `text-wrap: balance`, no `<br>`).\n\n- `Signoff` now carries one default **`615px`** heading measure; all\nfive closers drop `\\n`.\n- The width was **measured, not guessed**: each heading was rendered\nheadlessly in the real production fonts (Aleo 300 body, Host Grotesk 300\naccent — each heading mixes both) at the desktop size with `text-wrap:\nbalance`, then I found the common window where every heading breaks\nidentically: whyTwenty `[565–820]`, customers `[425–800]`, partner\n`[380–730]`, product `[380–660]` — `615` sits in all of them. Each was\nthen verified to reproduce its exact current break at 615px.\n- **Affects 4 other pages** (why-twenty, customers, customers/[slug],\npartners) — all verified to render identically, and headings now reflow\non narrow viewports instead of being pinned by `\\n`.\n- Drops the one-off `headingMaxWidth` prop (now unused).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- oxfmt, oxlint, check-conventions, typecheck — all green.\n- Headless measurement confirms all five signoff headings reproduce\ntheir current desktop break at 615px (no visual regression).\n- Visually confirmed the product closer and the four sibling signoffs.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPqyzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq7kQAHdvL288XXYG+Gaxueybmzk0\naDEX0WYQrJAcrBTCsfHXvr2h+VE3dUPbbEcrls2160yC29rsUDZV8I0GsnkFtI7x\njFKgRGCTavQLo6i9JfJ8kkX6fLZ9Gt9ZOdCXCCDk44l7eOIVlQyRSaM9Y8JAg6fY\n2Un2sfiG74YTsOp+tkMLctEnMv+qqnQhuxIR/USkcGJWBF9z1qPuQ+5RbeiZnR+6\nm3ZaNZTl7M6pS4l4nD2C6ijQ+teRWeW8sUZJK40Kb2F4GXaO0sJpUxIB0mXomnJt\nVlKiNtqEC1bhppegWYBjqUhQyiy64r+cv11LqSsWtnO/5SEkYU+jqrv0U7vvqQnD\npaB5BZJuVJxHNskYlUXwSXghQNI8LMhrqRoX1LznOJPY49rEpPGZ3bZfm0fT35sL\n7I8eqT2NR9pOrNIeL+TAce36RAJurZxezUtpF3+ld3/f8cJIkv5t0mnctx97Iu5b\ns7aFC156m0jjCy/9k35C9IpTIFNIlpxhR7iRknG5NyUmcLJtzUJA3qQ5D0HiHZwP\nowGB4OcAlVebjz25LfAHhKEsTlL2phrskuxnmb57rLxMaGOwa8XFJnfNEF6P/mDC\nm2PLUodWD50EI1OO1sSe/Pr7tBsx8sTBUfKLATGSduD7T3CUUHRZpOvdvQczgddZ\np/CDsSjQd63JCEDLuWJ8\n=HMIt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T14:47:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/d58ec64e10b407ceef012b581e6100f73da6928c","node_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKGQ1OGVjNjRlMTBiNDA3Y2VlZjAxMmI1ODFlNjEwMGY3M2RhNjkyOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/e747bc3e4271f79605b695b4504b6ab4a659eb6e","sha":"e747bc3e4271f79605b695b4504b6ab4a659eb6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/e747bc3e4271f79605b695b4504b6ab4a659eb6e"}],"sha":"d58ec64e10b407ceef012b581e6100f73da6928c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/d58ec64e10b407ceef012b581e6100f73da6928c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29927851?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/martmull","id":29927851,"login":"martmull","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI3ODUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/e747bc3e4271f79605b695b4504b6ab4a659eb6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-26T16:21:27Z","email":"martmull@hotmail.fr","name":"martmull"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T16:21:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add backfill installation feature for pre-installed apps (#22199)\n\n## After\n\n<img width=\"1070\" height=\"514\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9cbd2ff5-1678-4c2f-84da-074568f37c51\"\n/>\n\n\n## Summary\nAdds the ability to backfill application installations across all\nexisting workspaces. This allows admins to retroactively install a\npre-registered application on every active and suspended workspace\nthrough a background job, making the feature idempotent and\nnon-blocking.\n\n## Key Changes\n\n- **Backend Service**: Added `backfillApplicationOnAllWorkspaces()`\nmethod to `PreInstalledAppsService` that:\n  - Validates the application registration exists\n  - Iterates through all workspaces using `WorkspaceIteratorService`\n  - Installs the app on each workspace\n  - Swallows `APP_ALREADY_INSTALLED` errors for idempotency\n  - Logs success/failure counts\n\n- **Background Job**: Created `BackfillApplicationInstallationJob` to\nprocess backfill requests asynchronously via the message queue\n\n- **GraphQL Mutation**: Added `backfillApplicationInstallation` mutation\nto `AdminPanelResolver` that:\n  - Validates the application registration exists\n  - Enqueues the background job\n  - Returns immediately without blocking the request\n\n- **UI Components**: Enhanced\n`SettingsAdminApplicationRegistrationGeneralToggles` with:\n- New \"Pre-install on new workspaces\" toggle for the `isPreInstalled`\nflag\n  - \"Backfill on all workspaces\" button with confirmation modal\n  - Loading state and success/error snack bar feedback\n\n- **Data Model**: Added `isPreInstalled` field to\n`UpdateApplicationRegistrationPayload` input type\n\n- **Tests**: Added comprehensive unit tests for\n`PreInstalledAppsService.backfillApplicationOnAllWorkspaces()` covering:\n  - Missing registration validation\n  - Successful multi-workspace installation\n  - Idempotent handling of already-installed errors\n  - Proper error propagation for unexpected failures\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nThe backfill operation is designed to be:\n- **Idempotent**: Already-installed apps are skipped without error\n- **Non-blocking**: Runs as a background job via message queue\n- **Resilient**: Per-workspace failures don''t block other installations\n- **Observable**: Logs aggregated success/failure counts for monitoring\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22199?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: cubic-dev-ai[bot] <191113872+cubic-dev-ai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"78d28c9b5426016cb5c1d30532e4a12edaf51bec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/78d28c9b5426016cb5c1d30532e4a12edaf51bec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/e747bc3e4271f79605b695b4504b6ab4a659eb6e","verification":{"payload":"tree 78d28c9b5426016cb5c1d30532e4a12edaf51bec\nparent fea2b8736fef4bbdfd095773ffab5e5e1351da45\nauthor martmull <martmull@hotmail.fr> 1782490887 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782490887 +0000\n\nAdd backfill installation feature for pre-installed apps (#22199)\n\n## After\n\n<img width=\"1070\" height=\"514\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9cbd2ff5-1678-4c2f-84da-074568f37c51\"\n/>\n\n\n## Summary\nAdds the ability to backfill application installations across all\nexisting workspaces. This allows admins to retroactively install a\npre-registered application on every active and suspended workspace\nthrough a background job, making the feature idempotent and\nnon-blocking.\n\n## Key Changes\n\n- **Backend Service**: Added `backfillApplicationOnAllWorkspaces()`\nmethod to `PreInstalledAppsService` that:\n  - Validates the application registration exists\n  - Iterates through all workspaces using `WorkspaceIteratorService`\n  - Installs the app on each workspace\n  - Swallows `APP_ALREADY_INSTALLED` errors for idempotency\n  - Logs success/failure counts\n\n- **Background Job**: Created `BackfillApplicationInstallationJob` to\nprocess backfill requests asynchronously via the message queue\n\n- **GraphQL Mutation**: Added `backfillApplicationInstallation` mutation\nto `AdminPanelResolver` that:\n  - Validates the application registration exists\n  - Enqueues the background job\n  - Returns immediately without blocking the request\n\n- **UI Components**: Enhanced\n`SettingsAdminApplicationRegistrationGeneralToggles` with:\n- New \"Pre-install on new workspaces\" toggle for the `isPreInstalled`\nflag\n  - \"Backfill on all workspaces\" button with confirmation modal\n  - Loading state and success/error snack bar feedback\n\n- **Data Model**: Added `isPreInstalled` field to\n`UpdateApplicationRegistrationPayload` input type\n\n- **Tests**: Added comprehensive unit tests for\n`PreInstalledAppsService.backfillApplicationOnAllWorkspaces()` covering:\n  - Missing registration validation\n  - Successful multi-workspace installation\n  - Idempotent handling of already-installed errors\n  - Proper error propagation for unexpected failures\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nThe backfill operation is designed to be:\n- **Idempotent**: Already-installed apps are skipped without error\n- **Non-blocking**: Runs as a background job via message queue\n- **Resilient**: Per-workspace failures don''t block other installations\n- **Observable**: Logs aggregated success/failure counts for monitoring\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22199?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: cubic-dev-ai[bot] <191113872+cubic-dev-ai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPqcHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAr0AQAFCFi59ciM+aTZbpdlXQfpTp\nx1EdZy2ITmsaPOJL7PXrJg0tVPo9K/dGX1+KssAbo3L6x5iw67GPu9VV/I3l3C5r\nP/f318opf9G5VPyXOvvVAVWlqiJ1+5JNqXDNUCA/YvJuMS/5DpxBGy3o2KmYFsX9\nK/kh+W54vN6bPHCfDPVLS6dZXvJO/rw0nCY3FZBjlzzjE2sJirRhj2r6OS9KvFJC\nwDWIpfzXyFLdkDg4ki56UBoPl+L7RBfoQsH35ePk3MY4lULxtVGCxE92dEaSAZU/\n9ipOIllLHR3NWRaFaRNuxV22p48H9jwRJ+NRzqdIVD28Y8v/sTwz+VcHox2/t5RR\nihI9Ap8nHRh3s+8/Qob1JJ1Bh2k4xj8zmm8y+vPD2NxY7t8Rcnj1WaKX/4wozN2m\nMwxucqjCbufP2KXGxKZQLWGQ+4RiyoF2iLmCG5Uczy1lSuooMi1ofatP22SCpGsP\nGZWpbmRtAbJto+4dv12stkk7EhLxwoT6G0lTujTG1wA8fZlsGqd/tRVn1s/Tqsmh\nxmi+xe7r8T9Yi5Y41r8yMU4z14XkZhaKizdc1gmWLADg7DUyOlmwJaVHJAby4QGk\nHKYrAUaB4opOSJlhQ5Lemk4men8VLBrlfWCfbTGtwBBTRtiSNa+7SBvgiEO36wBJ\nt5Rzy1iVeGkA9XhY9LrW\n=aWj/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T14:47:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/e747bc3e4271f79605b695b4504b6ab4a659eb6e","node_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKGU3NDdiYzNlNDI3MWY3OTYwNWI2OTViNDUwNGI2YWI0YTY1OWViNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/fea2b8736fef4bbdfd095773ffab5e5e1351da45","sha":"fea2b8736fef4bbdfd095773ffab5e5e1351da45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/fea2b8736fef4bbdfd095773ffab5e5e1351da45"}],"sha":"e747bc3e4271f79605b695b4504b6ab4a659eb6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/e747bc3e4271f79605b695b4504b6ab4a659eb6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125115953?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mabdullahabaid","id":125115953,"login":"mabdullahabaid","node_id":"U_kgDOB3UeMQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/fea2b8736fef4bbdfd095773ffab5e5e1351da45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-26T15:57:21Z","email":"125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdullah."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T15:57:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(website): rebuild dashboard visual faithful to twenty-front (#22218)\n\nRebuilds the product-feature **DashboardVisual** to mirror\ntwenty-front''s dashboard widgets, with colors traced to twenty-front''s\nactual source rather than eyeballed.\n\n## Widgets\n- **Bar — \"Deals by month\"**: single-series `blue8` (twenty-front''s\n`GRAPH_DEFAULT_COLOR`), dashed `4 4` gridlines, value labels, nice\nrounded Y-ticks. Replaces the old stacked bar (stacked bars aren''t used\nin twenty-front).\n- **Donut — \"Deals by stage\"**: the real opportunity pipeline\n(New/Screening/Meeting/Proposal/Customer), each segment colored by that\nstage option''s own color from the metadata\n(`red/purple/sky/turquoise/yellow`), with a center total and a paginated\nhorizontal legend.\n- **KPIs**: big-number cards (Revenue YTD / Avg deal size / Win rate).\n\n## Responsive — `mediaUp(''md'')`\nThe dashboard is the full-width spotlight tile, whose frame is short\nbelow md and grows to 420px at md+. So the layout keys off md: below it\ncollapses to **2-up KPIs + a full-width bar** (donut and the 3rd KPI\nhidden, smaller breadcrumb), and the spotlight frame''s mobile min-height\nis bumped so the bar has room; at md+ the full 3-KPI + side-by-side\nlayout returns. The donut caps at its size and shrinks with its\ncontainer.\n\n## Notes\n- Follows the `product-feature` conventions (per-visual folder,\none-export-per-file, split types).\n- `Tiles.tsx`: one-line spotlight mobile min-height bump (only the\ndashboard uses the spotlight tile).\n- typecheck + lint + build all green.\n\n<img width=\"1148\" height=\"638\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1eb8f120-88c2-45d1-adf9-ec00abe11006\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"89aaadd986dff7803a6bd6ba4915797b242c29b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/89aaadd986dff7803a6bd6ba4915797b242c29b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/fea2b8736fef4bbdfd095773ffab5e5e1351da45","verification":{"payload":"tree 89aaadd986dff7803a6bd6ba4915797b242c29b5\nparent 8a257e0de3ffe81adae8f825b2eb85815ffe5968\nauthor Abdullah. <125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com> 1782489441 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782489441 +0500\n\nfeat(website): rebuild dashboard visual faithful to twenty-front (#22218)\n\nRebuilds the product-feature **DashboardVisual** to mirror\ntwenty-front''s dashboard widgets, with colors traced to twenty-front''s\nactual source rather than eyeballed.\n\n## Widgets\n- **Bar — \"Deals by month\"**: single-series `blue8` (twenty-front''s\n`GRAPH_DEFAULT_COLOR`), dashed `4 4` gridlines, value labels, nice\nrounded Y-ticks. Replaces the old stacked bar (stacked bars aren''t used\nin twenty-front).\n- **Donut — \"Deals by stage\"**: the real opportunity pipeline\n(New/Screening/Meeting/Proposal/Customer), each segment colored by that\nstage option''s own color from the metadata\n(`red/purple/sky/turquoise/yellow`), with a center total and a paginated\nhorizontal legend.\n- **KPIs**: big-number cards (Revenue YTD / Avg deal size / Win rate).\n\n## Responsive — `mediaUp(''md'')`\nThe dashboard is the full-width spotlight tile, whose frame is short\nbelow md and grows to 420px at md+. So the layout keys off md: below it\ncollapses to **2-up KPIs + a full-width bar** (donut and the 3rd KPI\nhidden, smaller breadcrumb), and the spotlight frame''s mobile min-height\nis bumped so the bar has room; at md+ the full 3-KPI + side-by-side\nlayout returns. The donut caps at its size and shrinks with its\ncontainer.\n\n## Notes\n- Follows the `product-feature` conventions (per-visual folder,\none-export-per-file, split types).\n- `Tiles.tsx`: one-line spotlight mobile min-height bump (only the\ndashboard uses the spotlight tile).\n- typecheck + lint + build all green.\n\n<img width=\"1148\" height=\"638\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1eb8f120-88c2-45d1-adf9-ec00abe11006\"\n/>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPqFhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqvgQADKm9dkvc9GwgeXd/pfK8YQf\nfoaQwBQWjcGRMbDSHJJWeNQxcvaRtMNViCoZ2p6Sw0QF08voaMCS4BLgv7T+dRMW\nDwgb+ODBljRoLx1v39d14tly+ew1Tl6GN6OOiRuVklEs8KqBgechvruwPuhQN/Yx\nZ0nly70yb+C7RomxtD/XiPLuSriCfohzeZvLJGqwG1qj0jE+5elQi0B4927jp5Zo\nUs3Lb25Nvh7TuTuKqHlyfJOXbwUmPGN/S3TAEwJtzBedoDFgsJ/Q/59DyiUm7XMp\njcAhyPxkwfo+/S0+Ywx3lH09+ADnzfhF0y+ENIML9LYxoZjn4Rix99qXaFR+xy7m\nIa1cfyANrBd5+swt0qeRnMrn2ldRKk6iwOEZnCof+SoRuL7kFpleIlOgfVCs6Xrt\n03sqEMeWMuC9qMWu4Op+kSGwVLXbb+2RbwlAFB6BjNqpJQoA7k+ydbp+Xpcu5P5s\nSafkxEjPBQKJnnWVVzYjDVcUvqI/nF/rOPinVxPOCQXIVr2S5BqRH/nMyZqRDzGR\n/uiIG/bdtzFXPilGgqCkk3UYF4mHoor98oN2GXUn9OuIOE08aA67RL3oumlegD0o\nPU4WLWX15cbb6Pi0SZImBsBVWES48GA4tSCJjYg2d8Wpy3I299RF4EykeLN9KfIc\nVnPbfHwet3nStbGj4ZeK\n=xnh/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T14:47:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","s