":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/7caf2a14c5dbc34bb609bb95a96f873f67ceb2b5","node_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKDdjYWYyYTE0YzVkYmMzNGJiNjA5YmI5NWE5NmY4NzNmNjdjZWIyYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/1b4bddba6f49a6b5ac3b8fc2f6aaa3ce534c4efb","sha":"1b4bddba6f49a6b5ac3b8fc2f6aaa3ce534c4efb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/1b4bddba6f49a6b5ac3b8fc2f6aaa3ce534c4efb"}],"sha":"7caf2a14c5dbc34bb609bb95a96f873f67ceb2b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/7caf2a14c5dbc34bb609bb95a96f873f67ceb2b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125115953?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mabdullahabaid","id":125115953,"login":"mabdullahabaid","node_id":"U_kgDOB3UeMQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mabdullahabaid","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/1b4bddba6f49a6b5ac3b8fc2f6aaa3ce534c4efb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-26T14:43:45Z","email":"125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdullah."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T14:43:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(website): polish product hero AI transition (panel reveal timing + title wrapping) (#22223)\n\n## Summary\n\nTwo desktop/tablet polish refinements to the product page hero''s hero→AI\ntransition (`product-hero`).\n\n### 1. Delay the Ask-AI panel reveal to after the wipe (`b638d600`)\n\nThe Ask-AI side panel used to reveal *during* the dark \"wipe up\" (keyed\nto the morph `0.45 → 0.70`), so it competed with the rising black edge\nand piled onto the heaviest motion phase — rough on weaker laptops.\n\nIt''s now keyed to raw scroll progress over `[0.60, 0.70]` — the\npreviously-idle hold after the wipe settles at `0.55` — so it slides in\non its own beat once the eye has followed the black up. `morphProgress`\nis pinned at `1` across the whole post-wipe stretch, so leaving the\nmorph clock was the only way to time the panel *after* the wipe. The\nconversation playback moves with it, so the chat doesn''t stream while\nthe panel is still `width: 0`.\n\n### 2. Keep the AI heading to three lines below desktop (`8ae69a4b`)\n\nThe AI heading is the page''s longest line. Below `md`, only the mobile\ncopy renders, where the measure was frozen at `360px` while the heading\nfont scales fluidly toward `md` — so on tablet widths the title crammed\nonto four lines, recovering only at `921px` when the `672px` measure\nkicks in.\n\nAdds an `sm`-breakpoint measure step (`560px`) scoped to the AI heading;\nthe intro heading and the desktop measuring path keep their existing\n`360/672` steps.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `product-hero-scroll-model` jest suite updated and green (11/11),\nincluding a new post-morph panel-timing test.\n- Lint (`check-conventions` + `oxlint` + `oxfmt`) and typecheck green.\n- Visually confirmed: the panel reveals after the wipe settles, and the\nAI title holds three lines across tablet widths.","tree":{"sha":"a1a2fba7498fe876c9369459a903a9fe2dad15f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/a1a2fba7498fe876c9369459a903a9fe2dad15f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/1b4bddba6f49a6b5ac3b8fc2f6aaa3ce534c4efb","verification":{"payload":"tree a1a2fba7498fe876c9369459a903a9fe2dad15f6\nparent adf56cac56402aa06349fc716cbac7ee30297e48\nauthor Abdullah. <125115953+mabdullahabaid@users.noreply.github.com> 1782485025 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782485025 +0500\n\nfix(website): polish product hero AI transition (panel reveal timing + title wrapping) (#22223)\n\n## Summary\n\nTwo desktop/tablet polish refinements to the product page hero''s hero→AI\ntransition (`product-hero`).\n\n### 1. Delay the Ask-AI panel reveal to after the wipe (`b638d600`)\n\nThe Ask-AI side panel used to reveal *during* the dark \"wipe up\" (keyed\nto the morph `0.45 → 0.70`), so it competed with the rising black edge\nand piled onto the heaviest motion phase — rough on weaker laptops.\n\nIt''s now keyed to raw scroll progress over `[0.60, 0.70]` — the\npreviously-idle hold after the wipe settles at `0.55` — so it slides in\non its own beat once the eye has followed the black up. `morphProgress`\nis pinned at `1` across the whole post-wipe stretch, so leaving the\nmorph clock was the only way to time the panel *after* the wipe. The\nconversation playback moves with it, so the chat doesn''t stream while\nthe panel is still `width: 0`.\n\n### 2. Keep the AI heading to three lines below desktop (`8ae69a4b`)\n\nThe AI heading is the page''s longest line. Below `md`, only the mobile\ncopy renders, where the measure was frozen at `360px` while the heading\nfont scales fluidly toward `md` — so on tablet widths the title crammed\nonto four lines, recovering only at `921px` when the `672px` measure\nkicks in.\n\nAdds an `sm`-breakpoint measure step (`560px`) scoped to the AI heading;\nthe intro heading and the desktop measuring path keep their existing\n`360/672` steps.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `product-hero-scroll-model` jest suite updated and green (11/11),\nincluding a new post-morph panel-timing test.\n- Lint (`check-conventions` + `oxlint` + `oxfmt`) and typecheck green.\n- Visually confirmed: the panel reveals after the wipe settles, and the\nAI title holds three lines across tablet widths.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPpAhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATtgQAJKoLJo+wkgsDYiMDDKhAiuC\n7IcvB9YaQKF3YmB5oN36uKOo3X7KqA67TceikzIWlh+Cbt24/IbFi2gVkBoG98Le\nxXcaJA7qOyeFluNBmRt/I9XYvjDBUfTzZoxyYEFg4GWzAHX97OFsiOkvy5h10QqZ\nC3iBaAGAah2GqEYaOr8sbQdBtXnJxi7SwpZdow9leh4nCjddf+fQq/EIfjV4o9hQ\nEjDCQghSveHNY9Sbx0N1wFLuWJof/piRoLUZrqVoQnQuf7GQ5A156x5GzLjgPG/L\nJ0TZ8vS2QQubg9aX09tErH3oSapLym7arjPjM4JRSZkr++wEwd4j4wx3k/ZFThNF\nMFtLdFtpnkgRii/xLxvtbEkA1GWiJFpGtjPyGZESvecIHBik38jiiIxTrex99Ob4\nQ5Lvyj1lIP3SA3EmFhhpiTPDJfI0Y2eWHWgO5x3sfXm8RHXGkUYNccbntzLMGmXa\niC0KE8yN7SGHbArgOlCoTsTgSChjR0EvSMGnpuqKjFygrR50r4pSBROqP4rKe9ZK\n3LGJSMqtGTyefdDv40nDkqnMok3yrLGQRibH6p+6MBDgrG5Ikb0VOM/7rPoV4ULy\naOFVsxPbrKsbasTIFfjsKTFoC+1hr6eyuQWfL46EEfOJv/7QBNuYnBPys4sp+HnR\nkquzX3Pgx1NV9WaJ0EtC\n=HE8F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T14:47:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/1b4bddba6f49a6b5ac3b8fc2f6aaa3ce534c4efb","node_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKDFiNGJkZGJhNmY0OWE2YjVhYzNiOGZjMmY2YWFhM2NlNTM0YzRlZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/adf56cac56402aa06349fc716cbac7ee30297e48","sha":"adf56cac56402aa06349fc716cbac7ee30297e48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/adf56cac56402aa06349fc716cbac7ee30297e48"}],"sha":"1b4bddba6f49a6b5ac3b8fc2f6aaa3ce534c4efb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/1b4bddba6f49a6b5ac3b8fc2f6aaa3ce534c4efb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/adf56cac56402aa06349fc716cbac7ee30297e48/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-26T14:19:35Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T14:19:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflow): avoid ''file not found'' when duplicating unbuilt code steps (#22179)\n\n## Context\nDuplicating a workflow version (e.g. when editing an active workflow)\nclones each Code step''s logic function via copyResources, which copied\nboth the source and the built artifact unconditionally. Logic functions\ncreated from source are not built yet (no index.mjs,\nisBuildUpToDate=false), so copying the missing built file threw\nFILE_NOT_FOUND.\n\nCopy the built artifact only when it exists. This is safe because the\nduplicate inherits isBuildUpToDate=false and is rebuilt lazily on\nactivation or run.\n\nIn seed dev case for example, they are created with source but never\nbuilt\n\n## Test\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a7febba-413b-4041-985e-f84a99a5ebda","tree":{"sha":"5b1251a8488447e3d2ed59e1dc03d3a2f83c5d16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/5b1251a8488447e3d2ed59e1dc03d3a2f83c5d16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/adf56cac56402aa06349fc716cbac7ee30297e48","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b1251a8488447e3d2ed59e1dc03d3a2f83c5d16\nparent b84f7482373dfc9d60f76f967c8c470d5bc5a1b9\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1782483575 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782483575 +0200\n\nfix(workflow): avoid ''file not found'' when duplicating unbuilt code steps (#22179)\n\n## Context\nDuplicating a workflow version (e.g. when editing an active workflow)\nclones each Code step''s logic function via copyResources, which copied\nboth the source and the built artifact unconditionally. Logic functions\ncreated from source are not built yet (no index.mjs,\nisBuildUpToDate=false), so copying the missing built file threw\nFILE_NOT_FOUND.\n\nCopy the built artifact only when it exists. This is safe because the\nduplicate inherits isBuildUpToDate=false and is rebuilt lazily on\nactivation or run.\n\nIn seed dev case for example, they are created with source but never\nbuilt\n\n##