ers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/107686682013094b7875b8923a67cbcd1d421e46","node_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKDEwNzY4NjY4MjAxMzA5NGI3ODc1Yjg5MjNhNjdjYmNkMWQ0MjFlNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/35d64ac7f216d46b0d39b199e6c7a1e675f84b0d","sha":"35d64ac7f216d46b0d39b199e6c7a1e675f84b0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/35d64ac7f216d46b0d39b199e6c7a1e675f84b0d"}],"sha":"107686682013094b7875b8923a67cbcd1d421e46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/107686682013094b7875b8923a67cbcd1d421e46"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/84903907?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alibildir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alibildir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alibildir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alibildir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alibildir","id":84903907,"login":"alibildir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0OTAzOTA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alibildir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alibildir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alibildir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alibildir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alibildir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alibildir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/35d64ac7f216d46b0d39b199e6c7a1e675f84b0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T16:10:07Z","email":"84903907+alibildir@users.noreply.github.com","name":"alibildir"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T16:10:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): wrap file storage upsert and read in transaction (#21924)\n\n## Summary\nThis PR fixes a race condition occurring during file and image uploads\nin environments that use Pgpool-II or similar connection poolers with\nread-replica scaling.\n\nCurrently, in `FileStorageService.writeFile`, `fileRepository.upsert`\nwrites the file record to the primary database node. However, the\nimmediate subsequent call to `fileRepository.findOneOrFail` is executed\noutside of a transaction. Consequently, connection poolers like Pgpool\ncan route this `SELECT` query to a read-replica. Due to replication lag,\nthe replica may not yet reflect the newly inserted record, throwing an\n`EntityNotFoundError` and failing the upload process (even though the\nfile is successfully saved in S3 and the database).\n\nThis PR wraps both operations in a TypeORM database transaction when\n`queryRunner` is not provided. This ensures that the `SELECT` query\ncorrectly targets the primary node, guaranteeing immediate\nread-after-write consistency.\n\n## Affected version\n- Twenty Self-hosted (e.g. `v2.14.x`) configured with\nPgpool/read-replicas.\n\n## Changes Made\n- **`file-storage.service.ts`**: Wrapped `transactionalFileRepo.upsert`\nand `transactionalFileRepo.findOneOrFail` within\n`this.applicationRepository.manager.transaction` to ensure\nread-after-write consistency.\n\n## How to Test\n1. Set up Twenty in a self-hosted environment using Pgpool configured\nwith load balancing / read-replicas.\n2. Attempt to upload a file to a `Files` custom field or upload an image\nas an organization logo.\n3. Observe that the upload completes successfully without throwing an\n`EntityNotFoundError` in the server logs.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/21924?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ali Bildir <[alibildir@gmail.com]>\nCo-authored-by: Charles Bochet <charles@twenty.com>","tree":{"sha":"b6a1c87f907a0c150508faf36a5d94a0254d5237","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/b6a1c87f907a0c150508faf36a5d94a0254d5237"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/35d64ac7f216d46b0d39b199e6c7a1e675f84b0d","verification":{"payload":"tree b6a1c87f907a0c150508faf36a5d94a0254d5237\nparent ce9ca1184c5f93f7a201308ffc149696f19ec4ef\nauthor alibildir <84903907+alibildir@users.noreply.github.com> 1782403807 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782403807 +0200\n\nfix(server): wrap file storage upsert and read in transaction (#21924)\n\n## Summary\nThis PR fixes a race condition occurring during file and image uploads\nin environments that use Pgpool-II or similar connection poolers with\nread-replica scaling.\n\nCurrently, in `FileStorageService.writeFile`, `fileRepository.upsert`\nwrites the file record to the primary database node. However, the\nimmediate subsequent call to `fileRepository.findOneOrFail` is executed\noutside of a transaction. Consequently, connection poolers like Pgpool\ncan route this `SELECT` query to a read-replica. Due to replication lag,\nthe replica may not yet reflect the newly inserted record, throwing an\n`EntityNotFoundError` and failing the upload process (even though the\nfile is successfully saved in S3 and the database).\n\nThis PR wraps both operations in a TypeORM database transaction when\n`queryRunner` is not provided. This ensures that the `SELECT` query\ncorrectly targets the primary node, guaranteeing immediate\nread-after-write consistency.\n\n## Affected version\n- Twenty Self-hosted (e.g. `v2.14.x`) configured with\nPgpool/read-replicas.\n\n## Changes Made\n- **`file-storage.service.ts`**: Wrapped `transactionalFileRepo.upsert`\nand `transactionalFileRepo.findOneOrFail` within\n`this.applicationRepository.manager.transaction` to ensure\nread-after-write consistency.\n\n## How to Test\n1. Set up Twenty in a self-hosted environment using Pgpool configured\nwith load balancing / read-replicas.\n2. Attempt to upload a file to a `Files` custom field or upload an image\nas an organization logo.\n3. Observe that the upload completes successfully without throwing an\n`EntityNotFoundError` in the server logs.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/21924?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ali Bildir <[alibildir@gmail.com]>\nCo-authored-by: Charles Bochet <charles@twenty.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPVLfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwYUQADZEiYkSDHNoN1ePLXEixgr7\naU3GO94Vf9uGvuoIj9ikSxqYd5B8rgB2gpayMRZ3in15ElyHeawDwEyNhMB6mLon\ng2QlJgq/a/ccQpa+cf4jdXZpmNJrPUXHMv/sJTx5d++I0/httgIrgM13ibehzIc0\nFnQvjlFo5hvbs17T9hQY3Q9gSJ1RHyUKnvllRJ+NllO6yTjgP2P+nLpAAhzBzKdT\nNDcuWLHlv2B24K3ndmWWpWAvV0BREAPXGSJfLuBNpac9HJR/k1u60D5wov/VBYr9\nTbG6vrWcXWTcgaQTLK7FjsMCreXuucEt43Ry7IIRe5ClrC854+4l3IzAe84CP01I\nU0QoozZNi4VLHSn9Ktn/i+6Wy/F3GM+DY0xgfuQ03aLbWq2RZMYbtXHCkBN3TLa6\njlgEktQ3ISLKCEHokd9I+SYWm5YShwpmnYhfCpOX9XmTUTQCgyLF0wLzr+yewGw3\nQuJnFFQQ2jGWDsr2VWn5bdQrMG2U6yFObhfwCbz2D8sIl1cZm9FKog+3y+Grke/c\nUNS0S7W/vKCaJdkzmb8tvtqcLamhVFwrCPGEqSq4WkClF20teniQrDznh1Exwc/e\nniZmsH8RDAys/WCDE2xLp7yna0Hw2lU/vtmazmWPCFI+oYuA1B5eV0VZldfsoE17\nMYcW+m0nHv5T6jC53g/d\n=n4ee\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T14:47:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://git