","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/f270fb25c8ccf5630f85247e0b5839f28d9092a3","node_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKGYyNzBmYjI1YzhjY2Y1NjMwZjg1MjQ3ZTBiNTgzOWYyOGQ5MDkyYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/0b31d2a6a0ee1668ddd75f690a324ab99700f48f","sha":"0b31d2a6a0ee1668ddd75f690a324ab99700f48f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/0b31d2a6a0ee1668ddd75f690a324ab99700f48f"}],"sha":"f270fb25c8ccf5630f85247e0b5839f28d9092a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/f270fb25c8ccf5630f85247e0b5839f28d9092a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12417145?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ak800i/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ak800i/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ak800i/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ak800i/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ak800i","id":12417145,"login":"ak800i","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDE3MTQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ak800i/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ak800i/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ak800i/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ak800i/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ak800i/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ak800i","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/0b31d2a6a0ee1668ddd75f690a324ab99700f48f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T14:49:11Z","email":"12417145+ak800i@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Aleksa Jankovic"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T14:49:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(front): wrap long note/markdown text on mobile browsers (#21909)\n\nFixes #21929\n\n### Issue\n\nWhen viewing/reading a note''s body (BlockNote rich-text / markdown\ncontent) on Android, long text overflows horizontally off the viewport\nin **Chrome** and **Firefox**, while it wraps correctly on **iOS\nSafari**.\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe note body is rendered by the BlockNote editor (`StyledEditor` in\n`BlockEditor.tsx`). The block/inline content had no `overflow-wrap`, and\nthe flex-based `.bn-block-content` had no `min-width` constraint. WebKit\n(iOS Safari) breaks the content, but Blink (Android Chrome) and Gecko\n(Android Firefox) keep the intrinsic *min-content* width of the flex\nchildren, so the container expands past the viewport instead of\nwrapping.\n\n### Fix\n\nAdd wrapping/sizing rules to the editor container so text breaks and\nwraps consistently across browsers, without changing the desktop layout:\n\n- `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on `.bn-block-content` /\n`.bn-inline-content` — unlike `break-word`, this reduces the min-content\nsize so flex children can actually shrink.\n- `min-width: 0` on `.bn-block-content` and on the editor wrapper, plus\n`max-width: 100%` on the wrapper.\n\n### Test plan\n\n- Open a Note containing a very long word / URL or a long paragraph.\n- Android Chrome & Firefox: text now wraps within the viewport (no\nhorizontal overflow).\n- iOS Safari: unchanged (still wraps).\n- Desktop: layout unchanged.\n\n### Screenshots\nAndroid\n<img width=\"1080\" height=\"1949\"\nalt=\"Screenshot_20260620_231356_Chrome(1)\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bb1e38cf-198a-4ded-9dde-e0a26e637ed8\"\n/>\n\niPhone\n<img width=\"686\" height=\"1280\" alt=\"IMG_20260620_231841_096\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9cee7557-bb69-453d-bea4-a5c37de220af\"\n/>\n\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Verified on a real Android device\n\nReproduced and validated on a **Samsung Galaxy A71 (Android, Chrome /\nBlink)** using the exact note show-page DOM/CSS chain (`ScrollWrapper` →\nfull-width container → `StyledEditor` → `.bn-mantine` `container-type:\ninline-size` → flex `.bn-block-content` → ProseMirror `word-wrap:\nbreak-word`):\n\n- **Without the fix:** a long unbreakable string stays on one line and\noverflows horizontally off the viewport (`scrollWidth ≈ 1336px` in a\n~360px viewport, with a horizontal scrollbar) — matching the reported\nbug.\n- **With the fix:** the same string wraps within the viewport.\n\nNotably this does **not** reproduce on desktop Chromium — only on the\nmobile engine — which matches the original report (Android\nChrome/Firefox broken, iOS Safari fine). The flex `.bn-block-content`\n(`min-width: auto`) resolves to the unbreakable token''s intrinsic width\non Android Blink; `min-width: 0` + `overflow-wrap: anywhere` lets it\nshrink and wrap.\n\nScreenshot\n<img width=\"1080\" height=\"2400\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/827dc579-4b1e-43ea-8b28-0ca781b12d88\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"6771d6b7da901a0dae4adb822a1973750f718f2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/6771d6b7da901a0dae4adb822a1973750f718f2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/0b31d2a6a0ee1668ddd75f690a324ab99700f48f","verification":{"payload":"tree 6771d6b7da901a0dae4adb822a1973750f718f2d\nparent 9870d1e6a97daa290c58c7852b0a9ba113606d98\nauthor Aleksa Jankovic <12417145+ak800i@users.noreply.github.com> 1782398951 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782398951 +0200\n\nfix(front): wrap long note/markdown text on mobile browsers (#21909)\n\nFixes #21929\n\n### Issue\n\nWhen viewing/reading a note''s body (BlockNote rich-text / markdown\ncontent) on Android, long text overflows horizontally off the viewport\nin **Chrome** and **Firefox**, while it wraps correctly on **iOS\nSafari**.\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe note body is rendered by the BlockNote editor (`StyledEditor` in\n`BlockEditor.tsx`). The block/inline content had no `overflow-wrap`, and\nthe flex-based `.bn-block-content` had no `min-width` constraint. WebKit\n(iOS Safari) breaks the content, but Blink (Android Chrome) and Gecko\n(Android Firefox) keep the intrinsic *min-content* width of the flex\nchildren, so the container expands past the viewport instead of\nwrapping.\n\n### Fix\n\nAdd wrapping/sizing rules to the editor container so text breaks and\nwraps consistently across browsers, without changing the desktop layout:\n\n- `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on `.bn-block-content` /\n`.bn-inline-content` — unlike `break-word`, this reduces the min-content\nsize so flex children can actually shrink.\n- `min-width: 0` on `.bn-block-content` and on the editor wrapper, plus\n`max-width: 100%` on the wrapper.\n\n### Test plan\n\n- Open a Note containing a very long word / URL or a long paragraph.\n- Android Chrome & Firefox: text now wraps within the viewport (no\nhorizontal overflow).\n- iOS Safari: unchanged (still wraps).\n- Desktop: layout unchanged.\n\n### Screenshots\nAndroid\n<img width=\"1080\" height=\"1949\"\nalt=\"Screenshot_20260620_231356_Chrome(1)\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bb1e38cf-198a-4ded-9dde-e0a26e637ed8\"\n/>\n\niPhone\n<img width=\"686\" height=\"1280\" alt=\"IMG_20260620_231841_096\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9cee7557-bb69-453d-bea4-a5c37de220af\"\n/>\n\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Verified on a real Android device\n\nReproduced and validated on a **Samsung Galaxy A71 (Android, Chrome /\nBlink)** using the exact note show-page DOM/CSS chain (`ScrollWrapper` →\nfull-width container → `StyledEditor` → `.bn-mantine` `container-type:\ninline-size` → flex `.bn-block-content` → ProseMirror `word-wrap:\nbreak-word`):\n\n- **Without the fix:** a long unbreakable string stays on one line and\noverflows horizontally off the viewport (`scrollWidth ≈ 1336px` in a\n~360px viewport, with a horizontal scrollbar) — matching the reported\nbug.\n- **With the fix:** the same string wraps within the viewport.\n\nNotably this does **not** reproduce on desktop Chromium — only on the\nmobile engine — which matches the original report (Android\nChrome/Firefox broken, iOS Safari fine). The flex `.bn-block-content`\n(`min-width: auto`) resolves to the unbreakable token''s intrinsic width\non Android Blink; `min-width: 0` + `overflow-wrap: anywhere` lets it\nshrink and wrap.\n\nScreenshot\n<img width=\"1080\" height=\"2400\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/827dc579-4b1e-43ea-8b28-0ca781b12d88\"\n/>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPT/nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUNoQAHtPp8dRAkuTJQpt+X6fJcmZ\npKqrFm5ixfbNHoeVcIPngEYbIj/wyHFLA+fzgRBJ652/TUOqIG36A9sLZ1NVt9lN\n8matdc/P3OX0uwdJRgGNG3HwdDYcYMglWqZOrE+9t3HbdsfZJPBwy+GM6iAuz581\n5XvBlRbOszG2JJ9o2PRdtuADoS/9WewGY4hNDD1qwNgd4PkSlKkn4rv1LqiKr9Jj\nC3Zjn2QqWLPIUyaAy5yZJej6/XZbUCP6L0u2mmhlezgLEOfLGbtRWi2aWtktNZl/\nHwLwAH1ek1EZNsb/tMWvgnwi0mWv/jLgkgIp3B2isfAvGgJ3IESVDcXHNqhA5XxZ\nnUq7jzU8vS/u0KMbHPph1xu14MJR6MJv+dd7QtvbInms+XZuF4o6eiAp1HiPZh3H\nzKkb687k5rf8a5jdo9mD5egiO1zV6lnLeluhV6KWBcIIGgemxmdyLGE8tNHaKDv8\nzN6CthFMTXj4TD+Cn4FHIzl5jorK6PuueuxHgdBu/9ErqZzojQCIV2JGmE96E1yY\n9DsNCHtVWg0GMUe4ZsMmWuf87h6q/RMTYLYEIsZwoP4UaMh9tKBMSH+MnKLH8gRs\n793Ho/mVt4rpsrCGtD1LPjDMOBEgaCGutI7gTRGSBNLV7TD3zikKtUN9dp7QPmSw\n0UPyaNUS64rU7t3JAK/B\n=k1Kg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T14:47:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/0b31d2a6a0ee1668ddd75f690a324ab99700f48f","node_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKDBiMzFkMmE2YTBlZTE2NjhkZGQ3NWY2OTBhMzI0YWI5OTcwMGY0OGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/9870d1e6a97daa290c58c7852b0a9ba113606d98","sha":"9870d1e6a97daa290c58c7852b0a9ba113606d98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/9870d1e6a97daa290c58c7852b0a9ba113606d98"}],"sha":"0b31d2a6a0ee1668ddd75f690a324ab99700f48f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/0b31d2a6a0ee1668ddd75f690a324ab99700f48f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19412894?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Bonapara","id":19412894,"login":"Bonapara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDEyODk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/9870d1e6a97daa290c58c7852b0a9ba113606d98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T14:22:17Z","email":"tdesfrancs@gmail.com","name":"Thomas des Francs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T14:22:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix source icon SVG ID collisions (#22177)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes the Gmail and Google Calendar source icons by replacing\ndocument-global generic SVG IDs (`a`, `b`, `c`, etc.) with icon-specific\nIDs. This prevents inline SVG gradients, masks, and filters from\nresolving against another icon instance when the icons render together\nin the record table actor/source column.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe Gmail and Google Calendar SVG assets both used generic IDs. Browser\nSVG fragment references are document-global for inline SVG, so whichever\nicon appears first can hijack the other icon''s `url(#...)` references.\nThat made the Calendar icon pick up Gmail gradients, and could also\naffect Gmail depending on DOM order.\n\n## Before\n\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" alt=\"Before icon collision screenshot\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82ce20a8-47c7-4b70-8af2-e134cf88c0b8\"\n/>\n\n## After\n\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" alt=\"After icon collision screenshot\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/240120a6-b84e-4682-a116-0ccb48192543\"\n/>\n\n## Validation\n\n- Rendered Gmail + Calendar in both DOM orders via a local browser\nfixture.\n- Verified the before fixture had 14 generic SVG IDs and the after\nfixture had 0.\n- Verified 4 SVGs rendered, no cross-icon URL reference problems, and no\nbrowser console warnings/errors.\n- Ran `xmllint --noout packages/twenty-ui/src/assets/icons/gmail.svg\npackages/twenty-ui/src/assets/icons/google-calendar.svg`.\n- Ran `rg -n\n\"id=\\\"[a-z]\\\"|url\\(#[a-z]\\)|mask=\\\"url\\(#[a-z]\\)\\\"|filter=\\\"url\\(#[a-z]\\)\\\"\"\npackages/twenty-ui/src/assets/icons -S` and confirmed no matches.\n\n`yarn nx build twenty-ui` could not run in this worktree because\n`node_modules` is missing, and Yarn reports: `Couldn''t find the\nnode_modules state file`.","tree":{"sha":"6699482e547bbac8348e2c05f1635a1f655b9313","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/6699482e547bbac8348e2c05f1635a1f655b9313"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/9870d1e6a97daa290c58c7852b0a9ba113606d98","verification":{"payload":"tree 6699482e547bbac8348e2c05f1635a1f655b9313\nparent f86bf637d1097a75d339222c82f67c86cded65e7\nauthor Thomas des Francs <tdesfrancs@gmail.com> 1782397337 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782397337 +0000\n\nFix source icon SVG ID collisions (#22177)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes the Gmail and Google Calendar source icons by replacing\ndocument-global generic SVG IDs (`a`, `b`, `c`, etc.) with icon-specific\nIDs. This prevents inline SVG gradients, masks, and filters from\nresolving against another icon instance when the icons render together\nin the record table actor/source column.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe Gmail and Google Calendar SVG assets both used generic IDs. Browser\nSVG fragment references are document-global for inline SVG, so whichever\nicon appears first can hijack the other icon''s `url(#...)` references.\nThat made the Calendar icon pick up Gmail gradients, and could also\naffect Gmail depending on DOM order.\n\n## Before\n\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" alt=\"Before icon collision screenshot\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82ce20a8-47c7-4b70-8af2-e134cf88c0b8\"\n/>\n\n## After\n\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" alt=\"After icon collision screenshot\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/240120a6-b84e-4682-a116-0ccb48192543\"\n/>\n\n## Validation\n\n- Rendered Gmail + Calendar in both DOM orders via a local browser\nfixture.\n- Verified the before fixture had 14 generic SVG IDs and the after\nfixture had 0.\n- Verified 4 SVGs rendered, no cross-icon URL reference problems, and no\nbrowser console warnings/errors.\n- Ran `xmllint --noout packages/twenty-ui/src/assets/icons/gmail.svg\npackages/twenty-ui/src/assets/icons/google-calendar.svg`.\n- Ran `rg -n\n\"id=\\\"[a-z]\\\"|url\\(#[a-z]\\)|mask=\\\"url\\(#[a-z]\\)\\\"|filter=\\\"url\\(#[a-z]\\)\\\"\"\npackages/twenty-ui/src/assets/icons -S` and confirmed no matches.\n\n`yarn nx build twenty-ui` could not run in this worktree because\n`node_modules` is missing, and Yarn reports: `Couldn''t find the\nnode_modules state file`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPTmZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvD4QAHnt4zUcfr23zyzw2XEURqwA\n8yq39FyuSe6FeOwGoFmjLWHXw/Wh6k8Q2AFX8cPh0eCFZEU8UzsNoCFItQTMEnqr\nmTiWJ6fpftyaxgUSia5EWyu85nvreCzXDYCm66DDdKT2vVaf/6ymq1rwW1U8FP12\namZqMuhA+twq8xNxgI+rXvwYmoqgLWOJs4WpjSVqMmntrXPy5Fkx0zGbtIQF9l11\njtG5U+osrmeahgtq9gAt8/L9PyqTCTvr4i8krvK6YSYVZPAOtkQtUTjLojwC7pPl\n6bEfZIcIjXAxdiDLxisepMZboolsWUXEYzfWT1Hw0jBpY4PYmfx4X6dadVe4PCSE\nXii1LiX00KqAohD05ncZaLsKrpz8uIw9xAC5kbATTuqR99190srzl4PhUIJJiexo\nK0oHr9/r4CmAqR8JtglK5PNjRZdvymsOILhwOYwW5MZy9RLNNh+8SwO1KyY1akzV\njrvICac18ytgfaJRhgdH/eh+4Jo3y6vt4cY+bu5t8Od9EEALS9L9KcI3pI2cHBVC\nHILbS4yYVCU1zuT0/oxvePbASTYQItSJ8vA1P47KOB1jY1qRHCezcNNB6KZ1KGea\nBdULm0S9LHnFm2W00cM0P8Xy+4jpGHzZjhFJff9bO+Ie4gAYXwMf6+htjSHQBImv\nnqe98gg+9bx8q2g8j8yj\n=CKOX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T14:47:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/9870d1e6a97daa290c58c7852b0a9ba113606d98","node_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKDk4NzBkMWU2YTk3ZGFhMjkwYzU4Yzc4NTJiMGE5YmExMTM2MDZkOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/f86bf637d1097a75d339222c82f67c86cded65e7","sha":"f86bf637d1097a75d339222c82f67c86cded65e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/f86bf637d1097a75d339222c82f67c86cded65e7"}],"sha":"9870d1e6a97daa290c58c7852b0a9ba113606d98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/9870d1e6a97daa290c58c7852b0a9ba113606d98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142569587?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ehconitin","id":142569587,"login":"ehconitin","node_id":"U_kgDOCH9wcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ehconitin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e