rgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/cdd1aba3e09390310d8d08c4dc1e34d268734b73","node_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKGNkZDFhYmEzZTA5MzkwMzEwZDhkMDhjNGRjMWUzNGQyNjg3MzRiNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/f416f815486b0a088c21794bbe9da2c5dde8377a","sha":"f416f815486b0a088c21794bbe9da2c5dde8377a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/f416f815486b0a088c21794bbe9da2c5dde8377a"}],"sha":"cdd1aba3e09390310d8d08c4dc1e34d268734b73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/cdd1aba3e09390310d8d08c4dc1e34d268734b73"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12035771?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesBochet","id":12035771,"login":"charlesBochet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDM1Nzcx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/f416f815486b0a088c21794bbe9da2c5dde8377a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T09:27:51Z","email":"charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Bochet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T09:27:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): retry Danger.js on transient GitHub API fetch errors (#22151)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe `danger-js` job in **CI Utils** has been failing across most PRs.\nThe failure is not a real Danger violation — it''s a transient network\nerror fetching the PR diff/commits from the GitHub API:\n\n```\nFailed to fetch GitHub pull request files: FetchError: Invalid response body while trying to fetch\nhttps://api.github.com/repos/twentyhq/twenty/pulls/XXXXX/files?page=1&per_page=100: Premature close\n    at Gunzip.<anonymous> (.../node_modules/node-fetch/lib/index.js:400:12)\n  errno: ''ERR_STREAM_PREMATURE_CLOSE'',\n  code: ''ERR_STREAM_PREMATURE_CLOSE''\n```\n\nGitHub closes the gzipped HTTP response mid-stream, and Danger''s bundled\n`node-fetch` has **no retry** on a dropped connection — so any single\nblip fails the whole check.\n\n## Why is this happening now?\n\nNothing on our side changed at the boundary where failures started. The\nNode 24.16 bump landed Jun 8 (the job stayed green for 2+ weeks after),\nDanger has been pinned at `13.0.4` for months, and there are **zero\ncommits** to `.nvmrc`, `twenty-utils/package.json`, or the\n`yarn-install` action since Jun 22.\n\nWhat changed is GitHub''s API reset rate, and it changed abruptly:\n\n| Day | Failures | Successes | Failure rate |\n|-----|----------|-----------|--------------|\n| Jun 23 | 1 | 48 | ~2% (green) |\n| Jun 24 | 38 | 204 | ~16% |\n| Jun 25 | 23 | 25 | **~48%** |\n\nThe same PR passes on one run and fails on the next (e.g. one PR shows\nup as both pass and fail; another failed 3 runs in a row) — a code bug\ncan''t flip outcomes on identical input, only an infrastructure flake\ncan. When GitHub''s connection-reset rate was ~0% we never noticed; now\nthat it''s in the tens of percent, roughly half of all PRs trip it.\n\n## Fix\n\nWrap the Danger invocation in a small retry loop (3 attempts, 5s\nbackoff) so the check absorbs these transient fetch errors instead of\nred-flagging the PR. Applied to both the `danger-js` and `congratulate`\njobs since they share the same failure mode.\n\nThis is the correct mitigation rather than a code revert — there''s no\nchange on our side to revert. 3 attempts drop a ~48% single-shot failure\nrate to ~11%, and a less-degraded ~16% rate to well under 1%. If\nGitHub''s reliability recovers, the retries simply stop firing and cost\nnothing.\n\nThis is a CI-only change — no application code is touched.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22151?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"6ce7d74654189e5e562df5e40b07c38108b769c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/6ce7d74654189e5e562df5e40b07c38108b769c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/f416f815486b0a088c21794bbe9da2c5dde8377a","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ce7d74654189e5e562df5e40b07c38108b769c5\nparent 6a36fc3ba8d0c9616cb30e3526f2c7dafc8f6525\nauthor Charles Bochet <charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com> 1782379671 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782379671 +0200\n\nfix(ci): retry Danger.js on transient GitHub API fetch errors (#22151)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe `danger-js` job in **CI Utils** has been failing across most PRs.\nThe failure is not a real Danger violation — it''s a transient network\nerror fetching the PR diff/commits from the GitHub API:\n\n```\nFailed to fetch GitHub pull request files: FetchError: Invalid response body while trying to fetch\nhttps://api.github.com/repos/twentyhq/twenty/pulls/XXXXX/files?page=1&per_page=100: Premature close\n    at Gunzip.<anonymous> (.../node_modules/node-fetch/lib/index.js:400:12)\n  errno: ''ERR_STREAM_PREMATURE_CLOSE'',\n  code: ''ERR_STREAM_PREMATURE_CLOSE''\n```\n\nGitHub closes the gzipped HTTP response mid-stream, and Danger''s bundled\n`node-fetch` has **no retry** on a dropped connection — so any single\nblip fails the whole check.\n\n## Why is this happening now?\n\nNothing on our side changed at the boundary where failures started. The\nNode 24.16 bump landed Jun 8 (the job stayed green for 2+ weeks after),\nDanger has been pinned at `13.0.4` for months, and there are **zero\ncommits** to `.nvmrc`, `twenty-utils/package.json`, or the\n`yarn-install` action since Jun 22.\n\nWhat changed is GitHub''s API reset rate, and it changed abruptly:\n\n| Day | Failures | Successes | Failure rate |\n|-----|----------|-----------|--------------|\n| Jun 23 | 1 | 48 | ~2% (green) |\n| Jun 24 | 38 | 204 | ~16% |\n| Jun 25 | 23 | 25 | **~48%** |\n\nThe same PR passes on one run and fails on the next (e.g. one PR shows\nup as both pass and fail; another failed 3 runs in a row) — a code bug\ncan''t flip outcomes on identical input, only an infrastructure flake\ncan. When GitHub''s connection-reset rate was ~0% we never noticed; now\nthat it''s in the tens of percent, roughly half of all PRs trip it.\n\n## Fix\n\nWrap the Danger invocation in a small retry loop (3 attempts, 5s\nbackoff) so the check absorbs these transient fetch errors instead of\nred-flagging the PR. Applied to both the `danger-js` and `congratulate`\njobs since they share the same failure mode.\n\nThis is the correct mitigation rather than a code revert — there''s no\nchange on our side to revert. 3 attempts drop a ~48% single-shot failure\nrate to ~11%, and a less-degraded ~16% rate to well under 1%. If\nGitHub''s reliability recovers, the retries simply stop firing and cost\nnothing.\n\nThis is a CI-only change — no application code is touched.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22151?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPPSXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXpkQABP33fp3RXM/uK2k7yBA5KSg\n/nb91Y/tOu6nkKW7iI+fwC7ylyhud0OlgYZ/zXsh/Z/rba+kK/31epOMzvs8dn71\nvFONsTCoeJYm9LyyXBuA2FM6CoCq6x5G7bRM8whSq7YWhYUl+ATLV7sR0J6Y92X7\nMafOfEYOc2x4W6gNXs/bnMDJNwzesB63eT+RPtAGuL99iKCQNs3/Fjpxk+yqvfaN\nN3Kg0Ytm+PTS5GjaoIdsoQGfoD/THJjWosyY7LXLra9vhGvOX3/QGPx8vqJ17RIy\nrztDuXngPVaeuNQwMmK3hhJe+fW03Y8HMYz5oGOUBKfZXLKepE9y9cpasGMkAEnr\niY7RJ0regwwqsDE6al2AYYVfLoM2rXQzfkwvpsWMuf/gT3GvWEjgySQr1gXpQQkj\nZcD4XKL+VUf6Ladb2jsYs2NmrUv4IeUu1bs4NZRyUcL7Lm23Z7F0w4KpFQJ8DbG1\nHet0KMtUgpzYP1ywLF+LwWFFGcFA44Q/U/JBoPHvKjPBM9Rgh4Y4KLAcOsWQ1fCz\nPmyw9pIpwV8hFhxMQ9lDs2/Hm1fBUA36k5GccsRRIhimhEc05FBR5quPWhWEUDXZ\n7L8LJKKSYrEn3fMoVBKd7rgxQj8VZroYUI+i+XMbRu1gOQNnKDYbmWbpNTBwf3Et\nD83XuHV/o0BrjFGx+0xV\n=/AH4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T14:47:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/f416f815486b0a088c21794bbe9da2c5dde8377a","node_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKGY0MTZmODE1NDg2YjBhMDg4YzIxNzk0YmJlOWRhMmM1ZGRlODM3N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/6a36fc3ba8d0c9616cb30e3526f2c7dafc8f6525","sha":"6a36fc3ba8d0c9616cb30e3526f2c7dafc8f6525","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/6a36fc3ba8d0c9616cb30e3526f2c7dafc8f6525"}],"sha":"f416f815486b0a088c21794bbe9da2c5dde8377a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/f416f815486b0a088c21794bbe9da2c5dde8377a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29927851?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/martmull","id":29927851,"login":"martmull","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI3ODUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/6a36fc3ba8d0c9616cb30e3526f2c7dafc8f6525/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T09:21:51Z","email":"martmull@hotmail.fr","name":"martmull"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T09:21:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(sdk): evict compiled manifest modules from require cache in dev mode (#22129)\n\n## Problem\n\n`yarn twenty dev` crashes after running for a while with:\n\n```\nFATAL ERROR: Reached heap limit Allocation failed - JavaScript heap out of memory\n```\n\nThe crash happens during the **Manifest Build** phase, after the process\nhas been up for a long time (~35 min in the reported case) — the\nsignature of a slow memory leak in the long-running watch process, not a\nsingle oversized operation.\n\nFixes the issue described in `core-team-issues#2560`.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`manifest-extract-config-from-file.ts``loadModule()` compiles each\nentity file with esbuild (`bundle: true`, so the whole dependency graph\nis inlined), writes it to a unique `mkdtemp` directory, and loads it\nwith `appRequire(tempFile)`.\n\n`createRequire` shares Node''s global module cache (`Module._cache`), so\n**every loaded temp module is retained in the require cache forever**.\nTwo things made this unbounded:\n\n1. `mkdtemp` generates a fresh random directory each call, so cache keys\nnever collide — entries purely accumulate.\n2. The `finally` block removed the temp dir **from disk** but never\nevicted the `require.cache` entry, so the evaluated, fully-bundled\nmodule object stayed pinned in the JS heap.\n\nIn dev mode the orchestrator re-runs `buildManifest` on **every** file\nchange and watcher rebuild (`scheduleSync()`), and each rebuild compiles\n& `require()`s ~one module per entity file (53 in the reported case).\nOver a session of editing, thousands of large bundled module objects\npile up in `require.cache` until V8''s heap is exhausted → FATAL OOM.\n\n## Fix\n\nDelete the temp module from the require cache after loading it, so\nmemory stays bounded to a single rebuild. Because `bundle: true` inlines\nthe whole graph, the temp module is the only cache entry per load, so\ndeleting it lets the bundled object be GC''d.\n\n```ts\n} finally {\n  delete appRequire.cache[tempFile];\n  await remove(tempDir);\n}\n```\n\n## Test\n\nAdds a regression test (`manifest-extract-config-from-file.spec.ts`)\nthat runs `extractManifestFromFile` repeatedly and asserts no\n`twenty-manifest` temp modules accumulate in the require cache.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0168hN9yEYvjZbqdz7PckKn8\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_0168hN9yEYvjZbqdz7PckKn8)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22129?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"56c49481b7043cebbf9f3d5d31469d48c3ab76a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/56c49481b7043cebbf9f3d5d31469d48c3ab76a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/6a36fc3ba8d0c9616cb30e3526f2c7dafc8f6525","verification":{"payload":"tree 56c49481b7043cebbf9f3d5d31469d48c3ab76a5\nparent db687c7407bcd2b4863865fa9d4a24f5b7fa5e97\nauthor martmull <martmull@hotmail.fr> 1782379311 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782379311 +0200\n\nfix(sdk): evict compiled manifest modules from require cache in dev mode (#22129)\n\n## Problem\n\n`yarn twenty dev` crashes after running for a while with:\n\n```\nFATAL ERROR: Reached heap limit Allocation failed - JavaScript heap out of memory\n```\n\nThe crash happens during the **Manifest Build** phase, after the process\nhas been up for a long time (~35 min in the reported case) — the\nsignature of a slow memory leak in the long-running watch process, not a\nsingle oversized operation.\n\nFixes the issue described in `core-team-issues#2560`.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`manifest-extract-config-from-file.ts``loadModule()` compiles each\nentity file with esbuild (`bundle: true`, so the whole dependency graph\nis inlined), writes it to a unique `mkdtemp` directory, and loads it\nwith `appRequire(tempFile)`.\n\n`createRequire` shares Node''s global module cache (`Module._cache`), so\n**every loaded temp module is retained in the require cache forever**.\nTwo things made this unbounded:\n\n1. `mkdtemp` generates a fresh random directory each call, so cache keys\nnever collide — entries purely accumulate.\n2. The `finally` block removed the temp dir **from disk** but never\nevicted the `require.cache` entry, so the evaluated, fully-bundled\nmodule object stayed pinned in the JS heap.\n\nIn dev mode the orchestrator re-runs `buildManifest` on **every** file\nchange and watcher rebuild (`scheduleSync()`), and each rebuild compiles\n& `require()`s ~one module per entity file (53 in the reported case).\nOver a session of editing, thousands of large bundled module objects\npile up in `require.cache` until V8''s heap is exhausted → FATAL OOM.\n\n## Fix\n\nDelete the temp module from the require cache after loading it, so\nmemory stays bounded to a single rebuild. Because `bundle: true` inlines\nthe whole graph, the temp module is the only cache entry per load, so\ndeleting it lets the bundled object be GC''d.\n\n```ts\n} finally {\n  delete appRequire.cache[tempFile];\n  await remove(tempDir);\n}\n```\n\n## Test\n\nAdds a regression test (`manifest-extract-config-from-file.spec.ts`)\nthat runs `extractManifestFromFile` repeatedly and asserts no\n`twenty-manifest` temp modules accumulate in the require cache.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0168hN9yEYvjZbqdz7PckKn8\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_0168hN9yEYvjZbqdz7PckKn8)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22129?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPPMvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYT8QAJkxTu2MBImFtJAdl8CLkFRE\nyaa44S7vTXOYKWQcUYHshwgOlkLx+4iwV9wmblB12qJz8auZ81LMDunqvh5JNQDH\nR+4AuLqx1nOotN/mfwnJBqFUZ1+ova5TXXk0whiDetWN9KacotnketSJ5zpJ5bB3\nX1c7rPDpRzoYMC3PNshcQxpfkjPypgehpMGDwmRIlROseOxqW2C8+h3s8/1BYQqJ\nATM5PKSDC2tM27KeEpWGuxYID5X8uT9e9uH2ZCRcJOHLT4DvsaTeIvMxRoIEzfXw\n+DaVP5uHIZN/7I2yFbkZzk+n87hkg/8ExVYW/7MUASYnAY1fCUl1C/n8ALgLgxAk\nyqdfzacCBuoVZpXEsM1yfb3Fwt9E3oyChr65VH233x6Cop0Pt4FGUvFrWCTZ6WCZ\nxUa7VGi1IUEPJfNHK5fKSZ5v+/0r67wGKAAKVSobHzSbmpJGb6crPPzuy0BWdT0X\nrIvaUrUKXLWYRkZiONrgpmIbuggIKGV8jmTYia4JTPCy8TC6BYi/zm3ry5n+9aG4\n9vkRfK7m3Hv