_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKGUyMmQzMWM1NTM4OWNiNjFkZTVlNDY2MDQ3MDZmNTAyNjlmODkxZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/ad61d6d8a3d8105fb747ec7766dd1027699cd09a","sha":"ad61d6d8a3d8105fb747ec7766dd1027699cd09a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/ad61d6d8a3d8105fb747ec7766dd1027699cd09a"}],"sha":"e22d31c55389cb61de5e46604706f50269f891da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/e22d31c55389cb61de5e46604706f50269f891da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12035771?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesBochet","id":12035771,"login":"charlesBochet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDM1Nzcx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/ad61d6d8a3d8105fb747ec7766dd1027699cd09a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-24T17:14:19Z","email":"charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Bochet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-24T17:14:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): dispatch each cron trigger exactly once (#22113)\n\n## Problem\n\nApp/logic-function crons occasionally fire **twice, ~1 minute apart**.\nThe most visible symptom is a notification cron sending the same Discord\nDM (or channel post) at e.g. `17:00` and again at `17:01`.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`CronTriggerCronJob` runs every minute (`* * * * *`) and re-dispatches\nany logic function whose pattern is \"due\" according to `shouldRunNow`:\n\n```ts\nconst diff = Math.abs(prevTriggerDate.getTime() - now.getTime());\nreturn diff < rootCronIntervalMs; // 60_000\n```\n\nThe detection window (`60_000ms`) is **equal to** the 60s tick interval.\nSo when a root tick drifts across a minute boundary (runs slightly\nearly/late, or BullMQ fires a catch-up), two adjacent ticks can both see\nthe *same* trigger as \"within the last 60s\" and each enqueue a\n`LogicFunctionTriggerJob`. The dispatch isn''t idempotent, so the\nfunction runs twice.\n\n## Fix\n\nMake dispatch idempotent, keyed on the trigger itself:\n\n- New `getMatchingTriggerTimestamp(pattern, now)` returns the epoch-ms\nof the matched trigger (stable regardless of *when* within the window\nthe root job runs), or `null`. `shouldRunNow` now delegates to it —\nbehaviour unchanged.\n- Before enqueuing, `CronTriggerCronJob` claims a\n`logic-function-cron:{workspace}:{function}:{triggerTs}` key in the\n`EngineLock` cache. A second tick that resolves to the same trigger\nfinds the key and skips.\n\nDistinct triggers always have distinct timestamps (hence distinct keys),\nso a later legitimate run is never suppressed. The TTL (2 min) only\nneeds to outlive the detection window.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `WorkflowCronTriggerCronJob` uses the same `shouldRunNow` pattern and\nhas the same latent double-dispatch; left out of this PR to keep it\nfocused, but the new helper makes the same guard a small follow-up.\n- The cache `get`-then-`set` isn''t atomic; for the observed failure mode\n(ticks ~1 min apart, sequential) it''s reliable. A Redis `SET NX` would\nalso close the rare concurrent-multi-instance race.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `should-run-now.utils.spec.ts` extended: two ticks within one\nwindow resolve to the same timestamp; out-of-window and invalid patterns\nreturn `null`. All 8 pass.\n- [x] `oxlint --type-aware` + `oxfmt` clean on changed files.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22113?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"092669301891ee1ddd261dee13f790a962974b34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/092669301891ee1ddd261dee13f790a962974b34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/ad61d6d8a3d8105fb747ec7766dd1027699cd09a","verification":{"payload":"tree 092669301891ee1ddd261dee13f790a962974b34\nparent 02120aac42a65ce2db85ab5b904d7c2109dd1b06\nauthor Charles Bochet <charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com> 1782321259 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782321259 +0200\n\nfix(server): dispatch each cron trigger exactly once (#22113)\n\n## Problem\n\nApp/logic-function crons occasionally fire **twice, ~1 minute apart**.\nThe most visible symptom is a notification cron sending the same Discord\nDM (or channel post) at e.g. `17:00` and again at `17:01`.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`CronTriggerCronJob` runs every minute (`* * * * *`) and re-dispatches\nany logic function whose pattern is \"due\" according to `shouldRunNow`:\n\n```ts\nconst diff = Math.abs(prevTriggerDate.getTime() - now.getTime());\nreturn diff < rootCronIntervalMs; // 60_000\n```\n\nThe detection window (`60_000ms`) is **equal to** the 60s tick interval.\nSo when a root tick drifts across a minute boundary (runs slightly\nearly/late, or BullMQ fires a catch-up), two adjacent ticks can both see\nthe *same* trigger as \"within the last 60s\" and each enqueue a\n`LogicFunctionTriggerJob`. The dispatch isn''t idempotent, so the\nfunction runs twice.\n\n## Fix\n\nMake dispatch idempotent, keyed on the trigger itself:\n\n- New `getMatchingTriggerTimestamp(pattern, now)` returns the epoch-ms\nof the matched trigger (stable regardless of *when* within the window\nthe root job runs), or `null`. `shouldRunNow` now delegates to it —\nbehaviour unchanged.\n- Before enqueuing, `CronTriggerCronJob` claims a\n`logic-function-cron:{workspace}:{function}:{triggerTs}` key in the\n`EngineLock` cache. A second tick that resolves to the same trigger\nfinds the key and skips.\n\nDistinct triggers always have distinct timestamps (hence distinct keys),\nso a later legitimate run is never suppressed. The TTL (2 min) only\nneeds to outlive the detection window.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `WorkflowCronTriggerCronJob` uses the same `shouldRunNow` pattern and\nhas the same latent double-dispatch; left out of this PR to keep it\nfocused, but the new helper makes the same guard a small follow-up.\n- The cache `get`-then-`set` isn''t atomic; for the observed failure mode\n(ticks ~1 min apart, sequential) it''s reliable. A Redis `SET NX` would\nalso close the rare concurrent-multi-instance race.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `should-run-now.utils.spec.ts` extended: two ticks within one\nwindow resolve to the same timestamp; out-of-window and invalid patterns\nreturn `null`. All 8 pass.\n- [x] `oxlint --type-aware` + `oxfmt` clean on changed files.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22113?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPBBrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoBYQAAJ1GYF0VVaOkTm5lFnVqIDJ\nl/5sOY1/2FBvXROU+0bkvudPQeyPt11E/9nUrl84DFyUr0diTFpjRteZQGcRwY4M\nrOslv+IwaF/pLs74HfhM/evzd5FUGzn+yUZZNrq2k79SMD2ZNDZd3A7IXuDnPzrv\n8sBe/VkXCCldEl7GWjeWOX7VeDORwOCnTX+8UjsZUyb/araRBvvTMR4IljNJyCtW\neL1y7JjVQIhFIylWx/qlhE1KJhHfDlDFvTMm2xw9TwlFK/0D5LdhKQ0BE3SP/hye\np9r6uwFfQRiIl1X/eY2YBw/ZBx7pQJtf+BhHYb/AJhROkhzJ2X2YcK+zbTawrpiI\nBM9DlGgnqhohnVGXp3rZPGIysbXgmKx4uHoPFNx4WpZnJZHCFSFoJIkcqpuBuZ0W\nWA+junz3/9mJtP4fKODEd1RT84m0/4oCeO170q6dK4q5k4cNAI91iRKGJ+2WfAZh\n7WWG7/xvTJNuZ0ilNDD2dpLPL8h9eZ2wbt7YAaLMxGeoEX+EV1OEJ96KW8w3O0v1\nG7D+E+s+tZYGWY/m+bcNEiT5LRdrTBQLq/6UqSV5mlacjFjvThe0mYpqawSB/Fgi\nE21PqCcAcFIglLN962rKPO4HbIuz979HaxXybGUe4nlmuEexwMmLJsUq7fMweXlz\nXV7fLjXr20n2EegLXxOL\n=Nff7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T14:47:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/ad61d6d8a3d8105fb747ec7766dd1027699cd09a","node_id":"C_kwDOTG3Rw9oAKGFkNjFkNmQ4YTNkODEwNWZiNzQ3ZWM3NzY2ZGQxMDI3Njk5Y2QwOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commit/02120aac42a65ce2db85ab5b904d7c2109dd1b06","sha":"02120aac42a65ce2db85ab5b904d7c2109dd1b06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/02120aac42a65ce2db85ab5b904d7c2109dd1b06"}],"sha":"ad61d6d8a3d8105fb747ec7766dd1027699cd09a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/ad61d6d8a3d8105fb747ec7766dd1027699cd09a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/commits/02120aac42a65ce2db85ab5b904d7c2109dd1b06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-24T17:13:20Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-24T17:13:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add v2 create-workspace onboarding screen (#22075)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/30d69db2-ef50-48b5-8233-d9a36511b5e8\n\nBuilds the second step of the new onboarding flow on top of #22027: the\nv2 \"Create your workspace\" screen, shown inside `/welcome-v2` at the\n`WorkspaceCreation` step.\n\nWhat changed:\n- New `SignInUpV2Header` (back chevron + Twenty logo) and\n`SignInUpWorkspaceCreationFormV2` (left-aligned title/subtitle, logo\nupload, Name + Subdomain fields, \"Create workspace\"), wired into\n`SignInUpV2` for the workspace-creation step.\n- When a subdomain is taken, a box now lists 3 server-verified-available\nalternatives. Backend `SubdomainAvailabilityDTO` returns\n`suggestedSubdomains` via a new `findAvailableSubdomains` helper.\n- The shared `useWorkspaceSubdomainField` hook is extended additively\n(new `suggestions` + `applySuggestionValue`) so the v1 `/welcome` screen\nis untouched.\n\nReviewer notes:\n- `generated-metadata/graphql.ts` was hand-patched (metadata codegen\nneeds a running server).\n- Storybook: `Pages/Auth/SignInUpV2 → WorkspaceCreation`.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22075?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"41fa725f8382284d37a23ec41acf5add8e85161d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/trees/41fa725f8382284d37a23ec41acf5add8e85161d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vaishnav1906/IDDA-CRM/git/commits/02120aac42a65ce2db85ab5b904d7c2109dd1b06","verification":{"payload":"tree 41fa725f8382284d37a23ec41acf5add8e85161d\nparent fdea2d6e1e27a5f349d08df4f49d3062f94ece57\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1782321200 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782321200 +0000\n\nAdd v2 create-workspace onboarding screen (#22075)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/30d69db2-ef50-48b5-8233-d9a36511b5e8\n\nBuilds the second step of the new onboarding flow on top of #22027: the\nv2 \"Create your workspace\" screen, shown inside `/welcome-v2` at the\n`WorkspaceCreation` step.\n\nWhat changed:\n- New `SignInUpV2Header` (back chevron + Twenty logo) and\n`SignInUpWorkspaceCreationFormV2` (left-aligned title/subtitle, logo\nupload, Name + Subdomain fields, \"Create workspace\"), wired into\n`SignInUpV2` for the workspace-creation step.\n- When a subdomain is taken, a box now lists 3 server-verified-available\nalternatives. Backend `SubdomainAvailabilityDTO` returns\n`suggestedSubdomains` via a new `findAvailableSubdomains` helper.\n- The shared `useWorkspaceSubdomainField` hook is extended additively\n(new `suggestions` + `applySuggestionValue`) so the v1 `/welcome` screen\nis untouched.\n\nReviewer notes:\n- `generated-metadata/graphql.ts` was hand-patched (metadata codegen\nneeds a running server).\n- Storybook: `Pages/Auth/SignInUpV2 → WorkspaceCreation`.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22075?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in