low/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/008e3ed7504698f2f93669c4bbabe4be159e7b23","node_id":"C_kwDOTG-nuNoAKDAwOGUzZWQ3NTA0Njk4ZjJmOTM2NjljNGJiYWJlNGJlMTU5ZTdiMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/f6185bef9bdfa5ef7a15089fd6cdebb0258fb9e3","sha":"f6185bef9bdfa5ef7a15089fd6cdebb0258fb9e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/f6185bef9bdfa5ef7a15089fd6cdebb0258fb9e3"}],"sha":"008e3ed7504698f2f93669c4bbabe4be159e7b23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/008e3ed7504698f2f93669c4bbabe4be159e7b23"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/f6185bef9bdfa5ef7a15089fd6cdebb0258fb9e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:10:10Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:10:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: describe the pipeline main actually runs, not the v0.0.1 snapshot (#130)\n\nThe README still documented the 10-agent pipeline that shipped at tag\np2k-v0.0.1. Since then main added four agents that a reader had no way to know\nabout: agent_5_5_executable_readiness, agent_5_6_readiness_remediator,\nagent_5_7_grounding_verifier, and agent_6_dag_generator. All four run in the\ndefault flow, and one of them (5.7) is the stage that makes the provenance\nclaim in the opening paragraph true.\n\nUpdates the count to 15 (eleven extraction, four comparison), adds the four\nstages to the pipeline diagram and the agent table, retargets the overview\ndiagram at steps 1-7, and adds a note covering the details the numbering hides:\nthe extract/compare numbering collision at 7, the two module names that lag\ntheir step number, 3.5 overlapping step 4, and step 5 launching four agents\nwith 5.6 conditional on 5.5 exiting 3.\n\nThe release line keeps its 10-agent description, which is correct for the tag,\nand now says so.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"85ba4a2ea638d3c457482d1926075ec4805c4174","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/85ba4a2ea638d3c457482d1926075ec4805c4174"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/f6185bef9bdfa5ef7a15089fd6cdebb0258fb9e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 85ba4a2ea638d3c457482d1926075ec4805c4174\nparent 2d87e8bfb3886b3bd2ba0d4cfc0299947a816c3b\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1788491410 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788491410 -0700\n\ndocs: describe the pipeline main actually runs, not the v0.0.1 snapshot (#130)\n\nThe README still documented the 10-agent pipeline that shipped at tag\np2k-v0.0.1. Since then main added four agents that a reader had no way to know\nabout: agent_5_5_executable_readiness, agent_5_6_readiness_remediator,\nagent_5_7_grounding_verifier, and agent_6_dag_generator. All four run in the\ndefault flow, and one of them (5.7) is the stage that makes the provenance\nclaim in the opening paragraph true.\n\nUpdates the count to 15 (eleven extraction, four comparison), adds the four\nstages to the pipeline diagram and the agent table, retargets the overview\ndiagram at steps 1-7, and adds a note covering the details the numbering hides:\nthe extract/compare numbering collision at 7, the two module names that lag\ntheir step number, 3.5 overlapping step 4, and step 5 launching four agents\nwith 5.6 conditional on 5.5 exiting 3.\n\nThe release line keeps its 10-agent description, which is correct for the tag,\nand now says so.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmjaSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuswQAFWXZbvtLcknMIYJIeSwRxjT\nIrvE/6Rtz5OVJ827njW2AoW3ukOJv6QxcSraJl1zk6KtQQFtS7B34ygoZsdlnaXQ\nllSHRRsmnGPkUWyMMsgGLP4KchjX1QRuIWy7UtBtoS3yAXI3kxgSsuxJeWqXOakZ\n5DaaBviV6IiJ8QM32g/GeEih+AEDGXe1Su/nGLppZoa50hHt9W4Oy45OO8R0Vhf5\n/cFMjlsUXWl+49Nv4CUm3lYP1PSgW/0YLIMzGZGf0XP09rJFHsm27wFLoM4qXLYd\nrIouGoJiKW3qiCfQ2l46TW/qYRAJkgec962QAye/BtECcge9maLxpxZvbEsbX11P\n3S/9q/luFE7WDmrpgJSSrkL1YrwWrwCMX1dTqp/nlCW4Xydv4lo3KBP/Q8db+h8d\nwJpYVYmqo3NcEhCdfbxyl5cTG1m7ie8rKasQJhMKvKXKKvlnrKQhjvWEvIbPmv02\nBWy48I3T+FvJvr+SjDZcdobzRXzEKYvvltJuqYVyVSYSHMDgNMt8E9Q3AxTDDd3Y\nHeG3Qa4ucVBbXhhS2z85C7sA3U2YULi8+yqzfXfSBEzanGpe5bDd2qPmf8kzaGkn\nqjyob/Djl4DmYEw9H0ZBgLBWvP4ktn7Q/x7LTwFRIC9n+b0+Zvx4LT+Srk7ap8g5\nq6xgdkiuLEmEOq364rxX\n=rWQR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T03:10:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/f6185bef9bdfa5ef7a15089fd6cdebb0258fb9e3","node_id":"C_kwDOTG-nuNoAKGY2MTg1YmVmOWJkZmE1ZWY3YTE1MDg5ZmQ2Y2RlYmIwMjU4ZmI5ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/2d87e8bfb3886b3bd2ba0d4cfc0299947a816c3b","sha":"2d87e8bfb3886b3bd2ba0d4cfc0299947a816c3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/2d87e8bfb3886b3bd2ba0d4cfc0299947a816c3b"}],"sha":"f6185bef9bdfa5ef7a15089fd6cdebb0258fb9e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/f6185bef9bdfa5ef7a15089fd6cdebb0258fb9e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/2d87e8bfb3886b3bd2ba0d4cfc0299947a816c3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:54:31Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:54:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(pipeline): port 6 bug fixes discovered by the compliance-to-code fork (#128)\n\n`compliance-to-code` (rrahimi-uci/compliance-to-code) is a research fork of\nthis repo''s extraction pipeline (Agents 1-5.7 + 6, re-scoped to the 4\nbenchmark-backed domains). A byte-for-byte diff of every kept file against\nthis repo found six pre-existing defects that the fork fixed independently\nbut were never ported back here. This commit ports all six, verbatim from\nthe fork, plus its two regression tests.\n\n1. agent_1_document_organizer.py\n   - process_knowledge_folder ran fully serial with a 1s sleep between\n     files (hours for 100+ documents) despite the LLM client already\n     supporting KG_LLM_CONCURRENCY-many in-flight requests. Now dispatches\n     each document (isolated output subfolder, no shared mutable state)\n     through a ThreadPoolExecutor sized by KG_ORGANIZER_WORKERS /\n     KG_LLM_CONCURRENCY (default 8).\n   - A present-but-blank section title (`\"\"`/whitespace) passed through\n     `.get(key, default)` unfixed, propagating an empty section_id into\n     source_reference and failing v2''s missing_evidence_reference_field\n     check. Now `.strip() or fallback`.\n   - Re-chunking a document no longer leaves orphaned files from a prior,\n     differently-chunked run in its output folder (cleared before rewrite).\n\n2. agent_2_entity_extractor.py\n   - analyze_extraction_quality returned wrong-named keys\n     (quality_score/completeness/suggestions); every caller reading\n     overall_score/entity_quality_score/relationship_quality_score/\n     business_rules_score/coverage_score silently got 0, always printed\n     \"0/100\" regardless of real results, and permanently disabled the\n     quality-target early-stop path. Fixed to return the keys actually read.\n\n3. agent_3_rules_extractor.py\n   - max_workers read MAX_WORKERS directly with a hardcoded fallback of 20,\n     duplicating (and silently diverging from) config.get_max_workers()''s\n     documented default of 40. Now calls config.get_max_workers().\n\n4. agent_5_5_executable_readiness.py\n   - BPMN eligibility was gated on a hardcoded, mortgage-shaped rule_type\n     set (process/validation/compliance/exception); every domain whose\n     extraction prompt uses a different rule_type vocabulary got zero BPMN\n     targets. Regated on a domain-agnostic signal: outputs + a named\n     responsible_party.\n   - contract_issues/requires_review were stamped once at extraction time\n     and never recomputed after normalization aliases a legacy\n     operator/value-type into canonical form, leaving stale\n     invalid-operator flags on structurally clean rules (~97% of rules on\n     one real run). Now re-validated via annotate_rule_contract after\n     normalization.\n   - variables[].type never got the LEGACY_VALUE_TYPES alias table applied\n     (only value_type fields did); \"enum_array\" and the operator\n     \"contains_any\" were missing from the alias tables entirely.\n   - The per-entity conflict-analysis output-variable buckets were\n     dispatched one LLM call at a time in a plain loop; now run through a\n     ThreadPoolExecutor, restoring the concurrency the outer per-entity\n     pool already had room for.\n\n5. agent_5_knowledge_graph_optimizer.py\n   - max_workers'' fallback was hardcoded to 1, fully serializing the dedup\n     batch loop and cross-batch dependency pass whenever --workers wasn''t\n     passed, despite the CLI help text and this class''s own docstring\n     describing a default of 40. Now calls config.get_max_workers().\n   - Deduplicating rules collected source_reference from every merged\n     duplicate but dropped their field_evidence (per-field citations)\n     entirely — real case on a full OPP-115 run: two sections'' only\n     citations vanished when their citing rule was merged as a duplicate,\n     failing corpus_manifest''s unexplained-removal check. Now collected and\n     merged into the surviving primary rule alongside source_reference.\n\n6. scripts/generate_benchmark_domain_prompts.py (+ the 4 domain packs it\n   generates: commercial_contracts, mobile_app_privacy, nda_confidentiality,\n   privacy_policy)\n   - The extraction prompt asked the model to emit both v1 prose\n     (conditions/consequences) and the v2 structured contract in the same\n     request — a self-contradictory instruction. Now asks only for the v2\n     contract fields, which fully supersede the v1 shape.\n\nAlso ported: two regression tests from the fork\n(test_agent_1_concurrent_organization.py,\ntest_agent_5_dedup_field_evidence.py) covering fixes #1 and #5, and the\nfork''s additions/updates to test_executable_readiness.py covering fix #4\n(including the required assertion update: the domain-agnostic BPMN gate\nmeans the existing fixture — an output variable + a responsible_party —\nnow correctly targets [\"DMN\", \"BPMN\"] instead of [\"DMN\"] alone).\n\nNot ported (out of scope for this port): the fork''s own scope-cut test\nremovals (Agent 7-10 / UI-backend / run-store tests it dropped because its\nown repo doesn''t carry those components — this repo still does and keeps\nits existing coverage for them), and its C2C_CONFIG_PATH env-var rename\n(cosmetic to that fork; this repo keeps P2K_CONFIG_PATH).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"336fde29f9183ce2410689049067b669eea6794c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/336fde29f9183ce2410689049067b669eea6794c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/2d87e8bfb3886b3bd2ba0d4cfc0299947a816c3b","verification":{"payload":"tree 336fde29f9183ce2410689049067b669eea6794c\nparent 4efc9a7a6ef9e9722e0d63bf37c43c08d40dd5c4\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1787975671 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787975671 -0700\n\nfix(pipeline): port 6 bug fixes discovered by the compliance-to-code fork (#128)\n\n`compliance-to-code` (rrahimi-uci/compliance-to-code) is a research fork of\nthis repo''s extraction pipeline (Agents 1-5.7 + 6, re-scoped to the 4\nbenchmark-backed domains). A byte-for-byte diff of every kept file against\nthis repo found six pre-existing defects that the fork fixed independently\nbut were never ported back here. This commit ports all six, verbatim from\nthe fork, plus its two regression tests.\n\n1. agent_1_document_organizer.py\n   - process_knowledge_folder ran fully serial with a 1s sleep between\n     files (hours for 100+ documents) despite the LLM client already\n     supporting KG_LLM_CONCURRENCY-many in-flight requests. Now dispatches\n     each document (isolated output subfolder, no shared mutable state)\n     through a ThreadPoolExecutor sized by KG_ORGANIZER_WORKERS /\n     KG_LLM_CONCURRENCY (default 8).\n   - A present-but-blank section title (`\"\"`/whitespace) passed through\n     `.get(key, default)` unfixed, propagating an empty section_id into\n     source_reference and failing v2''s missing_evidence_reference_field\n     check. Now `.strip() or