9eba8c217bb6fbba72c4b9fb6dd43e74b14c465f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/9eba8c217bb6fbba72c4b9fb6dd43e74b14c465f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/9594703b81012a62ae8588f8db167d7ce7141146/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:00:19Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:00:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(pipeline): resolve two bugs surfaced by a ContractNLI pilot run (#123)\n\nRan the pipeline against a 5-document ContractNLI (NDA) pilot with the\nnda_confidentiality domain pack to validate the pipeline works correctly\noutside the mortgage domain it was mostly hardened against this session.\nFound and fixed two real bugs, both reproduced against the pilot''s actual\nextraction output before being fixed:\n\n1. source_reference shape: documented everywhere (rule_contract_v2.txt,\n   every domain prompt) as a single citation object, but Agent 3 sometimes\n   emits a list of citations for a rule whose justification spans more than\n   one excerpt. Agent 5.7''s own _iter_references already tolerates this\n   shape, but Agent 5.5''s _evidence_pointer/_evidence_packet only accepted a\n   single Mapping — so a rule with no exceptions and a list-shaped\n   source_reference ended up with an empty field_evidence.exceptions, a hard\n   v2 schema violation that failed the whole pipeline outright rather than\n   just flagging the one rule. Both call sites now take the first usable\n   entry from a list, same as Agent 5.7 already does.\n\n2. schema_consistency/Agent 5.6 control flow: the invariant''s pass condition\n   folded in both genuine v2 structural violations and final-readiness\n   \"needs more evidence\" gaps (final_contract_error_count) into one count.\n   agent_5_5''s main() checks overall invariant_pass before checking whether\n   any rule needs review, so any final-readiness gap at all — precisely the\n   condition Agent 5.6 (focused remediation) exists to fix — triggered a\n   hard SystemExit(2) that always pre-empted the softer SystemExit(3) path\n   that auto-launches Agent 5.6. README.md documents \"the full pipeline\n   launches 5.6 automatically when Agent 5.5 requests remediation,\" but that\n   path was unreachable in practice on every real run so far this session\n   (49-56 such violations on one mortgage run, 7 on this pilot) — it always\n   hit the hard-stop first. schema_consistency''s pass is now gated on\n   contract_error_count (genuine structural violations) alone; both counts\n   stay in the evidence string for visibility.\n\nVerified end to end: after both fixes, the same 5-document pilot correctly\nprogresses through Steps 1-5.5, Agent 5.6 auto-launches for the first time\nobserved this session, converges after 2 passes (12 -> 18 of 32 rules\nready), and the pipeline correctly fails closed with 14 rules still\ngenuinely under review rather than either crashing on a false schema\nviolation or silently certifying an incomplete graph.\n\nTests: apps/pipeline/tests/test_executable_readiness.py — 5 new cases\ncovering _evidence_pointer/_evidence_packet with list-shaped\nsource_reference, and a reproduction of the schema_consistency/Agent-5.6\ncontrol-flow bug. Full suite: 1681 passed, 0 failed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8bc189b5c1983e4140de85a5561277abb8c61fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/c8bc189b5c1983e4140de85a5561277abb8c61fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/9594703b81012a62ae8588f8db167d7ce7141146","verification":{"payload":"tree c8bc189b5c1983e4140de85a5561277abb8c61fe\nparent ee492a2635d395d036dd51628d2fba4e5298ab77\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1787425219 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787425219 -0700\n\nfix(pipeline): resolve two bugs surfaced by a ContractNLI pilot run (#123)\n\nRan the pipeline against a 5-document ContractNLI (NDA) pilot with the\nnda_confidentiality domain pack to validate the pipeline works correctly\noutside the mortgage domain it was mostly hardened against this session.\nFound and fixed two real bugs, both reproduced against the pilot''s actual\nextraction output before being fixed:\n\n1. source_reference shape: documented everywhere (rule_contract_v2.txt,\n   every domain prompt) as a single citation object, but Agent 3 sometimes\n   emits a list of citations for a rule whose justification spans more than\n   one excerpt. Agent 5.7''s own _iter_references already tolerates this\n   shape, but Agent 5.5''s _evidence_pointer/_evidence_packet only accepted a\n   single Mapping — so a rule with no exceptions and a list-shaped\n   source_reference ended up with an empty field_evidence.exceptions, a hard\n   v2 schema violation that failed the whole pipeline outright rather than\n   just flagging the one rule. Both call sites now take the first usable\n   entry from a list, same as Agent 5.7 already does.\n\n2. schema_consistency/Agent 5.6 control flow: the invariant''s pass condition\n   folded in both genuine v2 structural violations and final-readiness\n   \"needs more evidence\" gaps (final_contract_error_count) into one count.\n   agent_5_5''s main() checks overall invariant_pass before checking whether\n   any rule needs review, so any final-readiness gap at all — precisely the\n   condition Agent 5.6 (focused remediation) exists to fix — triggered a\n   hard SystemExit(2) that always pre-empted the softer SystemExit(3) path\n   that auto-launches Agent 5.6. README.md documents \"the full pipeline\n   launches 5.6 automatically when Agent 5.5 requests remediation,\" but that\n   path was unreachable in practice on every real run so far this session\n   (49-56 such violations on one mortgage run, 7 on this pilot) — it always\n   hit the hard-stop first. schema_consistency''s pass is now gated on\n   contract_error_count (genuine structural violations) alone; both counts\n   stay in the evidence string for visibility.\n\nVerified end to end: after both fixes, the same 5-document pilot correctly\nprogresses through Steps 1-5.5, Agent 5.6 auto-launches for the first time\nobserved this session, converges after 2 passes (12 -> 18 of 32 rules\nready), and the pipeline correctly fails closed with 14 rules still\ngenuinely under review rather than either crashing on a false schema\nviolation or silently certifying an incomplete graph.\n\nTests: apps/pipeline/tests/test_executable_readiness.py — 5 new cases\ncovering _evidence_pointer/_evidence_packet with list-shaped\nsource_reference, and a reproduction of the schema_consistency/Agent-5.6\ncontrol-flow bug. Full suite: 1681 passed, 0 failed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqifHDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoIUQAH9TGL/5jMaIdvPo9nFMwnda\nSx9pwbclTi9jWaQpFzR1SBNopI+yUjvlVIqSItsvyqKpugT60Btz+yMt5k6zhlbD\ndkO3iLupq92Q+20eyXxe8C/EASTAg7L6isBHYloVVLlir/gFQrBBzl5nZxugmGJR\nshJOcpYGkH1+RX0AEUz6Wv0d2STlfpro9RujSbZMspFQYAPs7WaYzJaazMkJavi4\n84QfIST8x4IWy+mv5hHTgiCuG0OCx8+JlvTcgJoKzGv1VFk/dZI2La02L+4AAA89\ngXQpt/JUOdRcPJyW3JCK0Y1aNNZizDGqFKiZXxwly70BSsxz0CSsrRWxKU26I+qr\nu/RTFb/93M1oJp1B9vzvcnSIT/GIWwZIreHj+yZpxgRR5Pnu+YNZ3ADtCbDWpZe9\nbo+gIz/8mt53NpOuBQiB/5QL3krOLuduDdkM46+7wNq9wYcueDpj4f/psPGaXs+O\nHqIojhdPJyT+WCRAHZJlaXcFItv0xzCrvyoGWf8N53boKj9IMfXsN8Qr9+Eb0IV6\n/HogG9nZVZjB/eOrovfkcya75AVzyyPNynzthjl2LKt82RxSxReXriQGB07anUj8\n5xaaFBQND2Bhzz0sFWyrM4cWSYAQzQ/Qt3xrVl4HQNND3L+DIre9tkVPtjUFaIMm\nk2c26w80zIRoVlTYgrrP\n=0LcP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T19:00:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/9594703b81012a62ae8588f8db167d7ce7141146","node_id":"C_kwDOTG-nuNoAKDk1OTQ3MDNiODEwMTJhNjJhZTg1ODhmOGRiMTY3ZDdjZTcxNDExNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/ee492a2635d395d036dd51628d2fba4e5298ab77","sha":"ee492a2635d395d036dd51628d2fba4e5298ab77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/ee492a2635d395d036dd51628d2fba4e5298ab77"}],"sha":"9594703b81012a62ae8588f8db167d7ce7141146","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/9594703b81012a62ae8588f8db167d7ce7141146"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/ee492a2635d395d036dd51628d2fba4e5298ab77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:21:39Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:21:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(pipeline): align inter-agent rule contracts and add Agent 5.7 grounding verifier (#122)\n\n* feat(pipeline): add Agent 5.7 independent grounding verifier\n\nAdds a new pipeline stage that runs after all Agent 5.5/5.6 mutations and\nnever repairs or rewrites a rule itself: it projects every description,\ncondition, condition-logic expression, outcome, party, scope, exception, and\ntest vector into atomic claims, asks an independent verification pass to\nclassify each as supported/contradicted/insufficient_evidence, and requires\nevery supported or contradicted claim''s exact quote to be locatable\ndeterministically in the organized source corpus. The stage fails closed on\nany missing, duplicated, contradicted, or insufficiently-evidenced claim.\n\nWires the new stage into the CLI (`--step 5.7`, automatic chaining after\n5.5/5.6, and a hard gate on Step 6 visualization requiring a passing,\nhash-matched grounding certificate), adds its config knobs\n(KG_GROUNDING_*), and documents it in README.md/agents/README.md/\ncomplement-kg.md.\n\nTests: apps/pipeline/tests/test_grounding_verifier.py,\ntest_config_no_hardcoded.py updates for the new profile keys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(pipeline): bridge elided text spans in Agent 3 source quotes\n\nsource_reference.source_text could silently drop real intervening content\nwhen a quote''s start/end words matched the source but the model''s returned\ntext skipped a chunk in between (e.g. a worked \"Example\" paragraph) — the\nquote still validated as containing the endpoints but was not a faithful\ncontiguous excerpt.\n\nAdds bridge_exact_span(), which uses word-level SequenceMatcher matching\nblocks to find the true contiguous span connecting any gap, so a source_text\nthat skips real content gets corrected to the actual excerpt rather than\naccepted as-is.\n\nTests: apps/pipeline/tests/test_agent_3_source_verification.py (12 cases,\nincluding a reconstructed genuinely-unbridgeable fixture verifying the\nexisting lenient-acceptance fallback still applies when no coherent\nword-level run connects the endpoints).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(pipeline): require structural support for Agent 5 dependency edges\n\nAgent 5''s dependency analysis accepted any LLM-proposed rule dependency\nverbatim, with no check that the two rules actually share a variable or\nentity that could make one a real prerequisite/conflict of the other —\nan unsupported edge could reach the final graph unexamined.\n\nAdds dependency_has_structural_support() (a rule pair must share an\noutcome/condition variable, a responsible party/counterparty, or an explicit\npredicate reference before a dependency between them is accepted) and\nannotate_dependency_structural_support(), wired into all three places Agent 5\nproposes dependencies.\n\nTests: apps/pipeline/tests/test_agent_5_dependency_support.py (13 cases).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(pipeline): align Agent 3/5.5 rule shapes with kg_readiness validation\n\nA fresh end-to-end run surfaced a recurring bug shape: one agent (or its\nprompt) produces a field''s value/shape, a downstream validator expects a\ndifferent one, and the mismatch fails silently as \"review required\" rather\nthan crashing — invisible until measured against a real graph. This is a\nbatch of every such mismatch found this pass, plus the test suite built to\ncatch the class going forward.\n\nFixes (each reproduced and measured against a real 352-rule extraction):\n\n- scope_basis \"explicit_in_source\"/\"explicitly_none_in_source\": the model\n  extends exception_basis''s own documented convention to scope_basis by\n  direct analogy (rule_contract_v2.txt documents it for exception_basis but\n  never states scope_basis''s equivalent this precisely). Accepted as final,\n  evidence-requiring states in SCOPE_BASES/FINAL_SCOPE_BASES — 261 of 275\n  schema violations on one real run traced to the first of these alone.\n- A third scope_derivation/exception_verification evidence shape,\n  {derivation_type, source_evidence: [{chunk_path, section_id, quote}]},\n  recognized as an alias of the documented {evidence: [{..., source_text}]}\n  shape in both final_rule_issues and Agent 5.5''s own evidence normalizer.\n- Off-schema exception_basis/scope_basis free text (the model''s own\n  reasoning used wholesale as the enum value, e.g.\n  \"explicit_in_source_but_details_not_in_evidence_packet\") coerced to the\n  correct unresolved_* final state via _coerce_unresolved_basis(), preserving\n  the original text as unresolved_reason instead of failing v2 schema\n  validation with no actionable path.\n- Conflict-analysis gap-fill: entity_conflict_analysis.txt only asks the\n  model for \"every material pair or an unresolved group,\" but the consumer\n  demanded exhaustive pairwise coverage and stamped every uncovered pair as a\n  generic \"unresolved, manual review\" filler — 792 of one real run''s\n  review-required determinations. Small entity groups now get the same\n  mechanical disjoint-outcome-variable proof large groups already had before\n  falling back to a real \"unresolved\" state.\n- Generalized entity-name normalization: PascalCase entity_types keys\n  (CreditScore, DocumentCustodian, ...) only matched a fixed 6-name legacy\n  list; _build_entity_name_map now derives SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE forms from\n  whatever a run actually produced (380 naming violations on one real run),\n  and also catches a rule reference that never appears as an entity_types key\n  at all (a rule citing counterparty \"Borrower\" when entity_types only\n  defines \"BORROWER\") without inventing a mapping for an unrelated typo.\n- applicability_scope missing a standard key after a resolver completion\n  replaces it wholesale (12 rules on one real run) — re-defaulted after the\n  merge, not just before it, both in Agent 5.5 and in final_rule_issues''s own\n  read.\n- A latent crash: final_rule_issues''s unresolved_after_source_review branch\n  still read raw rule.get(\"scope_derivation\", {}).get(...) — the exact\n  AttributeError trap already fixed for exception_verification elsewhere in\n  the same function, just missed here. Hadn''t fired on real data yet, but the\n  new basis-coercion fix above can produce that exact value.\n\nAdds tests/test_inter_agent_contract_alignment.py: mechanical cross-checks\nbetween agent prompts and their validators (FINAL_*_BASES subset of the\nschema enums, prompt-documented enum values parsed and asserted against both,\nevery completion-promised field verified consumed downstream,\n_project_execution''s shape cross-checked against final_rule_issues''s reads)\nso this class of drift fails a test immediately instead of surfacing on a\nlive run.\n\nMeasured impact on one real 352-rule graph across this pass: 24 -> 265 rules\ncertified ready (7% -> 75%); naming_consistency and referential_integrity\ninvariants now pass; conflict-analysis \"unresolved\" determinations 792 -> 20,\nevery remaining one carrying a real, model-written justification.\n\nTests: 1676 passed (up from the pre-existing suite), including 40+ new cases\nacross test_rule_contract.py, test_kg_readiness_malformed_verification.py\n(new), test_entity_name_normalization.py (new), test_executable_readiness.py,\nand test_inter_agent_contract_alignment.py (new).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"12ef5cd5f8548aeb39a5958cb59d029a630531cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/12ef5cd5f8548aeb39a5958cb59d029a630531cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/ee492a2635d395d036dd51628d2fba4e5298ab77","verification":{"payload":"tree 12ef5cd5f8548aeb39a5958cb59d029a630531cf\nparent b6f95a6e3b35781f2df3b4435c473bcf216fdb3e\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1787419299 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787419299 -0700\n\nfix(pipeline): align inter-agent rule contracts and add Agent 5.7 grounding verifier (#122)\n\n* feat(pipeline): add Agent 5.7 independent grounding verifier\n\nAdds a new pipeline stage that runs after all Agent 5.5/5.6 mutations and\nnever repairs or rewrites a rule itself: it projects every description,\ncondition, condition-logic expression, outcome, party, scope, exception, and\ntest vector into atomic claims, asks an independent verification pass to\nclassify each as supported/contradicted/insufficient_evidence, and requires\nevery supported or contradicted claim''s exact quote to be locatable\ndeterministically in the organized source corpus. The stage fails closed on\nany missing, duplicated, contradicted, or insufficiently-evidenced claim.\n\nWires the new stage into the CLI (`--step 5.7`, automatic chaining after\n5.5/5.6, and a hard gate on Step 6 visualization requiring a passing,\nhash-matched grounding certificate), adds its config knobs\n(KG_GROUNDING_*), and documents it in README.md/agents/README.md/\ncomplement-kg.md.\n\nTests: apps/pipeline/tests/test_grounding_verifier.py,\ntest_config_no_hardcoded.py updates for the new profile keys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(pipeline): bridge elided text spans in Agent 3 source quotes\n\nsource_reference.source_text could silently drop real intervening content\nwhen a quote''s start/end words matched the source but the model''s returned\ntext skipped a chunk in between (e.g. a worked \"Example\" paragraph) — the\nquote still validated as containing the endpoints but was not a faithful\ncontiguous excerpt.\n\nAdds bridge_exact_span(), which uses word-level SequenceMatcher matching\nblocks to find the true contiguous span connecting any gap, so a source_text\nthat skips real content gets corrected to the actual excerpt rather than\naccepted as-is.\n\nTests: apps/pipeline/tests/test_agent_3_source_verification.py (12 cases,\nincluding a reconstructed genuinely-unbridgeable fixture verifying the\nexisting lenient-acceptance fallback still applies when no coherent\nword-level run connects the endpoints).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(pipeline): require structural support for Agent 5 dependency edges\n\nAgent 5''s dependency analysis accepted any LLM-proposed rule dependency\nverbatim, with no check that the two rules actually share a variable or\nentity that could make one a real prerequisite/conflict of the other —\nan unsupported edge could reach the final graph unexamined.\n\nAdds dependency_has_structural_support() (a rule pair must share an\noutcome/condition variable, a responsible party/counterparty, or an explicit\npredicate reference before a dependency between them is accepted) and\nannotate_dependency_structural_support(), wired into all three places Agent 5\nproposes dependencies.\n\nTests: apps/pipeline/tests/test_agent_5_dependency_support.py (13 cases).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(pipeline): align Agent 3/5.5 rule shapes with kg_readiness validation\n\nA fresh end-to-end run surfaced a recurring bug shape: one agent (or its\nprompt) produces a field''s value/shape, a downstream validator expects a\ndifferent one, and the mismatch fails silently as \"review required\" rather\nthan crashing — invisible until measured against a real graph. This is a\nbatch of every such mismatch found this pass, plus the test suite built to\ncatch the class going forward.\n\nFixes (each reproduced and measured against a real 352-rule extraction):\n\n- scope_basis \"explicit_in_source\"/\"explicitly_none_in_source\": the model\n  extends exception_basis''s own documented convention to scope_basis by\n  direct analogy (rule_contract_v2.txt documents it for exception_basis but\n  never states scope_basis''s equivalent this precisely). Accepted as final,\n  evidence-requiring states in SCOPE_BASES/FINAL_SCOPE_BASES — 261 of 275\n  schema violations on one real run traced to the first of these alone.\n- A third scope_derivation/exception_verification evidence shape,\n  {derivation_type, source_evidence: [{chunk_path, section_id, quote}]},\n  recognized as an alias of the documented {evidence: [{..., source_text}]}\n  shape in both final_rule_issues and Agent 5.5''s own evidence normalizer.\n- Off-schema exception_basis/scope_basis free text (the model''s own\n  reasoning used wholesale as the enum value, e.g.\n  \"explicit_in_source_but_details_not_in_evidence_packet\") coerced to the\n  correct unresolved_* final state via _coerce_unresolved_basis(), preserving\n  the original text as unresolved_reason instead of failing v2 schema\n  validation with no actionable path.\n- Conflict-analysis gap-fill: entity_conflict_analysis.txt only asks the\n  model for \"every material pair or an unresolved group,\" but the consumer\n  demanded exhaustive pairwise coverage and stamped every uncovered pair as a\n  generic \"unresolved, manual review\" filler — 792 of one real run''s\n  review-required determinations. Small entity groups now get the same\n  mechanical disjoint-outcome-variable proof large groups already had before\n  falling back to a real \"unresolved\" state.\n- Generalized entity-name normalization: PascalCase entity_types keys\n  (CreditScore, DocumentCustodian, ...) only matched a fixed 6-name legacy\n  list; _build_entity_name_map now derives SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE forms from\n  whatever a run actually produced (380 naming violations on one real run),\n  and also catches a rule reference that never appears as an entity_types key\n  at all (a rule citing counterparty \"Borrower\" when entity_types only\n  defines \"BORROWER\") without inventing a mapping for an unrelated typo.\n- applicability_scope missing a standard key after a resolver completion\n  replaces it wholesale (12 rules on one real run) — re-defaulted after the\n  merge, not just before it, both in Agent 5.5 and in final_rule_issues''s own\n  read.\n- A latent crash: final_rule_issues''s unresolved_after_source_review branch\n  still read raw rule.get(\"scope_derivation\", {}).get(...) — the exact\n  AttributeError trap already fixed for exception_verification elsewhere in\n  the same function, just missed here. Hadn''t fired on real data yet, but the\n  new basis-coercion fix above can produce that exact value.\n\nAdds tests/test_inter_agent_contract_alignment.py: mechanical cross-checks\nbetween agent prompts and their validators (FINAL_*_BASES subset of the\nschema enums, prompt-documented enum values parsed and asserted against both,\nevery completion-promised field verified consumed downstream,\n_project_execution''s shape cross-checked against final_rule_issues''s reads)\nso this class of drift fails a test immediately instead of surfacing on a\nlive run.\n\nMeasured impact on one real 352-rule graph across this pass: 24 -> 265 rules\ncertified ready (7% -> 75%); naming_consistency and referential_integrity\ninvariants now pass; conflict-analysis \"unresolved\" determinations 792 -> 20,\nevery remaining one carrying a real, model-written justification.\n\nTests: 1676 passed (up from the pre-existing suite), including 40+ new cases\nacross test_rule_contract.py, test_kg_readiness_malformed_verification.py\n(new), test_entity_name_normalization.py (new), test_executable_readiness.py,\nand test_inter_agent_contract_alignment.py (new).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqidqjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANeoQAFa+IhDqLDS1tWztJgY21mFq\nCkElZpEVlKru4VqYbJdLpZHL77EywANGyZt76uP6TTUMBzbUyxmW1QO2+GhC9Thg\nPZhXO+2VO3q7qTeKgBAGlgEVV/14V00W9YiloOVuV1gmkIuUMwcK85WnZY/bGErV\nPq7OIHk1hKdmNfykj3Vo1sVTTHDMm/VEOhpM1k3X+gsvIeJd9IXbKs8YXAHUQfoo\nSsGs4w4GMY0wnVbE00L2IHMNZQSiifCfzDZG4ht97KwiAFqG/YYVN3kBKlhLFFHF\npmJ7TCAlb1NJNGYGWLMCoQQQ1vTAK/JDuKCaW+7zzFoaF61aYS6i2/9DqrlyWXB0\nnrrKbPYvCtxLCl7YdlQyUbtx5CYdXfRUMm9agHIUnCtNPpxThizlYsRVxd2jEOk4\n5sJxgoF8YlKrLRE8LJgZJ/wI/JGIaEVYRCBa/IZ97CO