,"sha":"6b3d4358e4b24a19d34f366c2cabcf20bc7a76fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/6b3d4358e4b24a19d34f366c2cabcf20bc7a76fa"}],"sha":"b6f95a6e3b35781f2df3b4435c473bcf216fdb3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/b6f95a6e3b35781f2df3b4435c473bcf216fdb3e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/6b3d4358e4b24a19d34f366c2cabcf20bc7a76fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T05:14:03Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T05:14:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: remove the pipeline-p2c policy compiler app (#120)\n\nRemoves apps/pipeline-p2c (457 tracked files) and everything that pointed at\nit. Verified first that apps/pipeline does not depend on it: apps/pipeline has\nno code reference to p2c at all, and p2c''s `from pipeline.stages import ...`\nresolves to its own internal apps/pipeline-p2c/pipeline/ package, not to\napps/pipeline. The coupling ran one way only — p2c''s ingestion tests read the\ncorpus from apps/pipeline/compliance-files, and one markdown scope note in\napps/pipeline referenced p2c.\n\nAlso removed:\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml — the p2c-pytest job and its allure upload, which\n  would fail immediately with the directory gone\n- .gitignore — the 45-line p2c section covering compliance-files and the\n  stage 02/03/04/06/07/08 output artefacts\n- docs/STRUCTURE.md — the pipeline-p2c subtree; removing only its heading line\n  would have orphaned policy_ir/, ingestion/, compilers/ and the rest\n- apps/pipeline/complement-kg.md — a scope note asserting the complement does\n  not change p2c\n\nLeft untouched: the two docs/research/ plans that reference p2c. They are\nrecords of intent at a point in time, and the NeurIPS plan names p2c as its\ncandidate system — that is a call for the author, not a mechanical edit.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"719d076a24b10722adf115a957fff307bc7dbf78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/719d076a24b10722adf115a957fff307bc7dbf78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/6b3d4358e4b24a19d34f366c2cabcf20bc7a76fa","verification":{"payload":"tree 719d076a24b10722adf115a957fff307bc7dbf78\nparent 19780d6eddf50314c04f814ca955022f2c1ceab7\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1787375643 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787375643 -0700\n\nchore: remove the pipeline-p2c policy compiler app (#120)\n\nRemoves apps/pipeline-p2c (457 tracked files) and everything that pointed at\nit. Verified first that apps/pipeline does not depend on it: apps/pipeline has\nno code reference to p2c at all, and p2c''s `from pipeline.stages import ...`\nresolves to its own internal apps/pipeline-p2c/pipeline/ package, not to\napps/pipeline. The coupling ran one way only — p2c''s ingestion tests read the\ncorpus from apps/pipeline/compliance-files, and one markdown scope note in\napps/pipeline referenced p2c.\n\nAlso removed:\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml — the p2c-pytest job and its allure upload, which\n  would fail immediately with the directory gone\n- .gitignore — the 45-line p2c section covering compliance-files and the\n  stage 02/03/04/06/07/08 output artefacts\n- docs/STRUCTURE.md — the pipeline-p2c subtree; removing only its heading line\n  would have orphaned policy_ir/, ingestion/, compilers/ and the rest\n- apps/pipeline/complement-kg.md — a scope note asserting the complement does\n  not change p2c\n\nLeft untouched: the two docs/research/ plans that reference p2c. They are\nrecords of intent at a point in time, and the NeurIPS plan names p2c as its\ncandidate system — that is a call for the author, not a mechanical edit.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiTAbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAVkQAF4wWM2AAThbVUqGx89ED7Yf\nOuEty3cV1VW/dd4Bc/MTYjWwJstlEe95JmcwPppphCew5eqFrBCuSxSat5McaEbn\n9CO9Wd0TFo9uPfBfCr8J1RQMYN/eGpjDR3TCcGNbGXdUtW5tnlL5ffyK2VxqyyIB\n1talhfMEFSI2idXKade1s5EOOW1SIYfJyVwunlvojO3TMSKYRKIbtg4JPb/9uKGw\n50a4GtM6+WPqsxP4mMPK9iFjqbVVL9WYCAElOD/k9d2T7PcYLdab0otJ/0p9A/ea\nca7DCwMzr7K0mXnJ80Pq3KH5G5j71+fUJM6BXkEQsWbRVqumVy2q0pY6zl09Ik0r\nWLn2CeUE7OkARND3BliAB0L0yEj09hJZ/W3S/BHA42g4c3ek0KSvEU8SPnR6ETc3\nKhQ8DmF3JfpxmT8KfJFm5lX9/JRH5K2IicX2Sgb6LeBUApBS/w2ZCt1TPPkCXyTc\nggioqhYb6a0aTyEJngs1X/I1CPQlcgicpCJl/veq0kenw5Y5WK22kx9RguJ4OWqE\nxvNF9qx/FuXQaDl9f2eUviX4nNRooNjKd8F3QIhzaVLUghgkG5/H0pm4vV53RPWu\nfhjV6U/D75jkl0R6ISi78LEVdhcvrmv04NUhJOAvHQHJQpplzodEi7PyfLlLqskn\nhQYjzzlbuZCOhKz2REyW\n=tpgb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T05:14:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/6b3d4358e4b24a19d34f366c2cabcf20bc7a76fa","node_id":"C_kwDOTG-nuNoAKDZiM2Q0MzU4ZTRiMjRhMTlkMzRmMzY2YzJjYWJjZjIwYmM3YTc2ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/19780d6eddf50314c04f814ca955022f2c1ceab7","sha":"19780d6eddf50314c04f814ca955022f2c1ceab7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/19780d6eddf50314c04f814ca955022f2c1ceab7"}],"sha":"6b3d4358e4b24a19d34f366c2cabcf20bc7a76fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/6b3d4358e4b24a19d34f366c2cabcf20bc7a76fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/19780d6eddf50314c04f814ca955022f2c1ceab7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T04:36:14Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T04:36:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add CUAD, OPP-115, ContractNLI, and MAPP benchmark corpora with matching domain prompt packs (#118)\n\n* feat(pipeline): add executable kg readiness pass\n\n* fix(pipeline): enforce monotonic llm watchdog deadline\n\n* fix(pipeline): retry truncated rule batches\n\n* fix(pipeline): retry truncated rule parse responses\n\n* fix(pipeline): retry truncated rule batches with larger budget\n\n* docs(pipeline): document stable extraction profile\n\n* fix(pipeline): back off transport retries\n\n* fix(pipeline): checkpoint successful rule batches\n\n* fix(pipeline): bound readiness evidence prompts\n\n* fix(pipeline): escape conflict analysis prompt json\n\n* perf(pipeline): parallelize readiness evidence checks\n\n* feat(benchmarks): add legal/privacy benchmark corpora fetcher\n\nAdd apps/benchmarks with a reproducible downloader for the four\nexpert-annotated corpora we evaluate the extraction pipeline against:\nCUAD v1, OPP-115, ContractNLI, and the MAPP Corpus.\n\nThe corpora are fetched, not vendored — data/ and raw/ are git-ignored\n(~595 MB extracted, ~259 MB archived, two redistribution-restricted).\ndatasets.json pins each upstream URL, SHA-256, license, citation, and\nverified contents so a fresh clone reproduces byte-identical data.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(benchmarks): build pipeline-ready source docs per benchmark\n\nAdd scripts/build_source_docs.py, which normalizes each corpus''s documents\ninto a flat <benchmark>-source-docs/ folder of .txt so every benchmark can\nbe run through the extraction pipeline into its own knowledge graph:\n\n  cuad-source-docs         510 docs   copied verbatim from full_contract_txt\n  opp-115-source-docs      115 docs   ||| segments unwrapped from sanitized HTML\n  contract-nli-source-docs 607 docs   text field of the train/dev/test splits\n  mapp-source-docs         155 docs   EN + DE policies, en_/de_ prefixed\n\nEach folder emits the same text the gold annotations index into, so extracted\nrules stay alignable with the gold labels, plus a _manifest.json mapping every\nfilename back to its annotation key. Verified: CUAD byte-identical (510/510),\nContractNLI text-exact with in-range spans (607/607), OPP-115 segment counts\nmatching the annotation CSVs (115/115), MAPP annotations resolving (155/155).\n\nDerived output is git-ignored alongside data/ and raw/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(pipeline): add benchmark-corpus domain prompt packs for CUAD, ContractNLI, OPP-115, and MAPP (#119)\n\n* fix(pipeline): bound large entity conflict analysis\n\n* feat(pipeline): add benchmark-corpus domain prompt packs\n\nAdd four domain packs so each benchmark corpus can be extracted with a rule\nvocabulary aligned to its own gold taxonomy, instead of the mortgage default:\n\n  commercial_contracts  <- CUAD          41 clause categories\n  nda_confidentiality   <- ContractNLI   17 confidentiality propositions\n  privacy_policy        <- OPP-115       10 data-practice categories\n  mobile_app_privacy    <- MAPP          practice attrs incl. GDPR legal basis\n\nEach pack ships 13 templates, not the conventional 11. Agents 2 and 3 request\nentity_extraction_compact and business_rules_extraction_compact, which no\nexisting domain overrides, so today every domain runs entity and rule\nextraction on shared prompts that say \"prefer concrete mortgage concepts\".\nThose two templates are what decide what gets extracted at all, so the packs\noverride them; the non-compact pair is kept for the data-contract tests.\n\nPacks are generated by scripts/generate_benchmark_domain_prompts.py from a\nper-domain profile, keeping 52 templates structurally consistent. Also\nregisters rule-type palettes and quick-filter types in utils/config.py, graph\nname inference in graph_service.py, and the domains in config.example.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7fd9025b570354270a6097e7cb2e05ac55362e80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/7fd9025b570354270a6097e7cb2e05ac55362e80"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/19780d6eddf50314c04f814ca955022f2c1ceab7","verification":{"payload":"tree 7fd9025b570354270a6097e7cb2e05ac55362e80\nparent b3d15b2d00d7d6421643c68ee21371ca23266fda\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1787373374 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787373374 -0700\n\nfeat: add CUAD, OPP-115, ContractNLI, and MAPP benchmark corpora with matching domain prompt packs (#118)\n\n* feat(pipeline): add executable kg readiness pass\n\n* fix(pipeline): enforce monotonic llm watchdog deadline\n\n* fix(pipeline): retry truncated rule batches\n\n* fix(pipeline): retry truncated rule parse responses\n\n* fix(pipeline): retry truncated rule batches with larger budget\n\n* docs(pipeline): document stable extraction profile\n\n* fix(pipeline): back off transport retries\n\n* fix(pipeline): checkpoint successful rule batches\n\n* fix(pipeline): bound readiness evidence prompts\n\n* fix(pipeline): escape conflict analysis prompt json\n\n* perf(pipeline): parallelize readiness evidence checks\n\n* feat(benchmarks): add legal/privacy benchmark corpora fetcher\n\nAdd apps/benchmarks with a reproducible downloader for the four\nexpert-annotated corpora we evaluate the extraction pipeline against:\nCUAD v1, OPP-115, ContractNLI, and the MAPP Corpus.\n\nThe corpora are fetched, not vendored — data/ and raw/ are git-ignored\n(~595 MB extracted, ~259 MB archived, two redistribution-restricted).\ndatasets.json pins each upstream URL, SHA-256, license, citation, and\nverified contents so a fresh clone reproduces byte-identical data.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(benchmarks): build pipeline-ready source docs per benchmark\n\nAdd scripts/build_source_docs.py, which normalizes each corpus''s documents\ninto a flat <benchmark>-source-docs/ folder of .txt so every benchmark can\nbe run through the extraction pipeline into its own knowledge graph:\n\n  cuad-source-docs         510 docs   copied verbatim from full_contract_txt\n  opp-115-source-docs      115 docs   ||| segments unwrapped from sanitized HTML\n  contract-nli-source-docs 607 docs   text field of the train/dev/test splits\n  mapp-source-docs         155 docs   EN + DE policies, en_/de_ prefixed\n\nEach folder emits the same text the gold annotations index into, so extracted\nrules stay alignable with the gold labels, plus a _manifest.json mapping every\nfilename back to its annotation key. Verified: CUAD byte-identical (510/510),\nContractNLI text-exact with in-range spans (607/607), OPP-115 segment counts\nmatching the annotation CSVs (115/115), MAPP annotations resolving (155/155).\n\nDerived output is git-ignored alongside data/ and raw/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(pipeline): add benchmark-corpus domain prompt packs for CUAD, ContractNLI, OPP-115, and MAPP (#119)\n\n* fix(pipeline): bound large entity conflict analysis\n\n* feat(pipeline): add benchmark-corpus domain prompt packs\n\nAdd four domain packs so each benchmark corpus can be extracted with a rule\nvocabulary aligned to its own gold taxonomy, instead of the mortgage default:\n\n  commercial_contracts  <- CUAD          41 clause categories\n  nda_confidentiality   <- ContractNLI   17 confidentiality propositions\n  privacy_policy        <- OPP-115       10 data-practice categories\n  mobile_app_privacy    <- MAPP          practice attrs incl. GDPR legal basis\n\nEach pack ships 13 templates, not the conventional 11. Agents 2 and 3 request\nentity_extraction_compact and business_rules_extraction_compact, which no\nexisting domain overrides, so today every domain runs entity and rule\nextraction on shared prompts that say \"prefer concrete mortgage concepts\".\nThose two templates are what decide what gets extracted at all, so the packs\noverride them; the non-compact pair is kept for the data-contract tests.\n\nPacks are generated by scripts/generate_benchmark_domain_prompts.py from a\nper-domain profile, keeping 52 templates structurally consistent. Also\nregisters rule-type palettes and quick-filter types in utils/config.py, graph\nname inference in graph_service.py, and the domains in config.example.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiSc+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxzEQABM9vhV1AvicvP0a14OsfXdB\nb7S48eGSCu15ziRnAlaoDYrqYXu3WKY+qfglRwNLhmj95DirTiJDd4AV3gVuv+ur\nl317mgQjrTHHj8BYx7V36AbJTjNAvAZJJmXKNPzV0GsXQNqoOHzptbzJLb+jvlvb\n4xDA4CjN4Hnz9Zb8d8u+I1