om/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/a5f7aca756662189653a377303740091e40c6e59"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/2106d5a149c2085b6ec11e1887df4841ae3af066/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T01:51:34Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T01:51:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pipeline-p2c): model extraction pass, nine-stage runner, and interactive report (#112)\n\nFills the model-extractor seam pipeline-p2c was designed around, wires the app into a\nstaged resumable nine-stage pipeline ending in an interactive HTML report, and runs it\nend to end on the 1,191-page Fannie Mae Selling Guide.\n\nThe semantic layer is now stage 05 — before any executable projection, not skippable.\n`semantic/` existed but nothing invoked it, which left the pipeline free to drift\nDMN-first. The knowledge graph is the canonical representation; DMN and BPMN are narrow\nprojections of the subset that qualifies.\n\nThe run: 1,191 pages, 324 chunks, 11,678 units, gpt-5.2 at high reasoning, 324 calls\nwith 0 failures, 3.32M tokens, 6,104 proposals, 5,003 clauses admitted, 12,237 evidence\nspans, and 5,003 of 5,003 provenance-exact — every cited span matches its document hash\nat the exact offsets recorded. Zero DMN decisions and zero BPMN processes is the designed\noutcome: nothing becomes a decision table or workflow by default, 401 clauses are\nrecorded as ready_for_explicit_model, and 3,298 declare no projection at all because\ndefinitions, entities and constraints belong in the graph and nowhere else.\n\nSix failure classes came out of the run, all the same mistake — an open schema slot the\nmodel filled reasonably and the parser then refused, one paid call at a time. Durations\n(18% of the first 45 chunks), dates, duplicate citation roles, repeated unit indexes.\nEach is fixed by constraining the slot so the bad value is impossible to express rather\nthan refused after payment, and the narrowing lives in the extraction contract only,\nnever the IR schema.\n\nFour more defects came from looking at the rendered report: the six independent statuses\ndrawn as a funnel that claimed a nesting which does not exist; \"DMN eligible: 0\" silently\ndropped when it was the most important number on the page; a graph contradicting its own\nlegend because vis-network''s group palette overrode explicit colours; and a caption\nnaming a directory that the stage renumbering had moved.\n\nThe most consequential: segment_by_section split over-long sections on a hard character\nbudget, cutting 58 of 324 chunks mid-word. Every span stayed byte-exact — which is why\nthe gate reported 100% provenance and no test caught it — but the first unit of such a\nchunk read mid-token and the sentence straddling the cut was never shown whole to an\nextractor. Boundaries now snap to whitespace. This changes chunk IDs, so the committed\nartefacts were produced by the pre-fix chunking; they remain internally consistent and\nfully provenance-exact, and regenerating them means re-running the model pass.\n\nDurability was learned by losing 45 already-paid-for chunks to an interrupted run.\nReplies are now persisted as they arrive, resume is verdict-aware so a fix costs only the\nchunks that still need calling, and --reparse re-derives proposals from stored raw\nreplies with no model calls.\n\n674 passed, 8 skipped. 118 new tests, each naming the failure it prevents from recurring.\nCommitted outputs are 350 files / 22.7 MB; the 92 MB of derived bulk is rebuilt by\ndeterministic stages in about six seconds, verified byte-for-byte rather than asserted.","tree":{"sha":"05df8f24501516c97f4fe8f1e0e540d4ebc360e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/05df8f24501516c97f4fe8f1e0e540d4ebc360e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/2106d5a149c2085b6ec11e1887df4841ae3af066","verification":{"payload":"tree 05df8f24501516c97f4fe8f1e0e540d4ebc360e5\nparent 4f789f5b1df468b9a6a8e7b8e7dfed06700e65e8\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1787190694 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787190694 -0700\n\nfeat(pipeline-p2c): model extraction pass, nine-stage runner, and interactive report (#112)\n\nFills the model-extractor seam pipeline-p2c was designed around, wires the app into a\nstaged resumable nine-stage pipeline ending in an interactive HTML report, and runs it\nend to end on the 1,191-page Fannie Mae Selling Guide.\n\nThe semantic layer is now stage 05 — before any executable projection, not skippable.\n`semantic/` existed but nothing invoked it, which left the pipeline free to drift\nDMN-first. The knowledge graph is the canonical representation; DMN and BPMN are narrow\nprojections of the subset that qualifies.\n\nThe run: 1,191 pages, 324 chunks, 11,678 units, gpt-5.2 at high reasoning, 324 calls\nwith 0 failures, 3.32M tokens, 6,104 proposals, 5,003 clauses admitted, 12,237 evidence\nspans, and 5,003 of 5,003 provenance-exact — every cited span matches its document hash\nat the exact offsets recorded. Zero DMN decisions and zero BPMN processes is the designed\noutcome: nothing becomes a decision table or workflow by default, 401 clauses are\nrecorded as ready_for_explicit_model, and 3,298 declare no projection at all because\ndefinitions, entities and constraints belong in the graph and nowhere else.\n\nSix failure classes came out of the run, all the same mistake — an open schema slot the\nmodel filled reasonably and the parser then refused, one paid call at a time. Durations\n(18% of the first 45 chunks), dates, duplicate citation roles, repeated unit indexes.\nEach is fixed by constraining the slot so the bad value is impossible to express rather\nthan refused after payment, and the narrowing lives in the extraction contract only,\nnever the IR schema.\n\nFour more defects came from looking at the rendered report: the six independent statuses\ndrawn as a funnel that claimed a nesting which does not exist; \"DMN eligible: 0\" silently\ndropped when it was the most important number on the page; a graph contradicting its own\nlegend because vis-network''s group palette overrode explicit colours; and a caption\nnaming a directory that the stage renumbering had moved.\n\nThe most consequential: segment_by_section split over-long sections on a hard character\nbudget, cutting 58 of 324 chunks mid-word. Every span stayed byte-exact — which is why\nthe gate reported 100% provenance and no test caught it — but the first unit of such a\nchunk read mid-token and the sentence straddling the cut was never shown whole to an\nextractor. Boundaries now snap to whitespace. This changes chunk IDs, so the committed\nartefacts were produced by the pre-fix chunking; they remain internally consistent and\nfully provenance-exact, and regenerating them means re-running the model pass.\n\nDurability was learned by losing 45 already-paid-for chunks to an interrupted run.\nReplies are now persisted as they arrive, resume is verdict-aware so a fix costs only the\nchunks that still need calling, and --reparse re-derives proposals from stored raw\nreplies with no model calls.\n\n674 passed, 8 skipped. 118 new tests, each naming the failure it prevents from recurring.\nCommitted outputs are 350 files / 22.7 MB; the 92 MB of derived bulk is rebuilt by\ndeterministic stages in about six seconds, verified byte-for-byte rather than asserted.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhl2mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOrkQAJCKkTEpBmpz0EFqByoCbEEv\nLVtjj9CILOKFy2cy6GZXRT+DR6LfSKqgXBsblj53Bphh7xv9H+5Lpf+6wUHj+md5\nZTmQOX9O8L3XbZEz4yKjiuWP4Jbmr8vxPwCStBDoOjOqC9jpr61IH8yzuKx35bkL\ngxtO8UmPEivge93DgEuQjbHL/BrY3V6QG0rtnj7NSaM0iLJZbb9e8jZ1JQP6dsj+\n6xwdDOlQhZ1AFDSav3aeu0bN+gVWFxuiLx6MCPcjXgLVfx5NvFugmcVjb4IYm51a\n37Mfya2yV1IAKgOuza0QJtKJOJcTBvQPCRB92KwrCrpPUhVm9X2thOEu6w33GOp/\nq8vq3FoqciO9gtSBjYSiEZ0bnGPjAT/Kapoj3RJMdNfQTmOfru4JCbdvLJlGLMNy\nrON+TeG2WyrLb7nlXfESwL/YtgylvVD2YYdZCijOExzV/53FjFnIh1/1xCvc3LR3\n7ynzkqkdYh4nabRRKwTGnpaFKqZY47Q+1Yw7nOnmrfnPeU8nvczY/+JhNSB7mN70\n3pWX3dnnq93E6XR53hb3iH7A/jFaXwrlIIA1Qx++BwBW/dHsAGEbFbtgf6GRFPGe\npWi94xYpdIOh/qLVyjkmYRjJRXhSMOMAsaYmLrVUiTTsMn1ssJ65ZxDrUA3yzahf\nEU/LuYOFuuvpWABp9KUO\n=eUOE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T01:51:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https:/