7cf1d5fa862a2949900dffa6ccf360cb3e8b"}],"sha":"5e4e541d9d75bf6e90b07dccc0c0233fdad24e1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/5e4e541d9d75bf6e90b07dccc0c0233fdad24e1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/368c7cf1d5fa862a2949900dffa6ccf360cb3e8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:49:08Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:49:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add pipeline-p2c, an evidence-bound policy compiler for DMN and BPMN (#90)\n\n* feat(pipeline-p2c): add evidence-bound policy compiler for DMN and BPMN\n\nAdds apps/pipeline-p2c, implementing the deterministic core of\ndocs/research/policy-to-dmn-bpmn.md: a typed, evidence-anchored Policy IR\nv2 plus a fail-closed gate and three deterministic projections — the\nlegacy-compatible knowledge graph, DMN 1.5, and a conservative BPMN 2.0.2\nsubset.\n\nThe governing invariant is that no model element is emitted without\nsource-supported typed semantics. Policy IR records therefore carry no\neligibility verdicts of their own; the gate produces an admission report\nand the compilers consult only that, so nothing can mark itself\nexecutable.\n\nStructure (dependencies point one way, no cycles):\n\n- policy_ir/    closed enums, restricted expression AST, type checker,\n                FEEL serialiser and reader, decision-table decomposition\n                with a non-overlap prover, content-derived IDs, and a\n                JSON Schema generated from the dataclasses\n- ingestion/    immutable source registry: byte and canonical-text\n                hashes, real character offsets, evidence spans\n- validation/   the fail-closed gate: provenance verification, type\n                checking, literal and modality attestation, and six\n                independent admission statuses with named blockers\n- evaluation/   reference Policy IR evaluator with Kleene three-valued\n                logic, so a missing input is UNKNOWN rather than false\n- compilers/    graph projection, DMN 1.5, BPMN 2.0.2, traceability,\n                manifest, and offline structural verification\n- adapters/     legacy knowledge graph import that fabricates no\n                evidence, no expressions and no classifications\n- fixtures/     14 conformance fixtures with declared expected outcomes\n- cli/          compile_policy, with meaningful exit codes\n\nWhat the compiler refuses to do is the substance of the change: it will\nnot guess a hit policy (UNIQUE requires a machine-checked non-overlap\nproof), turn a temporal constraint into a BPMN timer, invent a gateway,\naccept a numeric or modal value the cited span does not contain, unify\nmismatched units or calendars, treat a missing input as false, or let a\nmodel author FEEL or XML.\n\nStandards targets verified against the normative OMG schemas on\n2026-08-19: DMN 1.5 formal/24-01-01 and BPMN 2.0.2 formal/13-12-09. DMN\n1.6 and 1.7 are listed by OMG as beta and are deliberately not targeted.\nThe schemas are not redistributed; schemas/PINNED.json records their URLs\nand SHA-256s and scripts/fetch_schemas.py reproduces exactly those bytes.\n\nAdds a \"Policy Compiler · pytest\" CI job and records the app in\ndocs/STRUCTURE.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(pipeline-p2c): drop unused imports\n\npyflakes reports clean across the app now, apart from the deliberate\n`# noqa: F401` re-exports in the package __init__ files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(pipeline-p2c): drop an unused parameter and tidy imports\n\n- _decision_is_emittable never read the IR; the parameter is gone.\n- Hoist two function-local imports that guarded against a cycle that no\n  longer exists after tabular/feel moved into policy_ir.\n- Group the policy_ir imports together in the two files where that move\n  left them stranded below the validation imports.\n\nNo behaviour change: the suite still passes and compiled output is\nbyte-identical.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0a650be68f647a7c0eb484a74f7e0dee1399856e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/0a650be68f647a7c0eb484a74f7e0dee1399856e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/368c7cf1d5fa862a2949900dffa6ccf360cb3e8b","verification":{"payload":"tree 0a650be68f647a7c0eb484a74f7e0dee1399856e\nparent b54143a1b0295cf59acca6051cbcb07f57492353\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1787154548 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787154548 -0700\n\nfeat: add pipeline-p2c, an evidence-bound policy compiler for DMN and BPMN (#90)\n\n* feat(pipeline-p2c): add evidence-bound policy compiler for DMN and BPMN\n\nAdds apps/pipeline-p2c, implementing the deterministic core of\ndocs/research/policy-to-dmn-bpmn.md: a typed, evidence-anchored Policy IR\nv2 plus a fail-closed gate and three deterministic projections — the\nlegacy-compatible knowledge graph, DMN 1.5, and a conservative BPMN 2.0.2\nsubset.\n\nThe governing invariant is that no model element is emitted without\nsource-supported typed semantics. Policy IR records therefore carry no\neligibility verdicts of their own; the gate produces an admission report\nand the compilers consult only that, so nothing can mark itself\nexecutable.\n\nStructure (dependencies point one way, no cycles):\n\n- policy_ir/    closed enums, restricted expression AST, type checker,\n                FEEL serialiser and reader, decision-table decomposition\n                with a non-overlap prover, content-derived IDs, and a\n                JSON Schema generated from the dataclasses\n- ingestion/    immutable source registry: byte and canonical-text\n                hashes, real character offsets, evidence spans\n- validation/   the fail-closed gate: provenance verification, type\n                checking, literal and modality attestation, and six\n                independent admission statuses with named blockers\n- evaluation/   reference Policy IR evaluator with Kleene three-valued\n                logic, so a missing input is UNKNOWN rather than false\n- compilers/    graph projection, DMN 1.5, BPMN 2.0.2, traceability,\n                manifest, and offline structural verification\n- adapters/     legacy knowledge graph import that fabricates no\n                evidence, no expressions and no classifications\n- fixtures/     14 conformance fixtures with declared expected outcomes\n- cli/          compile_policy, with meaningful exit codes\n\nWhat the compiler refuses to do is the substance of the change: it will\nnot guess a hit policy (UNIQUE requires a machine-checked non-overlap\nproof), turn a temporal constraint into a BPMN timer, invent a gateway,\naccept a numeric or modal value the cited span does not contain, unify\nmismatched units or calendars, treat a missing input as false, or let a\nmodel author FEEL or XML.\n\nStandards targets verified against the normative OMG schemas on\n2026-08-19: DMN 1.5 formal/24-01-01 and BPMN 2.0.2 formal/13-12-09. DMN\n1.6 and 1.7 are listed by OMG as beta and are deliberately not targeted.\nThe schemas are not redistributed; schemas/PINNED.json records their URLs\nand SHA-256s and scripts/fetch_schemas.py reproduces exactly those bytes.\n\nAdds a \"Policy Compiler · pytest\" CI job and records the app in\ndocs/STRUCTURE.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(pipeline-p2c): drop unused imports\n\npyflakes reports clean across the app now, apart from the deliberate\n`# noqa: F401` re-exports in the package __init__ files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(pipeline-p2c): drop an unused parameter and tidy imports\n\n- _decision_is_emittable never read the IR; the parameter is gone.\n- Hoist two function-local imports that guarded against a cycle that no\n  longer exists after tabular/feel moved into policy_ir.\n- Group the policy_ir imports together in the two files where that move\n  left them stranded below the validation imports.\n\nNo behaviour change: the suite still passes and compiled output is\nbyte-identical.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhdB0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQosQAJ7rLi1eZiHkgM8yWU0AxntB\ngukj2TBBNPys2azCL/yNfJaRDFSmvsLcJkzHuqrERJ0YTSMPSxQxz1rG/XpWrZ/z\nFHl9rZEk6DfkTGlnHH3/iBiQEyus4b6n32qNA66oThW0vtkrXhLBxlksEja9ZIZK\nrM8NLoLCLy8aHsBGF1Sl40w9Gwvob4x4XwKnC0cokZXUfSpiAoFUa/WntUtnLJH3\nzi4uxUPAPxitmEdpWBgkVL7Zar2/794