in":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/1b063fbc6013e5ab3335fab20349b337d6a4f161/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T14:11:40Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T14:11:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: design evidence-bound policy compilation to DMN and BPMN (#87)\n\n* docs: plan policy graph compilation to DMN and BPMN\n\n* docs: fix plan filename typo, ground claims in exact figures, relocate\n\nAddresses review feedback and tightens every repository-derived claim in\nthe DMN/BPMN redesign plan:\n\n- Rename the file from polict-to-dmn-bpmn.md to policy-to-dmn-bpmn.md and\n  drop the line that justified the misspelling as \"the requested name\".\n- Move the plan to docs/research/ so the repository root keeps matching\n  docs/STRUCTURE.md, and turn the eleven implementation-surface paths into\n  verified relative links.\n- Record that nothing under apps/ changed between the reviewed baseline\n  5179de7 and the current tip of main, so the observations still hold.\n- Replace \"600+ prerequisite edges and dozens of ...\" with the recomputed\n  distribution: prerequisite 603, conditional 249, complementary 179,\n  override 110, sequential 95, validation 80, contradictory 14.\n- Quantify the provenance finding: 247 of 1,582 span records carry\n  reference_verified true with a text_match_score below 0.6, lowest 0.008.\n- Cite the exact prompt instructions being replaced — the \"Add 5-10\n  attributes per entity (use domain knowledge)\" quota, the\n  exactly-one-of-ten rule_type classification, and the batch-number rule\n  ID scheme.\n- Name the concrete domain-prompt drift: the AML overlay asks for\n  conditions as an array and consequences as an object while the base and\n  the other three overlays ask for strings.\n- Name the sampling that must not feed executable edges: cross-batch\n  dependency analysis takes min(20, batch_size // 4) rules from the head\n  of each batch.\n- Pin the standards with document numbers: DMN 1.5 formal/24-01-01 with\n  DMN 1.6/1.7 identified as the beta revisions to avoid, and BPMN 2.0.2\n  formal/13-12-09 with its five normative XSDs.\n- Fence the ten indented code blocks to match the repository''s Markdown\n  style.\n\nThe docs/research/ entry in docs/STRUCTURE.md is added by #86; this PR\nleaves that file untouched so the two branches do not conflict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aff7a0fcbb6f544bd43acda5a1627808a2774af9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/aff7a0fcbb6f544bd43acda5a1627808a2774af9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/1b063fbc6013e5ab3335fab20349b337d6a4f161","verification":{"payload":"tree aff7a0fcbb6f544bd43acda5a1627808a2774af9\nparent 62d2cc1e6105c3f60b85c447aae0a2d797f36402\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1787148700 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787148700 -0700\n\ndocs: design evidence-bound policy compilation to DMN and BPMN (#87)\n\n* docs: plan policy graph compilation to DMN and BPMN\n\n* docs: fix plan filename typo, ground claims in exact figures, relocate\n\nAddresses review feedback and tightens every repository-derived claim in\nthe DMN/BPMN redesign plan:\n\n- Rename the file from polict-to-dmn-bpmn.md to policy-to-dmn-bpmn.md and\n  drop the line that justified the misspelling as \"the requested name\".\n- Move the plan to docs/research/ so the repository root keeps matching\n  docs/STRUCTURE.md, and turn the eleven implementation-surface paths into\n  verified relative links.\n- Record that nothing under apps/ changed between the reviewed baseline\n  5179de7 and the current tip of main, so the observations still hold.\n- Replace \"600+ prerequisite edges and dozens of ...\" with the recomputed\n  distribution: prerequisite 603, conditional 249, complementary 179,\n  override 110, sequential 95, validation 80, contradictory 14.\n- Quantify the provenance finding: 247 of 1,582 span records carry\n  reference_verified true with a text_match_score below 0.6, lowest 0.008.\n- Cite the exact prompt instructions being replaced — the \"Add 5-10\n  attributes per entity (use domain knowledge)\" quota, the\n  exactly-one-of-ten rule_type classification, and the batch-number rule\n  ID scheme.\n- Name the concrete domain-prompt drift: the AML overlay asks for\n  conditions as an array and consequences as an object while the base and\n  the other three overlays ask for strings.\n- Name the sampling that must not feed executable edges: cross-batch\n  dependency analysis takes min(20, batch_size // 4) rules from the head\n  of each batch.\n- Pin the standards with document numbers: DMN 1.5 formal/24-01-01 with\n  DMN 1.6/1.7 identified as the beta revisions to avoid, and BPMN 2.0.2\n  formal/13-12-09 with its five normative XSDs.\n- Fence the ten indented code blocks to match the repository''s Markdown\n  style.\n\nThe docs/research/ entry in docs/STRUCTURE.md is added by #86; this PR\nleaves that file untouched so the two branches do not conflict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhbmcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfNAQAJxUfH4irNPeC65Lhh8h3A7W\nmdEY2aU+LDmf3k8km4LO9bHQaVoYNRHWpLfVsTL+mLUIcLfyPuVSjfgSRnfVQdP4\nBmYPzsjA4A0kRi1g2dBB7vAw6+SDwePS/mIQYvNWt1