ithub.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/18fc312330c4471f250bc4a30ed84b25e8c0e39b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-30T01:58:39Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-30T01:58:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"data: bundle the real dataset so a fresh clone runs with populated graphs (#25)\n\nPer request: ship the actual compliance dataset and pipeline results in-repo so\nanyone who clones and runs `./start.sh` gets real, populated knowledge graphs\nout of the box — no pipeline run required. (Private repo; the data includes\nreal brand/regulatory names by design.)\n\n- Un-ignore and commit apps/explorer/kgs/ (the graphs loaded into JanusGraph on\n  first `setup`), apps/explorer/kbs/ (source-doc chunks backing reference\n  links), apps/pipeline/compliance-files/ (raw inputs), and\n  apps/pipeline/pipeline-output/ (pipeline artifacts). Runtime-only logs and the\n  UI run DB stay ignored.\n- Commit the graph manifest + generated JanusGraph configs (conf/graphs.yaml,\n  gremlin-server.yaml, init-graphs.groovy, janusgraph-*.properties) that\n  register these graphs.\n- Drop the debranding guard tests (test_debranding_scan.py and\n  test_graph_manifest''s brand-name check), which intentionally forbade exactly\n  this content; keeping them would fail CI now that real names are bundled.\n\nThe \"graph DB\" itself is not committed — JanusGraph/Cassandra storage is rebuilt\nfrom the committed kgs/*.json by load_all_graphs() on startup.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"597dc1ecc6bf0c804eac7cf1ec5039c88ccf2b2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/597dc1ecc6bf0c804eac7cf1ec5039c88ccf2b2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/18fc312330c4471f250bc4a30ed84b25e8c0e39b","verification":{"payload":"tree 597dc1ecc6bf0c804eac7cf1ec5039c88ccf2b2a\nparent 54474e1e9be93b73db095d21e557503b99d863a9\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1782784719 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782784719 -0700\n\ndata: bundle the real dataset so a fresh clone runs with populated graphs (#25)\n\nPer request: ship the actual compliance dataset and pipeline results in-repo so\nanyone who clones and runs `./start.sh` gets real, populated knowledge graphs\nout of the box — no pipeline run required. (Private repo; the data includes\nreal brand/regulatory names by design.)\n\n- Un-ignore and commit apps/explorer/kgs/ (the graphs loaded into JanusGraph on\n  first `setup`), apps/explorer/kbs/ (source-doc chunks backing reference\n  links), apps/pipeline/compliance-files/ (raw inputs), and\n  apps/pipeline/pipeline-output/ (pipeline artifacts). Runtime-only logs and the\n  UI run DB stay ignored.\n- Commit the graph manifest + generated JanusGraph configs (conf/graphs.yaml,\n  gremlin-server.yaml, init-graphs.groovy, janusgraph-*.properties) that\n  register these graphs.\n- Drop the debranding guard tests (test_debranding_scan.py and\n  test_graph_manifest''s brand-name check), which intentionally forbade exactly\n  this content; keeping them would fail CI now that real names are bundled.\n\nThe \"graph DB\" itself is not committed — JanusGraph/Cassandra storage is rebuilt\nfrom the committed kgs/*.json by load_all_graphs() on startup.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQyLPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz6gQAGyfKKt51fieFIHSv4n/MH48\n5tS76uMlsM9MVYu6wXfk8HvzmVfbio8SGsOt5ipDgOGT6fPMUrlBM9KmhhlAfmVC\nE/w+o0dceNXUaMoy86zUJk5QAsJH3I7f6yeTpQi2GfgLtBgQt/tf1XWwe3iiqBNd\nAAMO4vSP2Ih5HF9exA8242K0yFg5t0qYI15Ob5boxLTsKw7VNJq/5q8VYhNoupUU\nAZWglJiNQJQQQpwxQ7b9REKa/BlmE2nDq42pLvrmJDmA+a1GpJu2/g8onFp5fqal\nPOkYwq/amgWqSRPsKVoopqhGz87JqKCbiIN/KG4E8CFgEwNLgogv956hJKB8BpDr\ne7UyWKRBa9baWDZAYbOgfbhadFxIalUatEPFQpuWGwx4WajPRQHi6bfhngM/Yuw1\nPvdxmpfWK61rmOYpM9NV+R46znvU14ObonD8dQjme9C2ihnPLIZVERKipGPx2xWC\nXqcdp5BmBjyqYF9asQsFv/D5sEDhMwD5+pBu5xNJHExFcIMvTnlHKgQdF0Cj/New\nZANKtRm/0Cq41IB3wf/dW9mF8jIJYao5wigWPlJqZKYIN4KdJ3qGDGA8L/BF7LoB\n08knHpl7p3rTowJeVODsOcn1HgxTzOYv/ohRWGr6f+fQgi3iXYX6KQiDrslWzkcE\na7aXEphJ/OEJXyYXmAuq\n=4xT5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-30T01:58:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"htt