ithub.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/0903368d813ca81e4dc1ed817b14d2fe5f9bc7f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-30T00:44:12Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-30T00:44:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: validate and polish all documentation against the code (#21)\n\n* docs: validate and polish all documentation against the code\n\nA rigorous validation + polish pass over every doc, verifying each factual\nclaim against the actual code (agent files, CLI argparse, config, manifest,\nbackend routers, Dockerfiles, start/stop scripts, CI). Fixes real drift and a\nbrand-name leak; no behavior changes.\n\nSite / top-level:\n- docs/index.html: remove a \"CORTEX\" backronym (brand leak); replace fabricated\n  stats with verifiable facts; correct the rule_type taxonomy to the real 10\n  types; fix chat tool count (13); drop a broken \"Screenshots\" nav anchor.\n- .github/SECURITY.md: the app uses SQLite (not PostgreSQL) and calls OpenAI.\n\nPipeline docs:\n- agents/README.md: Agent 4 class KnowledgeEnricher (not RulesEntitiesMerger);\n  correct per-agent output filenames (drop nonexistent CSVs/JSONs); fix worker\n  counts and Agent 1 supported_formats.\n- PRODUCT_DEFINITION/SETUP/DOCKER/ARCHITECTURE: fix invalid flag (--file, not\n  --source-file), output path (pipeline-output/<doc>/, no openai/ subfolder),\n  agent_8 match types (IDENTICAL/EQUIVALENT/CONTRADICTORY/UNRELATED),\n  reasoning_effort=medium, supported formats, and compare-CLI examples.\n- prompts/README.md: clarify entity_resolution/rule_resolution usage.\n\nExplorer / tools docs:\n- explorer README: 6 graphs (not 2); data_loader uses traversal-source keys\n  (sample_guidelines_g); test ports/BASE_URL corrected.\n- explorer architecture.md: real schema (business_rule/entity_category +\n  depends_on/belongs_to_category/relates_to), confidence 0-100, the actual\n  single mixed index + k-NN index, and fetch().getReader() streaming (not\n  EventSource) with the real SSE event set.\n- explorer integration/e2e READMEs: correct URL_PREFIX/BASE_URL so requests\n  don''t 404; standardize the default test port.\n- tools/video/README.md: document the screenshot-capture scripts and generated\n  assets so a fresh checkout knows how to regenerate them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(explorer): reference only the shipped debranded example graphs\n\nThe validation pass listed all graphs from a local graphs.yaml, which included\nbrand-named entries (fannie/freddie). The committed manifest ships only\nsample_guidelines + example_policies; describe the multi-graph capability\ngenerically instead of enumerating private graphs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"acf0257aaa5bb6babfa749aaf22f31b60117a93c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/acf0257aaa5bb6babfa749aaf22f31b60117a93c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/0903368d813ca81e4dc1ed817b14d2fe5f9bc7f1","verification":{"payload":"tree acf0257aaa5bb6babfa749aaf22f31b60117a93c\nparent bb746a0fb5f216fe49c5d1e2ac4fa9f5cfbd6e6e\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1782780252 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782780252 -0700\n\ndocs: validate and polish all documentation against the code (#21)\n\n* docs: validate and polish all documentation against the code\n\nA rigorous validation + polish pass over every doc, verifying each factual\nclaim against the actual code (agent files, CLI argparse, config, manifest,\nbackend routers, Dockerfiles, start/stop scripts, CI). Fixes real drift and a\nbrand-name leak; no behavior changes.\n\nSite / top-level:\n- docs/index.html: remove a \"CORTEX\" backronym (brand leak); replace fabricated\n  stats with verifiable facts; correct the rule_type taxonomy to the real 10\n  types; fix chat tool count (13); drop a broken \"Screenshots\" nav anchor.\n- .github/SECURITY.md: the app uses SQLite (not PostgreSQL) and calls OpenAI.\n\nPipeline docs:\n- agents/README.md: Agent 4 class KnowledgeEnricher (not RulesEntitiesMerger);\n  correct per-agent output filenames (drop nonexistent CSVs/JSONs); fix worker\n  counts and Agent 1 supported_formats.\n- PRODUCT_DEFINITION/SETUP/DOCKER/ARCHITECTURE: fix invalid flag (--file, not\n  --source-file), output path (pipeline-output/<doc>/, no openai/ subfolder),\n  agent_8 match types (IDENTICAL/EQUIVALENT/CONTRADICTORY/UNRELATED),\n  reasoning_effort=medium, supported formats, and compare-CLI examples.\n- prompts/README.md: clarify entity_resolution/rule_resolution usage.\n\nExplorer / tools docs:\n- explorer README: 6 graphs (not 2); data_loader uses traversal-source keys\n  (sample_guidelines_g); test ports/BASE_URL corrected.\n- explorer architecture.md: real schema (business_rule/entity_category +\n  depends_on/belongs_to_category/relates_to), confidence 0-100, the actual\n  single mixed index + k-NN index, and fetch().getReader() streaming (not\n  EventSource) with the real SSE event set.\n- explorer integration/e2e READMEs: correct URL_PREFIX/BASE_URL so requests\n  don''t 404; standardize the default test port.\n- tools/video/README.md: document the screenshot-capture scripts and generated\n  assets so a fresh checkout knows how to regenerate them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(explorer): reference only the shipped debranded example graphs\n\nThe validation pass listed all graphs from a local graphs.yaml, which included\nbrand-named entries (fannie/freddie). The committed manifest ships only\nsample_guidelines + example_policies; describe the multi-graph capability\ngenerically instead of enumerating private graphs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQxFcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADMwQAHZeA89H8zT9kSC0TbSUYgmm\nZCHxF5ZW1kFlEbzrsTfC+BSJwGZQfleyiuonVroo5HFDVItz6stMOQQNFdK/+kQD\nxbTfQOdTk2P1vO+ddbredYkhtrch4uG/J8FSLeAMMYP66YLw3pXBHqX8fKjiCyai\np0IuXA9jKFNyV2WBUGvrjWI9n4ZsmbsNdXXgbAvOn1sTzkwtut2XYhkL9kYJhnkn\nA3nNI9V8yfQAcUJTwHOa9EywcVGpiGZX3JELIEEPGd3tAUwWCRPTYI0odkjseuJv\nA1247ltkp9A1OlRipMb9hucdaiO7eVppRqs29Y+9YkapA817kh/zmmqI20jq/m95\nPpbgdk0zZtdlt05qibT7LU9NXlK6f+R1+WPeQKDG/APK0vubvfrjR6S3hcfKOGF7\nAKuWAo8YWP2JNU8zZDByyr19zZReIJz1uLVRqshoOBZ6t2+t6kUEemdFr6cbquk2\na8XzhhMr7Eyoutcmx+dH/qH+vrOvIx5/D+R/NlELNQ5/3gbJIIzlF3HeUqzBqij7\n6KOuik1LDzziuu6Kf2cj+0jVNErErqDcP07LXuhfDEURsljCAqx14aFAe4uOCYHQ\n927qAHOc8d+J9YaoQcNNubBRibb7JnAd/1Wak4O6aEHD6VJbEJxfoDj7NL+SrT2t\njFbr52Mwqus+y4Sv+djZ\n=ZkIw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-30T00:44:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/0903368d813ca81e4dc1ed817b14d2fe5f9bc7f1","node_id":"C_kwDOTG-nuNoAKDA5MDMzNjhkODEzY2E4MWU0ZGMxZWQ4MTdiMTRkMmZlNWY5YmM3ZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/bb746a0fb5f216fe49c5d1e2ac4fa9f5cfbd6e6e","sha":"bb746a0fb5f216fe49c5d1e2ac4fa9f5cfbd6e6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/bb746a0fb5f216fe49c5d1e2ac4fa9f5cfbd6e6e"}],"sha":"0903368d813ca81e4dc1ed817b14d2fe5f9bc7f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/0903368d813ca81e4dc1ed817b14d2fe5f9bc7f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/bb746a0fb5f216fe49c5d1e2ac4fa9f5cfbd6e6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-30T00:43:53Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-30T00:43:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve 13 bugs found in deep code review (round 2) + regression tests (#20)\n\nA second deep review across all four surfaces (pipeline Python, pipeline UI,\nexplorer, suite shell). Each bug was trace-verified before fixing; each fix has\na regression test that fails without it. Disjoint from the prior review (#16).\n\nPipeline (Python):\n- publish.py: tarball added every nested doc twice (rglob + tarfile recursive\n  default) — pass recursive=False.\n- impact_analysis.py: basic-mode analysis ran the synchronous engine directly in\n  the async handler, blocking the event loop (and WS keepalives) — offload via\n  asyncio.to_thread.\n- agent_5: run-aborting KeyError on LLM dependency objects (raw dict subscripts\n  outside the try/except) + the per-dependency `confidence` field was silently\n  dropped on every parallel run — guard with .get()/skip and preserve confidence.\n- agent_8: batch verdicts were aligned to rule pairs by array position (ignoring\n  pair_id) and a short/truncated array discarded ALL verdicts as UNRELATED —\n  align by pair_id and preserve partial results.\n\nPipeline (UI):\n- ChatDrawer SSE: the final, non-newline-terminated line (which can carry the\n  terminal done/error event) was dropped on stream end — flush it via new tested\n  sse.ts helpers.\n\nExplorer:\n- chat tools get_vertex_details / find_related_rules defaulted graph_name to the\n  literal \"g\", which is not a real traversal source in multi-graph setups —\n  fall back to the default traversal source.\n- detail.js openReference referenced an undefined global `highlightTerms`,\n  throwing a ReferenceError (caught as \"Failed to resolve reference\") whenever a\n  source_text was present — drop the dead guard.\n- graph.js / create.js: server-controlled values (labels, rule_type, category,\n  dependency_type) interpolated raw into innerHTML — stored XSS; now escaped.\n- graph.js: vertex fetch did not URL-encode graph_name / id — encode both.\n- actions.js setReviewStatus pushed to data.reviewHistory without initializing\n  it — TypeError on annotations lacking the array; add the guard.\n\nSuite shell:\n- GraphComparison WebSocket onclose read a stale justFinished (always false),\n  tearing down the \"Comparison complete!\" transition and flashing an empty\n  state — track via a ref.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1a89680e353bd35565a23e0a6c37199703679e67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/1a89680e353bd35565a23e0a6c37199703679e67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/bb746a0fb5f216fe49c5d1e2ac4fa9f5cfbd6e6e","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a89680e353bd35565a23e0a6c37199703679e67\nparent 0560d183b8a4ac0c163c15d17046a23976c19c6d\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1782780233 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782780233 -0700\n\nfix: resolve 13 bugs found in deep code review (round 2) + regression tests (#20)\n\nA second deep review across all four surfaces (pipeline Python, pipeline UI,\nexplorer, suite shell). Each bug was trace-verified before fixing; each fix has\na regression test that fails without it. Disjoint from the prior review (#16).\n\nPipeline (Python):\n- publish.py: tarball added every nested doc twice (rglob + tarfile recursive\n  default) — pass recursive=False.\n- impact_analysis.py: basic-mode analysis ran the synchronous engine directly in\n  the async handler, blocking the event loop (and WS keepalives) — offload via\n  asyncio.to_thread.\n- agent_5: run-aborting KeyError on LLM dependency objects (raw dict subscripts\n  outside the try/except) + the per-dependency `confidence` field was silently\n  dropped on every parallel run — guard with .get()/skip and preserve confidence.\n- agent_8: batch verdicts were aligned to rule pairs by array position (ignoring\n  pair_id) and a short/truncated array discarded ALL verdicts as UNRELATED —\n  align by pair_id and preserve partial results.\n\nPipeline (UI):\n- ChatDrawer SSE: the final, non-newline-terminated line (which can carry the\n  terminal done/error event) was dropped on stream end — flush it via new tested\n  sse.ts helpers.\n\nExplorer:\n- chat tools get_vertex_details / find_related_rules defaulted graph_name to the\n  literal \"g\", which is not a real traversal source in multi-graph setups —\n  fall back to the default traversal source.\n- detail.js openReference referenced an undefined global `highlightTerms`,\n  throwing a ReferenceError (caught as \"Failed to resolve reference\") whenever a\n  source_text was present — drop the dead guard.\n- graph.js / create.js: server-controlled values (labels, rule_type, category,\n  dependency_type) interpolated raw into innerHTML — stored XSS; now escaped.\n- graph.js: vertex fetch did not URL-encode graph_name / id — encode both.\n- actions.js setReviewStatus pushed to data.reviewHistory without initializing\n  it — TypeError on annotations lacking the array; add the guard.\n\nSuite shell:\n- GraphComparison WebSocket onclose read a stale justFinished (always false),\n  tearing down the \"Comparison complete!\" transition and flashing an empty\n  state — track via a ref.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQxFJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApXEQAGGrADmtRab6PZiYjFlAVmyz\nSC82IAAMf5ttu3u+xuatgUphZh3Gh352MqJqAsIFI7tO3PrQBILnR2VFiV27JmH1\nAoPxOs7DZe5m6nFlWx/q6TqcHRY4yzSY7z6NAQNvsvjy2bUHpyMzBRoTjozxt01t\nda6Tgasu1zjBVyV7kLUUuLcK8uJvdFav3nXbsxoCwvIPXna0oBLvYvoewS1tvsyt\nhUJbslVOTpoKQSBm9KuIStXOiBzdeHZe1PFKRFUUIRgdLS8YvNfC2eAJriQH4n19\nDbct0f+rbHksv4gpjDZyAQUqYsA6QypgzTOabi2MSUMvC7a9Y3SQlseJSBDBZfSo\nsoGuEsgLmZK3iO49irb755bUeY5BGrH/ENQ55h0YW6pD7Lp8r1eAeHKKt9h58Pbs\nzf9FDUA0IELi1CG1HBYYUREvRrFuXDR/aWGsnrUixzC9502P7HA77Q901QZiitNw\nybm78YuwkEC1k8YsTa4B6s/WXEwH9gunXdrEJ1TPuWqtUkjRgNN3cg5ytSHmZr83\nArMxT5/y9oi+5HZARMS3WjddJwbdzaISGljpb0BGQdhAEKFFZ78BFvvn/nKUIw82\nIJvyr70TzSmYBrCrCa4tv0s5FxBHQ8WahJOTnKyL6JZEPFyc2/5AVydGmzmIIszt\nJ6VzFTkJd107FsWA79ws\n=uSQc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-30T00:43:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/bb746a0fb5f216fe49c5d1e2ac4fa9f5cfbd6e6e","node_id":"C_kwDOTG-nuNoAKGJiNzQ2YTBmYjVmMjE2ZmU0OWM1ZDFlMmFjNGZhOWY1Y2ZiZDZlNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/0560d183b8a4ac0c163c15d17046a23976c19c6d","sha":"0560d183b8a4ac0c163c15d17046a23976c19c6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/0560d183b8a4ac0c163c15d17046a23976c19c6d"}],"sha":"bb746a0fb5f216fe49c5d1e2ac4fa9f5cfbd6e6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/bb746a0fb5f216fe49c5d1e2ac4fa9f5cfbd6e6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/0560d183b8a4ac0c163c15d17046a23976c19c6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T23:03:13Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T23:03:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(explorer): route reference chunk link through the API resolver (#19)\n\nClicking a node''s source-document reference in the knowledge-graph explorer\ndid nothing when the explorer is embedded in the suite shell (or served\ncross-origin). openReference() opened the chunk via window.open(best.url),\nwhere best.url is a root-relative \"/app/api/reference/chunk?...\" path. Every\nfetch() in the UI is rewritten by a wrapper in state.js (prepend apiBaseUrl\ncross-origin, else the page''s url prefix), but window.open bypasses that\nwrapper — so the link resolved against the embedding page''s origin and 404''d.\nThe backend resolve + chunk endpoints were fine; only the click target was.\n\n- state.js: factor the fetch routing into a reusable resolveApiUrl() and have\n  the fetch wrapper delegate to it, so navigations that bypass fetch\n  (window.open, hrefs) can reuse identical routing. Exposed as window.resolveApiUrl.\n- detail.js: openReference now builds the chunk URL from the bare\n  /api/reference/chunk path + best.path and routes it through resolveApiUrl,\n  instead of window.open(best.url). Works standalone, embedded, and cross-origin.\n\nAdds source-level regression tests: resolve matches must carry `path`,\nstate.js must expose resolveApiUrl, and openReference must route via it\n(and never window.open(best.url) directly).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f30121f36bce6505628d7f8fdfe8d7a664605f21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/f30121f36bce6505628d7f8fdfe8d7a664605f21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/0560d183b8a4ac0c163c15d17046a23976c19c6d","verification":{"payload":"tree f30121f36bce6505628d7f8fdfe8d7a664605f21\nparent d7e481dee023b7255cf8d85289b998c7ca54f940\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1782774193 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782774193 -0700\n\nfix(explorer): route reference chunk link through the API resolver (#19)\n\nClicking a node''s source-document reference in the knowledge-graph explorer\ndid nothing when the explorer is embedded in the suite shell (or served\ncross-origin). openReference() opened the chunk via window.open(best.url),\nwhere best.url is a root-relative \"/app/api/reference/chunk?...\" path. Every\nfetch() in the UI is rewritten by a wrapper in state.js (prepend apiBaseUrl\ncross-origin, else the page''s url prefix), but window.open bypasses that\nwrapper — so the link resolved against the embedding page''s origin and 404''d.\nThe backend resolve + chunk endpoints were fine; only the click target was.\n\n- state.js: factor the fetch routing into a reusable resolveApiUrl() and have\n  the fetch wrapper delegate to it, so navigations that bypass fetch\n  (window.open, hrefs) can reuse identical routing. Exposed as window.resolveApiUrl.\n- detail.js: openReference now builds the chunk URL from the bare\n  /api/reference/chunk path + best.path and routes it through resolveApiUrl,\n  instead of window.open(best.url). Works standalone, embedded, and cross-origin.\n\nAdds source-level regression tests: resolve matches must carry `path`,\nstate.js must expose resolveApiUrl, and openReference must route via it\n(and never window.open(best.url) directly).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQvmxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsHEQAEEKk42uQRNqDo4m2Aa86JxB\nSABAizrJtzpu1nfIchmVflopvKUwFqaXALZlYiV9j+YRtTwtAo05gG0cImx/dySs\nco7An+l265sXNDMkYdUyxjxdOqJEVgj1cXvAQ2EMt1YVwfRWvGRL1IT59sYywp+A\n3jysKsBlcaWkZeHn2P7uy3BrcHMlmU3X+GE/fBtvT0hM7EoYPTpUcO/aNYMnmWn2\n7UfDU0GAS+GUJXRPj5obGNej2+2BRCXOZKHXxe3/EhBJROlwmfMkudmJ36RbKAhB\nSVY4QrKbn5VpSniPfyuEtbPukY/iy8WG+llF/frFb0yPzq8AbuoDbk7IGhP7B4Nt\nTFLgaT6Fpf5ziVrUb2wQXxj8LX1tQtbHWVjwunlZBl4garltcltyEIdBmTT+2BTO\nuJxUmb3nPIdUuGMBVtBycywAbPdxZOZ3yAvZdeHOGf1fEcbdTfnr9pzrJkeKwhIw\njmy0ahdABb3APcAjaxlB8roqtUGUY6UL6t/Tjv+k2aR0QS6w+gGG41hSotDEVEnv\nkPmN8HfXLzdY3PlxF9kny1j7IToXYlW9LjQ4J3+uHA27nEw5vjfwiUuttRrIoYbk\nYOljMzQPosAr5CxPaP53E7QNTUfJhc4sb7noNwFmxbPzjWDBfYg9B+1xO/K6Z5ej\nViWYoeklDSvrAZ5xH8z3\n=yrCE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T23:03:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/0560d183b8a4ac0c163c15d17046a23976c19c6d","node_id":"C_kwDOTG-nuNoAKDA1NjBkMTgzYjhhNGFjMGMxNjNjMTVkMTcwNDZhMjM5NzZjMTljNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/d7e481dee023b7255cf8d85289b998c7ca54f940","sha":"d7e481dee023b7255cf8d85289b998c7ca54f940","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/d7e481dee023b7255cf8d85289b998c7ca54f940"}],"sha":"0560d183b8a4ac0c163c15d17046a23976c19c6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/0560d183b8a4ac0c163c15d17046a23976c19c6d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/d7e481dee023b7255cf8d85289b998c7ca54f940/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T21:04:52Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T21:04:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(pipeline): bound every LLM call with a watchdog + TCP keep-alive (#18)\n\nThree extraction pipelines hung for hours, each blocked in a single OpenAI\nsocket read at Step 2. Stack samples showed the agent-2 workers parked in\n_ssl SSLSocket_read -> poll on a live-but-dead TLS connection to the OpenAI\nendpoint, while the parent extract.py blocked on `for line in process.stdout`.\nThe connections died silently when the machine slept; the SDK''s own 300s\ntimeout never fired on the stale socket, so the calls waited indefinitely.\n\nTwo layers of defense so this can''t recur:\n\n- TCP keep-alive on a custom httpx client (SO_KEEPALIVE + KEEPIDLE/INTVL/CNT):\n  the OS now probes idle connections and surfaces a dead peer within ~2 min,\n  so a read fails fast instead of parking forever. Best-effort — falls back\n  to the SDK default client if httpx/socket options are unavailable.\n- A hard wall-clock watchdog around every chat_completion: the call runs on a\n  daemon thread bounded by timeout x attempts + margin, guaranteeing control\n  returns in finite time regardless of socket state. A stranded thread is a\n  daemon (never blocks process exit) and keep-alive reaps its socket.\n\nAdds tests/test_llm_watchdog.py covering watchdog timeout, retry-aware\ndeadline, pass-through success, error propagation, and graceful keep-alive\nfallback.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"618b91fe5d1e20b5b566f9fe38421e80577f9b76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/618b91fe5d1e20b5b566f9fe38421e80577f9b76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/d7e481dee023b7255cf8d85289b998c7ca54f940","verification":{"payload":"tree 618b91fe5d1e20b5b566f9fe38421e80577f9b76\nparent 04f7e6472035262a4d823d8a30b6cca6dfd6daff\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1782767092 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782767092 -0700\n\nfix(pipeline): bound every LLM call with a watchdog + TCP keep-alive (#18)\n\nThree extraction pipelines hung for hours, each blocked in a single OpenAI\nsocket read at Step 2. Stack samples showed the agent-2 workers parked in\n_ssl SSLSocket_read -> poll on a live-but-dead TLS connection to the OpenAI\nendpoint, while the parent extract.py blocked on `for line in process.stdout`.\nThe connections died silently when the machine slept; the SDK''s own 300s\ntimeout never fired on the stale socket, so the calls waited indefinitely.\n\nTwo layers of defense so this can''t recur:\n\n- TCP keep-alive on a custom httpx client (SO_KEEPALIVE + KEEPIDLE/INTVL/CNT):\n  the OS now probes idle connections and surfaces a dead peer within ~2 min,\n  so a read fails fast instead of parking forever. Best-effort — falls back\n  to the SDK default client if httpx/socket options are unavailable.\n- A hard wall-clock watchdog around every chat_completion: the call runs on a\n  daemon thread bounded by timeout x attempts + margin, guaranteeing control\n  returns in finite time regardless of socket state. A stranded thread is a\n  daemon (never blocks process exit) and keep-alive reaps its socket.\n\nAdds tests/test_llm_watchdog.py covering watchdog timeout, retry-aware\ndeadline, pass-through success, error propagation, and graceful keep-alive\nfallback.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQt30CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjtMQAH/ZqY98DrbkziCSahSy0DAd\n7dmkh/2JAW/ITDh5dDxCn4zy9swct87OzXHl5VbkrP0qTiNHIQpiLWN8UJR2Hml0\npUruueoNq6ED/3ha0sWgli0EUawvMp5uZHBLaQOGF05Bt8sJzezYEvzKhSh0qBV4\n/ImTtowgzCGv9V07gAJuJV0GXN1rQa/CSDxtL3c7pmuaVubdo6O2JFXZN90PnFQz\nvm+1t1ZAXfvVkdlVS/V4wx33O3UKGdNM6MLChRpTmHPBG0NTjZM5QUYe2mVGgjrl\nr2IsZG6aYf4Ivf7u3fs2AX7oS+vT5GVCg/F0ccN5twRJfAvXXDMXdAelTpTWO4Vl\nj1wBdvqwd4wqmgEpETYjlwYm719huc5dQsEjOqDd66XGcMhxyNmFlmZ5bd+/CrzR\n79WnTKccxHm4tlzb7sSYSs39v38K3odsCFcgdfJ1YSAwQMjgNlOuOMnn5DUMJcE6\nAWyvtNLBur9zl1jvOeftJ9O9PjOzexWBaUl+hxhgp4/YIGYrWcHYGD+1JojUnLNf\naQ3QzkGSs3Xdw0Lghon1uutNFdZ+iAKG6+Q6geIWlK9MBA839RGuvBBqnt8LGjJU\nHBVaCRwVTGZ/4PpNvduemAvQIFf7I8gjX8C3bBGlUt8umg1CD1OGImK8YX3aiKaJ\n9XRncuu1iBMv1/Ht1ulc\n=G56m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T21:04:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/d7e481dee023b7255cf8d85289b998c7ca54f940","node_id":"C_kwDOTG-nuNoAKGQ3ZTQ4MWRlZTAyM2I3MjU1Y2Y4ZDg1Mjg5Yjk5OGM3Y2E1NGY5NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/04f7e6472035262a4d823d8a30b6cca6dfd6daff","sha":"04f7e6472035262a4d823d8a30b6cca6dfd6daff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/04f7e6472035262a4d823d8a30b6cca6dfd6daff"}],"sha":"d7e481dee023b7255cf8d85289b998c7ca54f940","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/d7e481dee023b7255cf8d85289b998c7ca54f940"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/04f7e6472035262a4d823d8a30b6cca6dfd6daff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T16:37:21Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T16:37:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui): render the KG-visualization logo; drop Assistant Runtime from Settings (#17)\n\nKG visualization HTML showed a broken \"Policy to Knowledge\" image: agents 6 & 10\nread logo.svg but always emitted `data:image/png;base64,...`, so the SVG bytes\ncouldn''t render. Fix the embed:\n- _get_logo_base64 now prefers logo.png, falls back to logo.svg, and declares\n  the correct MIME for the file found.\n- Bundle the brand logo.png in apps/pipeline/.\n- Guard the <img>: agent 6 omits it when no logo is bundled; agent 10 routes its\n  five logo tags through _logo_img_tag() — so an empty src never renders a broken\n  image (e.g. in a Docker image without the logo).\n- Regression test pins that the declared MIME matches the actual bytes.\n\nSettings: remove the \"Assistant Runtime · suite\" block (toggle, Runtime URL,\nReset suite defaults) from the shell Settings page; it now shows only the\nembedded pipeline configuration. Dropped the now-unused useSettings import.\n\nSuites: pipeline 835 passed; shell build clean + vitest 49 passed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be7d7d52d128964351d6e315445f93d7c8b8589e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/be7d7d52d128964351d6e315445f93d7c8b8589e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/04f7e6472035262a4d823d8a30b6cca6dfd6daff","verification":{"payload":"tree be7d7d52d128964351d6e315445f93d7c8b8589e\nparent b3e67965919289b5cb85758bd56d5823f85b2a71\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1782751041 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782751041 -0700\n\nfix(ui): render the KG-visualization logo; drop Assistant Runtime from Settings (#17)\n\nKG visualization HTML showed a broken \"Policy to Knowledge\" image: agents 6 & 10\nread logo.svg but always emitted `data:image/png;base64,...`, so the SVG bytes\ncouldn''t render. Fix the embed:\n- _get_logo_base64 now prefers logo.png, falls back to logo.svg, and declares\n  the correct MIME for the file found.\n- Bundle the brand logo.png in apps/pipeline/.\n- Guard the <img>: agent 6 omits it when no logo is bundled; agent 10 routes its\n  five logo tags through _logo_img_tag() — so an empty src never renders a broken\n  image (e.g. in a Docker image without the logo).\n- Regression test pins that the declared MIME matches the actual bytes.\n\nSettings: remove the \"Assistant Runtime · suite\" block (toggle, Runtime URL,\nReset suite defaults) from the shell Settings page; it now shows only the\nembedded pipeline configuration. Dropped the now-unused useSettings import.\n\nSuites: pipeline 835 passed; shell build clean + vitest 49 passed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQp9BCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ78QAKUJIXVST1TDbSSx/syJvdeB\nrn+jdT15sZjkyc7rLCwvpLoBJcV/L6fggot/7DPMZXxit9w0L5MZ0I+wF5QGqJuX\nU301K+2nltbaT2JWIsC4ZhNFWNxBU32OxUeK4UWhA2mEIEd3bhfv6OfcxKNEZmil\n50xFJ80uupcYPO+Kvsp+MLmavuvW2mx+WQBLj7QG+mAPfXPV0axjR3j6W2hI8LdY\nHLDmVGXN90tUCITLEjdH+UZQn2YGY4RtLoSRbZyKOyDUs0ZuMGG+yXf3E6Q60WNh\n3Dx4kvF0NgeoKBtB0SMOw04o/rAhni2Y/2Dtwwjkwkk85gCtsnadrsKLmPQj+Zzl\nXYyPi7/9Uxt6xuXvAchtVe0iCqKDhOW5HgZVRZiOc7yOtcFetD94KWz41x9pKc5f\n/LkbJjrlqONUCJZ9s4cHZghuFcJpx+XOOtvALGv0455ls2T0eIVx37ZM/gR1tZZk\nVglgOFkLraf9Hqryu6NwRCJsBePkRizpZ3Zb/H8E57E5rg/w6Y+PGlxdWvs5Rwhe\nhTcyr79y8sR2XsDXbHD1HHVaSk/Csfq3aoScxPQlbXJcdVSHyhHqT/qCYmOajPm+\nsYBGhjayJM/EyAuzcHsoJdgl/qhANcZ68h2r2UClGYmnKr8FAMABfWlYIPDiFAz7\n15BE84xqieo6jdHxusOR\n=DUqJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T16:37:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/04f7e6472035262a4d823d8a30b6cca6dfd6daff","node_id":"C_kwDOTG-nuNoAKDA0ZjdlNjQ3MjAzNTI2MmE0ZDgyM2Q4YTMwYjZjY2E2ZGZkNmRhZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/b3e67965919289b5cb85758bd56d5823f85b2a71","sha":"b3e67965919289b5cb85758bd56d5823f85b2a71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/b3e67965919289b5cb85758bd56d5823f85b2a71"}],"sha":"04f7e6472035262a4d823d8a30b6cca6dfd6daff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/04f7e6472035262a4d823d8a30b6cca6dfd6daff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/b3e67965919289b5cb85758bd56d5823f85b2a71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T15:08:35Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T15:08:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve bugs found in deep code review (+ regression tests) (#16)\n\nReviewed the codebase across pipeline core, FastAPI backend, explorer, and the\nReact frontends. Fixed 18 confirmed bugs, each with a regression test.\n\nPipeline core (agents/utils):\n- agent_8 read the API key at the wrong path (get(''openai_api_key'') → None);\n  use get_openai_api_key() so config.json keys work without an env var.\n- agents 6 & 10 embedded JSON in inline <script> without escaping; add\n  safe_json_for_html() (escapes <) so rule text containing </script> can''t break\n  the generated HTML.\n- agent_10 generate_summary_html hard-indexed all 5 set-ops → KeyError on a\n  partial/interrupted run; use .get() with safe defaults.\n- agent_2 raised an opaque crash when n_iterations <= 0; validate up front.\n- agent_1 standalone --files run wrote output to a folder named \"--files\";\n  resolve the positional output dir safely.\n\nBackend (ui/backend):\n- Dead concurrency guard: _conflicting_running_run read run[\"run_type\"] but the\n  column is \"type\" → guard never fired; two runs could race on the same output.\n- Path traversal: graphs/compare routers passed `name`/`operation` unvalidated\n  into pipeline-output paths (incl. shutil.rmtree); add containment checks → 400.\n- impact_store/obligation_store ignored PIPELINE_DATA_DIR (hardcoded path) while\n  run_store honored it → split DBs; unify on the env-aware path.\n- _advance_step matched \"Step 3\" inside \"Step 3.5\"; match a delimited token.\n- _kill_pid returned after SIGTERM so SIGKILL never escalated; poll then KILL.\n- WebSocket broadcast recreated removed subscriber keys (defaultdict leak); guard.\n\nExplorer (src/server.py):\n- _run_consistency_checks + force_reset/rebuild-embeddings called _engine.* with\n  no None guard → crashed/500''d when semantic search is unavailable; degrade.\n- JSON publish read pipeline-output/<provider>/<source_name> from unsanitized\n  input (path traversal); validate + contain under pipeline-output.\n\nFrontends:\n- Shell export links hardcoded /api/... (broke under a non-root base path);\n  route through apiUrl().\n- MicroFrame \"Retry\" called contentWindow.location.reload() → SecurityError on\n  cross-origin frames, stuck spinner; reload via src + re-arm watchdog.\n- Pipeline ErrorBoundary reset didn''t remount the subtree (Try-again no-op);\n  bump a resetKey like the shell boundary.\n- api.ts called res.json() on 204/empty bodies; return null for no-content.\n\nSuites: pipeline 832, explorer 114 (+2 skipped), shell 49, pipeline-UI 24 — all\ngreen; both frontend builds clean; debranding scan passes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c3c1c253bd9b57dfde4cb4945e0ceaf983f24426","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/trees/c3c1c253bd9b57dfde4cb4945e0ceaf983f24426"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/git/commits/b3e67965919289b5cb85758bd56d5823f85b2a71","verification":{"payload":"tree c3c1c253bd9b57dfde4cb4945e0ceaf983f24426\nparent 32d5e43892b126733ad2655aaf5a53e8ac8075a3\nauthor Reza Rahimi <145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com> 1782745715 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782745715 -0700\n\nfix: resolve bugs found in deep code review (+ regression tests) (#16)\n\nReviewed the codebase across pipeline core, FastAPI backend, explorer, and the\nReact frontends. Fixed 18 confirmed bugs, each with a regression test.\n\nPipeline core (agents/utils):\n- agent_8 read the API key at the wrong path (get(''openai_api_key'') → None);\n  use get_openai_api_key() so config.json keys work without an env var.\n- agents 6 & 10 embedded JSON in inline <script> without escaping; add\n  safe_json_for_html() (escapes <) so rule text containing </script> can''t break\n  the generated HTML.\n- agent_10 generate_summary_html hard-indexed all 5 set-ops → KeyError on a\n  partial/interrupted run; use .get() with safe defaults.\n- agent_2 raised an opaque crash when n_iterations <= 0; validate up front.\n- agent_1 standalone --files run wrote output to a folder named \"--files\";\n  resolve the positional output dir safely.\n\nBackend (ui/backend):\n- Dead concurrency guard: _conflicting_running_run read run[\"run_type\"] but the\n  column is \"type\" → guard never fired; two runs could race on the same output.\n- Path traversal: graphs/compare routers passed `name`/`operation` unvalidated\n  into pipeline-output paths (incl. shutil.rmtree); add containment checks → 400.\n- impact_store/obligation_store ignored PIPELINE_DATA_DIR (hardcoded path) while\n  run_store honored it → split DBs; unify on the env-aware path.\n- _advance_step matched \"Step 3\" inside \"Step 3.5\"; match a delimited token.\n- _kill_pid returned after SIGTERM so SIGKILL never escalated; poll then KILL.\n- WebSocket broadcast recreated removed subscriber keys (defaultdict leak); guard.\n\nExplorer (src/server.py):\n- _run_consistency_checks + force_reset/rebuild-embeddings called _engine.* with\n  no None guard → crashed/500''d when semantic search is unavailable; degrade.\n- JSON publish read pipeline-output/<provider>/<source_name> from unsanitized\n  input (path traversal); validate + contain under pipeline-output.\n\nFrontends:\n- Shell export links hardcoded /api/... (broke under a non-root base path);\n  route through apiUrl().\n- MicroFrame \"Retry\" called contentWindow.location.reload() → SecurityError on\n  cross-origin frames, stuck spinner; reload via src + re-arm watchdog.\n- Pipeline ErrorBoundary reset didn''t remount the subtree (Try-again no-op);\n  bump a resetKey like the shell boundary.\n- api.ts called res.json() on 204/empty bodies; return null for no-content.\n\nSuites: pipeline 832, explorer 114 (+2 skipped), shell 49, pipeline-UI 24 — all\ngreen; both frontend builds clean; debranding scan passes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQopzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwkQQAFsZZEVzwpY2yG3l8+LgVWwI\n3bX99hwDuti3hhMc4ZIrClb8NN+bgwNYPSsP2ynWApYEzwfgFBStAqQAut29gN1y\n0BpgK/rGmqiiAe8tz64m69xCUFqeZELpxux1IQMYgDMy7tsaopnxdRwzF/eK5q7F\nwNzQc07S/WjRW8bhjpMiUoe/bjdri9wN58LnpONg4h0yHJcftp4N8HFCD1GQph6J\nHtSrJ34ulkSDOrlIZ7TKci153i6dAwRqL7JvXjQUeHW15tRiNCUMjHoH/kSHA9jr\n3BAv5M/D0PSBDvwF4HbPdgQLHUzttMfdR166x3Rxfum9BWvGcuwzsLUPf4iixGsh\nFGJ38JZhgApR/lSZJBOqABuucWhSi/HBDyp5IvvgKQh2tSke+JKCj3FMHLWvh/c8\nrjeO9IYMsIAKvfO0lg/r5hThD9HcfW2Ki26GihhZbTUfOMwGPeBgk4dMXLaZAUnw\nF/TSV0SeHHBCiSDVHOmS7lvBk5Yn3lKMYdyS7g0Z5aoy2Wyoo6hqX2FSf1GsuyYK\nhIbjE1SVLQ7sprj7RaOL0M7YFRqxfrY9N9NZsqRkmUE1/yitiylUVQCPCwkBCOlE\nu2RzRTZtD3QUCCCsRtsvY4Pj5d0k5bpguI+zW9Q/2XUyrOLMx26QR0JFYrRYZaTJ\nPPR0aP8MznGtiBC+K7TV\n=qUnR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T15:08:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/b3e67965919289b5cb85758bd56d5823f85b2a71","node_id":"C_kwDOTG-nuNoAKGIzZTY3OTY1OTE5Mjg5YjVjYjg1NzU4YmQ1NmQ1ODIzZjg1YjJhNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commit/32d5e43892b126733ad2655aaf5a53e8ac8075a3","sha":"32d5e43892b126733ad2655aaf5a53e8ac8075a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/32d5e43892b126733ad2655aaf5a53e8ac8075a3"}],"sha":"b3e67965919289b5cb85758bd56d5823f85b2a71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/b3e67965919289b5cb85758bd56d5823f85b2a71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145064767?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rrahimi-uci","id":145064767,"login":"rrahimi-uci","node_id":"U_kgDOCKWDPw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrahimi-uci","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrahimi-uci/policy-to-knowledge/commits/32d5e43892b126733ad2655aaf5a53e8ac8075a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T14:30:58Z","email":"145064767+rrahimi-uci@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Reza Rahimi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T14:30:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"revert(settings): restore the clean reference Settings layout (#15)\n\nMatch the reference (Cortex Suite) Settings design. PR #12 had added extra\nfields — a Models subsection (optimizer/embeddings), an LLM Defaults section,\nbatch sizes in Parallelism, and an Optimizer Model picker — which cluttered the\npage versus the intended layout.\n\nRestore the original two-tab layout:\n- LLM Providers → OpenAI: API Key, Reasoning Model, Reasoning Effort, Timeout, Max Retries\n- Pipeline: Parallelism Defaults · Document Organization · Entity Extraction ·\n  Rules Extraction · Optimizer\n\nModel / reasoning / chunk-size / worker / temperature configuration all remain\navailable (and the shell now embeds this page, so it''s reachable from the suite).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"caa5513d3669a72506fcdeeb33ec4d1197b22b11","url":"https://api.github.