low/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/f34b7acf31e8ede56a9614e71baec705c6e0119b","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKGYzNGI3YWNmMzFlOGVkZTU2YTk2MTRlNzFiYWVjNzA1YzZlMDExOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/891f37a18d8ded39887d81f67e50de3cf7260849","sha":"891f37a18d8ded39887d81f67e50de3cf7260849","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/891f37a18d8ded39887d81f67e50de3cf7260849"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/e75d6e13c2a6f3a4db8fd478b19c3a1474954a2d","sha":"e75d6e13c2a6f3a4db8fd478b19c3a1474954a2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/e75d6e13c2a6f3a4db8fd478b19c3a1474954a2d"}],"sha":"f34b7acf31e8ede56a9614e71baec705c6e0119b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/f34b7acf31e8ede56a9614e71baec705c6e0119b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/e75d6e13c2a6f3a4db8fd478b19c3a1474954a2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T04:15:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T04:15:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"qa(sim): M6 pass — draw playhead cursor under WebGL, clamp tick delta\n\nFresh QA pass over M6 (playhead + agents), verified in real Chromium.\n\nBug found and fixed: the playhead \"now\" cursor was invisible under the WebGL\n(\"Boost\") renderer — RenderContext carried playheadX and CanvasRenderer drew it,\nbut WebGLRenderer.buildSliceVertices only handled the hover crosshair. A consumer\nrunning the timeline on WebGL (reachable in the demo, which toggles both WebGL and\nAgents) saw no cursor while scrubbing still worked — an invisible-but-live\ncontrol. Fixed by emitting a cursor bar in the vertex buffer alongside the\ncrosshair (the Canvas2D triangle handle stays a documented backend difference).\n\nHardening: the rAF tick now clamps its frame delta to 100ms, so a backgrounded\ntab (rAF paused) doesn''t teleport the playhead by seconds on refocus — playback\nresumes where it left off.\n\n- buildSliceVertices regression asserts the playhead emits its own rect at x.\n- ARCHITECTURE.md M6 QA note updated with the finding + browser verification\n  (element-screenshot diff during WebGL playback; visual confirmation of agents).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLmhnK8iiQxUDknMS8uD22","tree":{"sha":"6ae49bf84d306c6773ab448926ffddef9faf9e7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/6ae49bf84d306c6773ab448926ffddef9faf9e7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/e75d6e13c2a6f3a4db8fd478b19c3a1474954a2d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ae49bf84d306c6773ab448926ffddef9faf9e7e\nparent 584381504e3b3e07d92d4f144f8e101c7dce76cb\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783311337 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783311337 +0000\n\nqa(sim): M6 pass — draw playhead cursor under WebGL, clamp tick delta\n\nFresh QA pass over M6 (playhead + agents), verified in real Chromium.\n\nBug found and fixed: the playhead \"now\" cursor was invisible under the WebGL\n(\"Boost\") renderer — RenderContext carried playheadX and CanvasRenderer drew it,\nbut WebGLRenderer.buildSliceVertices only handled the hover crosshair. A consumer\nrunning the timeline on WebGL (reachable in the demo, which toggles both WebGL and\nAgents) saw no cursor while scrubbing still worked — an invisible-but-live\ncontrol. Fixed by emitting a cursor bar in the vertex buffer alongside the\ncrosshair (the Canvas2D triangle handle stays a documented backend difference).\n\nHardening: the rAF tick now clamps its frame delta to 100ms, so a backgrounded\ntab (rAF paused) doesn''t teleport the playhead by seconds on refocus — playback\nresumes where it left off.\n\n- buildSliceVertices regression asserts the playhead emits its own rect at x.\n- ARCHITECTURE.md M6 QA note updated with the finding + browser verification\n  (element-screenshot diff during WebGL playback; visual confirmation of agents).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLmhnK8iiQxUDknMS8uD22\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJqAMrRi\ncpjNAzB4uaRMj9q/geyYeDzpdhp3RNAnBetPd6e9km2xE+6YaiWprs6hcvwwBjSHwFrZC9ZLZUZO\nIg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T04:15:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/e75d6e13c2a6f3a4db8fd478b19c3a1474954a2d","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKGU3NWQ2ZTEzYzJhNmYzYTRkYjhmZDQ3OGIxOWMzYTE0NzQ5NTRhMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/584381504e3b3e07d92d4f144f8e101c7dce76cb","sha":"584381504e3b3e07d92d4f144f8e101c7dce76cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/584381504e3b3e07d92d4f144f8e101c7dce76cb"}],"sha":"e75d6e13c2a6f3a4db8fd478b19c3a1474954a2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/e75d6e13c2a6f3a4db8fd478b19c3a1474954a2d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/584381504e3b3e07d92d4f144f8e101c7dce76cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T02:56:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T02:56:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(sim): M6 — playhead, SimulationAdapter, and agent layers\n\nAdd a shared playback clock and an optional moving-agents seam on the map,\nwithout changing anything for consumers who don''t use them.\n\n- Playhead runes class (state/playhead.svelte.ts) on the shared context,\n  created lazily via ensurePlayhead() so TimelineToolbar''s play/pause/speed\n  controls and the timeline \"now\" cursor stay hidden until a consumer exists.\n  Advanced by a single rAF loop (the map''s, else the timeline''s) — no second\n  loop, no heavy work in runes. Draggable cursor drawn on the timeline canvas;\n  bind:playhead on <Timeline>/<GeoMap>.\n- SimulationAdapter + AgentSnapshot (sim/SimulationAdapter.ts): an optional\n  capability alongside DataSource. getPositionsAt(timeMs, out?) must be pure in\n  time and is called once per frame from the tick with a reused out buffer.\n- Two render paths: canvas bulk (GeoCanvasRenderer culls+projects agents inline,\n  oriented per kind) by default; a DOM `agents` snippet path via cullAgents\n  (sim/agents.ts, pure + decimated for LOD) for rich low-count visuals.\n- A <GeoMap adapter> seeds a span-relative default speed (so week-long datasets\n  are visible) and looping; the toolbar speed selector scales that base.\n- Reference waypoint adapter lives in the demo route only (not an SDK export);\n  the demo gains Agents on/off + count controls and playback.\n- Tests: playhead advance/clamp/loop/scrub; cullAgents culling/decimation +\n  adapter-contract purity and out-reuse; ensurePlayhead idempotence; toolbar\n  controls gating + speed; timeline scrub drag; snippet-path visible-only render.\n- ARCHITECTURE.md M6 section + plan status updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLmhnK8iiQxUDknMS8uD22","tree":{"sha":"b8a0bd20cc6bd7f6ce8289ac4f1ba0bc6187eaef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/b8a0bd20cc6bd7f6ce8289ac4f1ba0bc6187eaef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/584381504e3b3e07d92d4f144f8e101c7dce76cb","verification":{"payload":"tree b8a0bd20cc6bd7f6ce8289ac4f1ba0bc6187eaef\nparent 891f37a18d8ded39887d81f67e50de3cf7260849\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783306575 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783306575 +0000\n\nfeat(sim): M6 — playhead, SimulationAdapter, and agent layers\n\nAdd a shared playback clock and an optional moving-agents seam on the map,\nwithout changing anything for consumers who don''t use them.\n\n- Playhead runes class (state/playhead.svelte.ts) on the shared context,\n  created lazily via ensurePlayhead() so TimelineToolbar''s play/pause/speed\n  controls and the timeline \"now\" cursor stay hidden until a consumer exists.\n  Advanced by a single rAF loop (the map''s, else the timeline''s) — no second\n  loop, no heavy work in runes. Draggable cursor drawn on the timeline canvas;\n  bind:playhead on <Timeline>/<GeoMap>.\n- SimulationAdapter + AgentSnapshot (sim/SimulationAdapter.ts): an optional\n  capability alongside DataSource. getPositionsAt(timeMs, out?) must be pure in\n  time and is called once per frame from the tick with a reused out buffer.\n- Two render paths: canvas bulk (GeoCanvasRenderer culls+projects agents inline,\n  oriented per kind) by default; a DOM `agents` snippet path via cullAgents\n  (sim/agents.ts, pure + decimated for LOD) for rich low-count visuals.\n- A <GeoMap adapter> seeds a span-relative default speed (so week-long datasets\n  are visible) and looping; the toolbar speed selector scales that base.\n- Reference waypoint adapter lives in the demo route only (not an SDK export);\n  the demo gains Agents on/off + count controls and playback.\n- Tests: playhead advance/clamp/loop/scrub; cullAgents culling/decimation +\n  adapter-contract purity and out-reuse; ensurePlayhead idempotence; toolbar\n  controls gating + speed; timeline scrub drag; snippet-path visible-only render.\n- ARCHITECTURE.md M6 section + plan status updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLmhnK8iiQxUDknMS8uD22\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOljKIQz\nbT2FJqQ4sVZbvRodjBRer7KioFuJjMDTeq09OPWHJnwCnjnuQe8ieonXIv5CdhxKjMrOXTK/RlqJ\nGQI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T02:56:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_ur