l":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/14ee3b231838e9c176c3963aef3520b12b56c602","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKDE0ZWUzYjIzMTgzOGU5YzE3NmMzOTYzYWVmMzUyMGIxMmI1NmM2MDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/4274a028fc82620f69aecf86f0ff0b0efad8d73a","sha":"4274a028fc82620f69aecf86f0ff0b0efad8d73a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/4274a028fc82620f69aecf86f0ff0b0efad8d73a"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/ccb7c0da7e86733424bb473cf384a9dba43470f3","sha":"ccb7c0da7e86733424bb473cf384a9dba43470f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/ccb7c0da7e86733424bb473cf384a9dba43470f3"}],"sha":"14ee3b231838e9c176c3963aef3520b12b56c602","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/14ee3b231838e9c176c3963aef3520b12b56c602"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/ccb7c0da7e86733424bb473cf384a9dba43470f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-04T15:43:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-04T15:43:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor(worker): split brush epoch channel, stamp metadata on cache hit\n\nApplies the three QA follow-ups from the M2 review:\n\n- Independent epoch channels: a bounds-filtered (brush) query now rides a\n  `query:brush` channel separate from the plain timeline `query`, so when\n  M4 wires up brushing the two streams won''t cancel each other. Channel is\n  derived from method + bounds presence on both sides (WorkerDataSource\n  keeps a distinct #brushEpoch counter; WorkerCore.channelOf mirrors it).\n- Cache-hit metadata: on an LRU hit, re-stamp the response''s bounds/range\n  with the current request''s values so the declared window matches what was\n  asked (cells/events are absolute; only metadata could lag a sub-cell pan).\n- Tighten WorkerCore.handle to a non-init `Handleable` request type and\n  drop the unreachable `init` case (the worker drain handles init directly).\n\nAdds a plain-vs-brush channel-independence test. Full suite (132) +\nsvelte-check green; Chromium worker smoke unchanged (50 queued pans → 48\nstale, newest always real).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwVCHc8wsonSA1wqWrKgrv","tree":{"sha":"d86ffe592d3e8e9806673dee3d28e742b74f07f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/d86ffe592d3e8e9806673dee3d28e742b74f07f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/ccb7c0da7e86733424bb473cf384a9dba43470f3","verification":{"payload":"tree d86ffe592d3e8e9806673dee3d28e742b74f07f9\nparent 719fa81c6475513009c0104974cbec325064af02\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783179812 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783179812 +0000\n\nrefactor(worker): split brush epoch channel, stamp metadata on cache hit\n\nApplies the three QA follow-ups from the M2 review:\n\n- Independent epoch channels: a bounds-filtered (brush) query now rides a\n  `query:brush` channel separate from the plain timeline `query`, so when\n  M4 wires up brushing the two streams won''t cancel each other. Channel is\n  derived from method + bounds presence on both sides (WorkerDataSource\n  keeps a distinct #brushEpoch counter; WorkerCore.channelOf mirrors it).\n- Cache-hit metadata: on an LRU hit, re-stamp the response''s bounds/range\n  with the current request''s values so the declared window matches what was\n  asked (cells/events are absolute; only metadata could lag a sub-cell pan).\n- Tighten WorkerCore.handle to a non-init `Handleable` request type and\n  drop the unreachable `init` case (the worker drain handles init directly).\n\nAdds a plain-vs-brush channel-independence test. Full suite (132) +\nsvelte-check green; Chromium worker smoke unchanged (50 queued pans → 48\nstale, newest always real).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwVCHc8wsonSA1wqWrKgrv\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLFFzkJ8\nLPPmXIXxCkh9HOIDDLBtu8bi7T521Khi5W6n4cEexAOtu4Osqr+qoOyywivL1p9SgScb8bkNOFlp\nVwg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-04T15:43:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/ccb7c0da7e86733424bb473cf384a9dba43470f3","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKGNjYjdjMGRhN2U4NjczMzQyNGJiNDczY2YzODRhOWRiYTQzNDcwZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/719fa81c6475513009c0104974cbec325064af02","sha":"719fa81c6475513009c0104974cbec325064af02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/719fa81c6475513009c0104974cbec325064af02"}],"sha":"ccb7c0da7e86733424bb473cf384a9dba43470f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/ccb7c0da7e86733424bb473cf384a9dba43470f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/719fa81c6475513009c0104974cbec325064af02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-04T15:29:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-04T15:29:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(worker): M2 — epoch cancellation + quantized LRU memoization\n\nAdds cooperative query cancellation and memoization to the aggregator\nworker, per SPATIAL_TEMPORAL_PLAN.md M2. Both mechanisms live in a new\n`WorkerCore` (data/workerCore.ts), factored out of aggregator.worker.ts\nso the logic is unit-testable on the main thread; the .worker.ts file is\nnow just postMessage plumbing plus the epoch-coalescing schedule.\n\n- Latest-wins epochs: WorkerDataSource stamps query/queryGeo with a\n  per-channel epoch; the worker records the highest observed per channel\n  and answers superseded requests with a `stale` response (new\n  WorkerResponse variant). The main thread resolves those with null,\n  which callers already drop via their queryId guard.\n- Deferred drain: onmessage does only the synchronous epoch observe, then\n  schedules a setTimeout(0) drain so a queued burst registers all its\n  epochs before any is handled — so only the newest computes.\n- Quantized LRU (data/lruCache.ts, 32 entries) for queryGeo and\n  bounds-filtered query, keyed on bounds snapped to the implied cell grid\n  and range snapped to a fixed time granularity, so sub-cell pans hit\n  cache. Unfiltered temporal query stays uncached (SummaryIndex is\n  already ~0.12ms). init() clears cache + epoch history.\n\nTests: workerCore.test.ts (epoch skipping, per-channel independence, LRU\nhit/miss/eviction, back-and-forth-pan hits, quantized-key stability) and\nlruCache.test.ts. Full suite + svelte-check green; verified on the real\nworker in Chromium (50 queued pans → 48 stale, newest always real).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwVCHc8wsonSA1wqWrKgrv","tree":{"sha":"98c421e4e9858deb564c4e043d956074994f9fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/98c421e4e9858deb564c4e043d956074994f9fcc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/719fa81c6475513009c0104974cbec325064af02","verification":{"payload":"tree 98c421e4e9858deb564c4e043d956074994f9fcc\nparent 4274a028fc82620f69aecf86f0ff0b0efad8d73a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783178994 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1783178994 +0000\n\nfeat(worker): M2 — epoch cancellation + quantized LRU memoization\n\nAdds cooperative query cancellation and memoization to the aggregator\nworker, per SPATIAL_TEMPORAL_PLAN.md M2. Both mechanisms live in a new\n`WorkerCore` (data/workerCore.ts), factored out of aggregator.worker.ts\nso the logic is unit-testable on the main thread; the .worker.ts file is\nnow just postMessage plumbing plus the epoch-coalescing schedule.\n\n- Latest-wins epochs: WorkerDataSource stamps query/queryGeo with a\n  per-channel epoch; the worker records the highest observed per channel\n  and answers superseded requests with a `stale` response (new\n  WorkerResponse variant). The main thread resolves those with null,\n  which callers already drop via their queryId guard.\n- Deferred drain: onmessage does only the synchronous epoch observe, then\n  schedules a setTimeout(0) drain so a queued burst registers all its\n  epochs before any is handled — so only the newest computes.\n- Quantized LRU (data/lruCache.ts, 32 entries) for queryGeo and\n  bounds-filtered query, keyed on bounds snapped to the implied cell grid\n  and range snapped to a fixed time granularity, so sub-cell pans hit\n  cache. Unfiltered temporal query stays uncached (SummaryIndex is\n  already ~0.12ms). init() clears cache + epoch history.\n\nTests: workerCore.test.ts (epoch skipping, per-channel independence, LRU\nhit/miss/eviction, back-and-forth-pan hits, quantized-key stability) and\nlruCache.test.ts. Full suite + svelte-check green; verified on the real\nworker in Chromium (50 queued pans → 48 stale, newest always real).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwVCHc8wsonSA1wqWrKgrv\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDcfPON0\nxtjCgriOWf+C/Xg2ke1F7FQwXJkHU9M9sc1ut4ZkBYbOt99ktPcGXV2aZTY1Sim0fXQtm8h03x5c\n/A4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-04T15:30:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/719fa81c6475513009c0104974cbec325064af02","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKDcxOWZhODFjNjQ3NTUxMzAwO