n":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/d72dbe5346034f87aacdf29cc87dc3ce236fb3c2","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKGQ3MmRiZTUzNDYwMzRmODdhYWNkZjI5Y2M4N2RjM2NlMjM2ZmIzYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/0d7a12a6807cbc63e2db196b34b52e45aa55c888","sha":"0d7a12a6807cbc63e2db196b34b52e45aa55c888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/0d7a12a6807cbc63e2db196b34b52e45aa55c888"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/615f98c46e6d152c77a67fb16da2a05b74ba1631","sha":"615f98c46e6d152c77a67fb16da2a05b74ba1631","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/615f98c46e6d152c77a67fb16da2a05b74ba1631"}],"sha":"d72dbe5346034f87aacdf29cc87dc3ce236fb3c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/d72dbe5346034f87aacdf29cc87dc3ce236fb3c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/615f98c46e6d152c77a67fb16da2a05b74ba1631/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T21:54:51Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T21:54:51Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Clear remaining QA items: idle DataTable, WebGL ping frames, renderer attach fallback\n\n- #6 DataTable recompute while collapsed. Adds an `active` prop; when false the\n  rows/truncated deriveds bail out before reading `context.slice`, so they don''t\n  subscribe to it and a collapsed table no longer recomputes on every query. The\n  demo binds it to the <details> open state.\n- #9 Wasted frames under WebGL. Renderers now advertise `animatesPing`\n  (CanvasRenderer true, WebGLRenderer false); the rAF loop only forces per-frame\n  redraws for a ping on a backend that animates it. resolvePing still expires the\n  ping either way.\n- #10 No fallback if attach throws. Timeline wraps renderer.attach in try/catch\n  and falls back to a CanvasRenderer (warning once) instead of erroring the whole\n  component, so a WebGL failure past isSupported() degrades gracefully. All\n  subsequent draw/resize/destroy use the active renderer.\n\nVerified: check 0/0, 92 tests (3 new: inactive DataTable, animatesPing flags,\nattach-fallback), build + publint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV","tree":{"sha":"f460893f9d521de6aa27787ee1d830ffd686e7c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/f460893f9d521de6aa27787ee1d830ffd686e7c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/615f98c46e6d152c77a67fb16da2a05b74ba1631","verification":{"payload":"tree f460893f9d521de6aa27787ee1d830ffd686e7c8\nparent c3c500b46b218d0f6cf7d19b7742f86f3f2e087c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782770091 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782770091 +0000\n\nClear remaining QA items: idle DataTable, WebGL ping frames, renderer attach fallback\n\n- #6 DataTable recompute while collapsed. Adds an `active` prop; when false the\n  rows/truncated deriveds bail out before reading `context.slice`, so they don''t\n  subscribe to it and a collapsed table no longer recomputes on every query. The\n  demo binds it to the <details> open state.\n- #9 Wasted frames under WebGL. Renderers now advertise `animatesPing`\n  (CanvasRenderer true, WebGLRenderer false); the rAF loop only forces per-frame\n  redraws for a ping on a backend that animates it. resolvePing still expires the\n  ping either way.\n- #10 No fallback if attach throws. Timeline wraps renderer.attach in try/catch\n  and falls back to a CanvasRenderer (warning once) instead of erroring the whole\n  component, so a WebGL failure past isSupported() degrades gracefully. All\n  subsequent draw/resize/destroy use the active renderer.\n\nVerified: check 0/0, 92 tests (3 new: inactive DataTable, animatesPing flags,\nattach-fallback), build + publint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAejetr7\n4ELD8h6pcqmXIMJwjFlVHA7RoxsecTZIza9r1ILak5w9Bdbqq5qYF5qPTTMjZoUs2X+aWzN0DC63\ndwM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T21:55:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/615f98c46e6d152c77a67fb16da2a05b74ba1631","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKDYxNWY5OGM0NmU2ZDE1MmM3N2E2N2ZiMTZkYTJhMDViNzRiYTE2MzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/c3c500b46b218d0f6cf7d19b7742f86f3f2e087c","sha":"c3c500b46b218d0f6cf7d19b7742f86f3f2e087c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/c3c500b46b218d0f6cf7d19b7742f86f3f2e087c"}],"sha":"615f98c46e6d152c77a67fb16da2a05b74ba1631","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/615f98c46e6d152c77a67fb16da2a05b74ba1631"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/c3c500b46b218d0f6cf7d19b7742f86f3f2e087c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T21:44:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T21:44:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"QA fixes: tooltip top-edge flip, theme-read throttling, debounced live region, WebGL crosshair theming\n\nClears the remaining QA findings:\n\n- #1 Tooltip clipped at the top. The tooltip flips below the cursor when near\n  the top edge (new --sg-tip-vert, mirroring the existing horizontal flip), so\n  it''s no longer cut off by the stage''s overflow:hidden.\n- #4 getComputedStyle per query. Theme colors are now read only on mount/resize\n  and on real theme changes (a MutationObserver on the document root watching\n  class/style) — not on every debounced query. No more style flushes mid-drag.\n- #5 aria-live flooding. The live-region summary is debounced ~400ms so\n  continuous pan/zoom announces once on settle instead of every frame.\n- #7 WebGL crosshair didn''t theme. getComputedStyle returns color-mix() tokens\n  unevaluated, and a fillStyle round-trip yields oklab() the WebGL parser can''t\n  read. New resolveCssColor samples a 1px canvas pixel (getImageData) to return\n  plain sRGB rgba(), which parseRgba handles — so the crosshair themes under\n  WebGL + shadcn. SSR/no-canvas: pass-through.\n\nVerified: check 0/0, 89 tests (2 new), build + publint clean, and a Chromium\nsmoke test — tooltip not clipped at y=6 (top), resolveCssColor yields\nrgba(255,0,0,0.6) for a color-mix token, WebGL renders with gl.getError() === 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV","tree":{"sha":"6cbd04de43a5e64e1661e80865af14743247af64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/6cbd04de43a5e64e1661e80865af14743247af64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/c3c500b46b218d0f6cf7d19b7742f86f3f2e087c","verification":{"payload":"tree 6cbd04de43a5e64e1661e80865af14743247af64\nparent 26fc8a089f2c76f72838018ee9bd5b717f21e8fb\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782769471 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782769471 +0000\n\nQA fixes: tooltip top-edge flip, theme-read throttling, debounced live region, WebGL crosshair theming\n\nClears the remaining QA findings:\n\n- #1 Tooltip clipped at the top. The tooltip flips below the cursor when near\n  the top edge (new --sg-tip-vert, mirroring the existing horizontal flip), so\n  it''s no longer cut off by the stage''s overflow:hidden.\n- #4 getComputedStyle per query. Theme colors are now read only on mount/resize\n  and on real theme changes (a MutationObserver on the document root watching\n  class/style) — not on every debounced query. No more style flushes mid-drag.\n- #5 aria-live flooding. The live-region summary is debounced ~400ms so\n  continuous pan/zoom announces once on settle instead of every frame.\n- #7 WebGL crosshair didn''t theme. getComputedStyle returns color-mix() tokens\n  unevaluated, and a fillStyle round-trip yields oklab() the WebGL parser can''t\n  read. New resolveCssColor samples a 1px canvas pixel (getImageData) to return\n  plain sRGB rgba(), which parseRgba handles — so the crosshair themes under\n  WebGL + shadcn. SSR/no-canvas: pass-through.\n\nVerified: check 0/0, 89 tests (2 new), build + publint clean, and a Chromium\nsmoke test — tooltip not clipped at y=6 (top), resolveCssColor yields\nrgba(255,0,0,0.6) for a color-mix token, WebGL renders with gl.getError() === 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHEaFDfW\n+V/gCFlrEjFbozd1uGowQU0ECpA3baF37evr8fMnA6Wd2I4OszffZSjd6vq8SmGaWiLwzDVf/WTB\nMgQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T21:44:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/c3c500b46b218d0f6cf7d19b7742f86f3f2e087c","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKGMzYzUwMGI0NmIyMThkMGY2Y2Y3ZDE5Yjc3NDJmODZmM2YyZTA4N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/26fc8a089f2c76f72838018ee9bd5b717f21e8fb","sha":"26fc8a089f2c76f72838018ee9bd5b717f21e8fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/26fc8a089f2c76f72838018ee9bd5b717f21e8fb"}],"sha":"c3c500b46b218d0f6cf7d19b7742f86f3f2e087c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/c3c500b46b218d0f6cf7d19b7742f86f3f2e087c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/26fc8a089f2c76f72838018ee9bd5b717f21e8fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T21:21:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T21:21:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Refactor TimelineContext (derived summary) and add component-level test coverage\n\nTimelineContext: keep it as the cohesive aggregate root for one timeline''s\nshared state, but stop letting components push presentation into it. `summary`\nis now a $derived computed from the shared data (slice + track count) via a pure\n`summarizeSlice`, instead of a string written by Timeline on every query. The\nclass doc states the intent (composes AnnotationStore; holds data, derives\npresentation).\n\nExtract component logic into pure, unit-testable modules:\n- src/lib/interaction/hitTest.ts — nearest event / bucket-cell under the cursor.\n- src/lib/interaction/viewportKeys.ts — the keyboard pan/zoom keymap.\nTimeline now delegates to these.\n\nFix a bindable-range bug surfaced while testing: when a consumer provided an\ninitial range, the observe effect returned before reading vp.range, so it never\ntracked it and the bound range went stale after the first interaction. It now\nreads vp.range up front every run; a one-time seed still lets a consumer''s\ninitial range (e.g. restored from a URL) win over the loaded extent.\n\nTest coverage (vitest): 87 tests across two layers —\n- node env: data layer, Viewport, TimelineContext (load, labelFor, derived\n  summary, destroy-mid-load), WebGL geometry, hitTest, viewportKeys.\n- jsdom (@testing-library/svelte, per-file env): DataTable, RangeSelector,\n  TimelineToolbar via a context Harness, and Timeline mounted with stubbed\n  ResizeObserver/rAF/canvas (labels, keyboard-driven pan, bindable-range seed).\nTest files never ship (tests/ outside src/lib; colocated *.test.* stripped from\ndist). check 0/0, build + publint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV","tree":{"sha":"11b7cc9d71812a920e95af99b11a5938fee9d8b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/11b7cc9d71812a920e95af99b11a5938fee9d8b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/26fc8a089f2c76f72838018ee9bd5b717f21e8fb","verification":{"payload":"tree 11b7cc9d71812a920e95af99b11a5938fee9d8b1\nparent 380841e7bbc009d997104b9a1576ccec8a6ef4f1\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782768114 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782768114 +0000\n\nRefactor TimelineContext (derived summary) and add component-level test coverage\n\nTimelineContext: keep it as the cohesive aggregate root for one timeline''s\nshared state, but stop letting components push presentation into it. `summary`\nis now a $derived computed from the shared data (slice + track count) via a pure\n`summarizeSlice`, instead of a string written by Timeline on every query. The\nclass doc states the intent (composes AnnotationStore; holds data, derives\npresentation).\n\nExtract component logic into pure, unit-testable modules:\n- src/lib/interaction/hitTest.ts — nearest event / bucket-cell under the cursor.\n- src/lib/interaction/viewportKeys.ts — the keyboard pan/zoom keymap.\nTimeline now delegates to these.\n\nFix a bindable-range bug surfaced while testing: when a consumer provided an\ninitial range, the observe effect returned before reading vp.range, so it never\ntracked it and the bound range went stale after the first interaction. It now\nreads vp.range up front every run; a one-time seed still lets a consumer''s\ninitial range (e.g. restored from a URL) win over the loaded extent.\n\nTest coverage (vitest): 87 tests across two layers —\n- node env: data layer, Viewport, TimelineContext (load, labelFor, derived\n  summary, destroy-mid-load), WebGL geometry, hitTest, viewportKeys.\n- jsdom (@testing-library/svelte, per-file env): DataTable, RangeSelector,\n  TimelineToolbar via a context Harness, and Timeline mounted with stubbed\n  ResizeObserver/rAF/canvas (labels, keyboard-driven pan, bindable-range seed).\nTest files never ship (tests/ outside src/lib; colocated *.test.* stripped from\ndist). check 0/0, build + publint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOIA86gq\nzCOs8DFBPlbmkSCTmQdiYVQ/GQ5JqCTYcxcv5i6aADRaQQW67VVeGxNNQlGHI7UCJxRjem15U6uF\nZA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T21:22:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/26fc8a089f2c76f72838018ee9bd5b717f21e8fb","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKDI2ZmM4YTA4OWYyYzc2ZjcyODM4MDE4ZWU5YmQ1YjcxN2YyMWU4ZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/380841e7bbc009d997104b9a1576ccec8a6ef4f1","sha":"380841e7bbc009d997104b9a1576ccec8a6ef4f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/380841e7bbc009d997104b9a1576ccec8a6ef4f1"}],"sha":"26fc8a089f2c76f72838018ee9bd5b717f21e8fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/26fc8a089f2c76f72838018ee9bd5b717f21e8fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/380841e7bbc009d997104b9a1576ccec8a6ef4f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T15:12:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T15:12:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add WebGLRenderer (Boost-style backend) for the pluggable Renderer interface\n\nA WebGL rendering backend alongside the default CanvasRenderer, completing the\nupgrade path the Renderer interface was designed for (cf. Highcharts'' Boost):\n\n- Batches every heatmap bucket / event marker (and the crosshair) into a single\n  TRIANGLES draw call with per-vertex colors; one shader program, DPR-aware via\n  a CSS-pixel resolution uniform. Shares the severity ramp (new severityRGB\n  helper) and focus dimming with the Canvas backend.\n- buildSliceVertices (the interleaved x,y,r,g,b,a builder) is pure and exported,\n  so it''s unit-tested without a GL context. parseRgba handles themed crosshair\n  colors; WebGLRenderer.isSupported() lets consumers feature-gate.\n- Handles context loss/restore and cleans up GL resources on destroy.\n- The animated Ping pulse stays Canvas2D-only by design; high-severity items\n  still read hot under WebGL via the color ramp.\n- Demo gains a \"WebGL (Boost)\" toggle (disabled where unsupported); Timeline\n  remounts on renderer change via {#key}.\n\nVerified: check 0/0, 56 tests (8 new), build + publint clean, and a Chromium\nsmoke test with SwiftShader — toggling WebGL yields a live WebGL context with\ngl.getError() === 0 (shaders compiled/linked, draw calls clean) and no errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV","tree":{"sha":"a226e3947b880cc4f967782753b386b025a197cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/a226e3947b880cc4f967782753b386b025a197cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/380841e7bbc009d997104b9a1576ccec8a6ef4f1","verification":{"payload":"tree a226e3947b880cc4f967782753b386b025a197cd\nparent 5ba9cebab090db81c915ca78e7229cca4508062b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782745961 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782745961 +0000\n\nAdd WebGLRenderer (Boost-style backend) for the pluggable Renderer interface\n\nA WebGL rendering backend alongside the default CanvasRenderer, completing the\nupgrade path the Renderer interface was designed for (cf. Highcharts'' Boost):\n\n- Batches every heatmap bucket / event marker (and the crosshair) into a single\n  TRIANGLES draw call with per-vertex colors; one shader program, DPR-aware via\n  a CSS-pixel resolution uniform. Shares the severity ramp (new severityRGB\n  helper) and focus dimming with the Canvas backend.\n- buildSliceVertices (the interleaved x,y,r,g,b,a builder) is pure and exported,\n  so it''s unit-tested without a GL context. parseRgba handles themed crosshair\n  colors; WebGLRenderer.isSupported() lets consumers feature-gate.\n- Handles context loss/restore and cleans up GL resources on destroy.\n- The animated Ping pulse stays Canvas2D-only by design; high-severity items\n  still read hot under WebGL via the color ramp.\n- Demo gains a \"WebGL (Boost)\" toggle (disabled where unsupported); Timeline\n  remounts on renderer change via {#key}.\n\nVerified: check 0/0, 56 tests (8 new), build + publint clean, and a Chromium\nsmoke test with SwiftShader — toggling WebGL yields a live WebGL context with\ngl.getError() === 0 (shaders compiled/linked, draw calls clean) and no errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB0L/F6R\nXDzH9ZsuQ7YJ6lAhVzLLe7SAUWazzGS+udGTINDhjM8wzkeXESEQ7c0m9r2BqCOTYUxkZysW1FPu\n5gI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T15:12:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/380841e7bbc009d997104b9a1576ccec8a6ef4f1","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKDM4MDg0MWU3YmJjMDA5ZDk5NzEwNGI5YTE1NzZjY2VjOGE2ZWY0ZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/5ba9cebab090db81c915ca78e7229cca4508062b","sha":"5ba9cebab090db81c915ca78e7229cca4508062b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/5ba9cebab090db81c915ca78e7229cca4508062b"}],"sha":"380841e7bbc009d997104b9a1576ccec8a6ef4f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/380841e7bbc009d997104b9a1576ccec8a6ef4f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/5ba9cebab090db81c915ca78e7229cca4508062b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T15:06:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T15:06:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make the kit themeable via --sg-* tokens, with an optional shadcn bridge\n\nPromote every hardcoded color in the components to a namespaced CSS custom\nproperty with an inline DeepCivic default (e.g. var(--sg-stage, #1e1a17)), so\nzero-config reproduces the current look and any token is overridable on an\nancestor — no global stylesheet to import.\n\n- Tokens span the stage (--sg-stage[-foreground|-muted], --sg-grid), accents\n  (--sg-primary[-hover|-foreground], --sg-ring, --sg-pin, --sg-danger), light\n  surfaces (--sg-surface[-foreground], --sg-border, --sg-muted-foreground),\n  panels (--sg-panel[-foreground|-border]), lens overlay, and the canvas-drawn\n  axis + crosshair.\n- Canvas chrome can''t read CSS, so Timeline resolves --sg-axis-text/-tick and\n  --sg-crosshair via getComputedStyle, cached and refreshed on mount/resize/\n  query (not per frame). Threaded through drawTimeAxis + RenderContext.\n- The severity heat ramp stays fixed (it encodes data, not brand).\n- Ship optional themes/shadcn.css mapping --sg-* onto shadcn semantic tokens;\n  lazy custom-property resolution means the single :root mapping tracks .dark\n  for free. Exported as ''sveltegraph/themes/shadcn.css''.\n\nVerified: check 0/0, 48 tests, build + publint clean (theme ships to\ndist/themes/), and a Chromium smoke test — default stage stays rgb(30,26,23),\noverriding --sg-stage/--sg-primary flows through to the canvas + buttons, no\nerrors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV","tree":{"sha":"af9a3d41db52abd272a16cb2c0bf809c1e56ebcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/af9a3d41db52abd272a16cb2c0bf809c1e56ebcf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/5ba9cebab090db81c915ca78e7229cca4508062b","verification":{"payload":"tree af9a3d41db52abd272a16cb2c0bf809c1e56ebcf\nparent da0db932b8600fb3ebe11535fa4d16fae23ffff0\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782745592 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782745592 +0000\n\nMake the kit themeable via --sg-* tokens, with an optional shadcn bridge\n\nPromote every hardcoded color in the components to a namespaced CSS custom\nproperty with an inline DeepCivic default (e.g. var(--sg-stage, #1e1a17)), so\nzero-config reproduces the current look and any token is overridable on an\nancestor — no global stylesheet to import.\n\n- Tokens span the stage (--sg-stage[-foreground|-muted], --sg-grid), accents\n  (--sg-primary[-hover|-foreground], --sg-ring, --sg-pin, --sg-danger), light\n  surfaces (--sg-surface[-foreground], --sg-border, --sg-muted-foreground),\n  panels (--sg-panel[-foreground|-border]), lens overlay, and the canvas-drawn\n  axis + crosshair.\n- Canvas chrome can''t read CSS, so Timeline resolves --sg-axis-text/-tick and\n  --sg-crosshair via getComputedStyle, cached and refreshed on mount/resize/\n  query (not per frame). Threaded through drawTimeAxis + RenderContext.\n- The severity heat ramp stays fixed (it encodes data, not brand).\n- Ship optional themes/shadcn.css mapping --sg-* onto shadcn semantic tokens;\n  lazy custom-property resolution means the single :root mapping tracks .dark\n  for free. Exported as ''sveltegraph/themes/shadcn.css''.\n\nVerified: check 0/0, 48 tests, build + publint clean (theme ships to\ndist/themes/), and a Chromium smoke test — default stage stays rgb(30,26,23),\noverriding --sg-stage/--sg-primary flows through to the canvas + buttons, no\nerrors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF+cc/wm\nCFFPn23THNKKg8nQtHJmUlKvZwcv3/4tSrnvKsp6u+rntJgj05dQ8z2b6SEMxWguNcHxuLemLjRO\nVwA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T15:12:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/5ba9cebab090db81c915ca78e7229cca4508062b","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKDViYTljZWJhYjA5MGRiODFjOTE1Y2E3OGU3MjI5Y2NhNDUwODA2MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/da0db932b8600fb3ebe11535fa4d16fae23ffff0","sha":"da0db932b8600fb3ebe11535fa4d16fae23ffff0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/da0db932b8600fb3ebe11535fa4d16fae23ffff0"}],"sha":"5ba9cebab090db81c915ca78e7229cca4508062b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/5ba9cebab090db81c915ca78e7229cca4508062b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/da0db932b8600fb3ebe11535fa4d16fae23ffff0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T13:48:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T13:48:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add Highcharts-inspired surfaces: crosshair/tooltip, range selector, a11y layer\n\nChecked svelteGraph against Highcharts Stock (the commercial reference for dense\ntime-series) and added the affordances it proves users expect, fitted to the\nLOD model:\n\n- Hover crosshair + tooltip. A pointer-tracked vertical guide (drawn via a new\n  RenderContext.crosshairX) and a DOM tooltip reporting the nearest event or\n  aggregated bucket. Hit-testing reuses the drawn slice; a `tooltip` snippet\n  customizes content.\n\n- RangeSelector component. Quick spans (1H/1D/1W/1M/All) plus optional datetime\n  inputs, driving Viewport.setRange through the shared context.\n\n- Accessibility layer (WCAG 2.1 AA), since the canvas is otherwise opaque to AT:\n  the timeline body is a focusable application widget with keyboard pan/zoom\n  (arrows, +/-, PageUp/Down, Home); an aria-live region announces the visible\n  slice (TimelineContext.summary); and a new DataTable component renders the\n  visible slice (TimelineContext.slice, kept as $state.raw) as a navigable table.\n\nDemo wires in the range selector and a \"view as data table\" disclosure. README\n+ ARCHITECTURE updated.\n\nVerified: check 0/0, 48 tests, build + publint clean, and a Chromium smoke test\n(canvas renders; worker pipeline populates 200 table rows; tooltip shows\n\"ACT Open Data … 26 events · max severity 0.90\"; live summary \"100000 events\ngrouped into 1240 cells across 40 tracks\"; keyboard + range clicks raise no\napplication errors).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV","tree":{"sha":"f736f62a00203d589a11034748acd82fe0f216af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/f736f62a00203d589a11034748acd82fe0f216af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/da0db932b8600fb3ebe11535fa4d16fae23ffff0","verification":{"payload":"tree f736f62a00203d589a11034748acd82fe0f216af\nparent 1e17bbc2c70d54a50e0e6e36d19cf2535ff3ddce\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782740902 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782740902 +0000\n\nAdd Highcharts-inspired surfaces: crosshair/tooltip, range selector, a11y layer\n\nChecked svelteGraph against Highcharts Stock (the commercial reference for dense\ntime-series) and added the affordances it proves users expect, fitted to the\nLOD model:\n\n- Hover crosshair + tooltip. A pointer-tracked vertical guide (drawn via a new\n  RenderContext.crosshairX) and a DOM tooltip reporting the nearest event or\n  aggregated bucket. Hit-testing reuses the drawn slice; a `tooltip` snippet\n  customizes content.\n\n- RangeSelector component. Quick spans (1H/1D/1W/1M/All) plus optional datetime\n  inputs, driving Viewport.setRange through the shared context.\n\n- Accessibility layer (WCAG 2.1 AA), since the canvas is otherwise opaque to AT:\n  the timeline body is a focusable application widget with keyboard pan/zoom\n  (arrows, +/-, PageUp/Down, Home); an aria-live region announces the visible\n  slice (TimelineContext.summary); and a new DataTable component renders the\n  visible slice (TimelineContext.slice, kept as $state.raw) as a navigable table.\n\nDemo wires in the range selector and a \"view as data table\" disclosure. README\n+ ARCHITECTURE updated.\n\nVerified: check 0/0, 48 tests, build + publint clean, and a Chromium smoke test\n(canvas renders; worker pipeline populates 200 table rows; tooltip shows\n\"ACT Open Data … 26 events · max severity 0.90\"; live summary \"100000 events\ngrouped into 1240 cells across 40 tracks\"; keyboard + range clicks raise no\napplication errors).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCDfK2BC\nvKEYpCsFcPstO8JkQakhuL+Xf/r+G/3NF0C9RuNjA50YI7pM5amd8oebzRnsIhK6xyGkbcKmUwwD\n4AQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T13:48:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/da0db932b8600fb3ebe11535fa4d16fae23ffff0","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKGRhMGRiOTMyYjg2MDBmYjNlYmUxMTUzNWZhNGQxNmZhZTIzZmZmZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/1e17bbc2c70d54a50e0e6e36d19cf2535ff3ddce","sha":"1e17bbc2c70d54a50e0e6e36d19cf2535ff3ddce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/1e17bbc2c70d54a50e0e6e36d19cf2535ff3ddce"}],"sha":"da0db932b8600fb3ebe11535fa4d16fae23ffff0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/da0db932b8600fb3ebe11535fa4d16fae23ffff0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/1e17bbc2c70d54a50e0e6e36d19cf2535ff3ddce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T08:03:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T08:03:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make dist publish-safe for an SDK future state\n\nSet the package up to ship as a standalone MIT npm package (same license\nfamily as Svelte) without publishing yet:\n\n- Add MIT LICENSE and npm metadata (author, repository, homepage, bugs,\n  keywords). Add a prepack script so publishing always rebuilds dist.\n- Fix the Web Worker default for packaged consumers. Vite''s\n  worker-import-meta-url plugin needs the new URL() literal to match the\n  on-disk source, so the source keeps `aggregator.worker.ts` (required for the\n  app/dev build) — but svelte-package emits `.js` without rewriting the string,\n  which would leave installed consumers resolving a `.ts` that isn''t in dist.\n  scripts/postpackage.mjs now rewrites the worker URL to `.js` in the packaged\n  file so the default worker path resolves the emitted file out of the box.\n- Strip colocated *.test.* artifacts from dist in the same step.\n- Document the packaging contract (and the worker-extension caveat) in\n  ARCHITECTURE.\n\nVerified: app build still bundles the worker, packaged dist references\naggregator.worker.js (which exists), 0 test files in dist, publint clean,\ncheck + 48 tests green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV","tree":{"sha":"f6efa07b10cfb15598f49b81a020d296ae555305","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/f6efa07b10cfb15598f49b81a020d296ae555305"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/1e17bbc2c70d54a50e0e6e36d19cf2535ff3ddce","verification":{"payload":"tree f6efa07b10cfb15598f49b81a020d296ae555305\nparent f193f44cb0dcfd1c5614a52b1ea2d02c694e64c0\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782720197 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782720197 +0000\n\nMake dist publish-safe for an SDK future state\n\nSet the package up to ship as a standalone MIT npm package (same license\nfamily as Svelte) without publishing yet:\n\n- Add MIT LICENSE and npm metadata (author, repository, homepage, bugs,\n  keywords). Add a prepack script so publishing always rebuilds dist.\n- Fix the Web Worker default for packaged consumers. Vite''s\n  worker-import-meta-url plugin needs the new URL() literal to match the\n  on-disk source, so the source keeps `aggregator.worker.ts` (required for the\n  app/dev build) — but svelte-package emits `.js` without rewriting the string,\n  which would leave installed consumers resolving a `.ts` that isn''t in dist.\n  scripts/postpackage.mjs now rewrites the worker URL to `.js` in the packaged\n  file so the default worker path resolves the emitted file out of the box.\n- Strip colocated *.test.* artifacts from dist in the same step.\n- Document the packaging contract (and the worker-extension caveat) in\n  ARCHITECTURE.\n\nVerified: app build still bundles the worker, packaged dist references\naggregator.worker.js (which exists), 0 test files in dist, publint clean,\ncheck + 48 tests green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDpY8e+w\nlaO+kEMfLaHcTOPlcXPzBeanYIGsDVcb9bDhGiIJuxJlKLHrARqbVQmiZvClrdGJqMHexLgjTIq9\ntAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T08:03:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/1e17bbc2c70d54a50e0e6e36d19cf2535ff3ddce","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKDFlMTdiYmMyYzcwZDU0YTUwZTBlNmUzNmQxOWNmMjUzNWZmM2RkY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/f193f44cb0dcfd1c5614a52b1ea2d02c694e64c0","sha":"f193f44cb0dcfd1c5614a52b1ea2d02c694e64c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/f193f44cb0dcfd1c5614a52b1ea2d02c694e64c0"}],"sha":"1e17bbc2c70d54a50e0e6e36d19cf2535ff3ddce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/1e17bbc2c70d54a50e0e6e36d19cf2535ff3ddce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/f193f44cb0dcfd1c5614a52b1ea2d02c694e64c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T07:29:43Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T07:29:43Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add Svelte 5 consumer-API enhancements: bindable state, snippets, labels, reduced motion\n\nBuild on the existing runes architecture with four practical, library-grade\nadditions:\n\n- Bindable Timeline state: bind:range, bind:selected, bind:focusedEntity\n  ($bindable), mirrored to the shared TimelineContext via guarded observe/\n  control effects (untracked + equality-checked so they never ping-pong).\n  External range writes go through a new Viewport.setRange that clamps to the\n  extent and minimum span. Enables URL deep-linking and timeline sync.\n\n- Snippet props on Timeline: `label` (custom entity-label content), `loading`,\n  and `empty`. Overlays sit over the stage so the canvas/ResizeObserver/rAF\n  wiring is never torn down; `empty` is driven by a UI-scale hasData flag set\n  when a query resolves, off the render hot path.\n\n- Entity label channel: optional DataSource.trackLabels() (in-memory + worker),\n  surfaced as TimelineContext.labelFor(id). The gutter now shows human labels\n  (falling back to the id) instead of raw ids.\n\n- Reduced-motion-aware Ping: a reactive prefersReducedMotion() singleton (one\n  matchMedia listener, no Svelte version bump) feeds a `reduced` flag into the\n  PingFrame; the renderer draws a steady highlight ring instead of an animated\n  pulse for users who prefer less motion.\n\nAlso fixes the documented demo smell (WorkerDataSource creation moved from\n$derived.by into $state + $effect) and showcases the loading/empty snippets.\nAdds tests for setRange, trackLabels, and the reduced-motion default; updates\nREADME and ARCHITECTURE. check + 48 tests + build all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV","tree":{"sha":"80cf596aff4812d351598011540110b2133bd661","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/80cf596aff4812d351598011540110b2133bd661"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/f193f44cb0dcfd1c5614a52b1ea2d02c694e64c0","verification":{"payload":"tree 80cf596aff4812d351598011540110b2133bd661\nparent e56ee073459474f644199a0561fedeb64f9901fe\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782718183 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782718183 +0000\n\nAdd Svelte 5 consumer-API enhancements: bindable state, snippets, labels, reduced motion\n\nBuild on the existing runes architecture with four practical, library-grade\nadditions:\n\n- Bindable Timeline state: bind:range, bind:selected, bind:focusedEntity\n  ($bindable), mirrored to the shared TimelineContext via guarded observe/\n  control effects (untracked + equality-checked so they never ping-pong).\n  External range writes go through a new Viewport.setRange that clamps to the\n  extent and minimum span. Enables URL deep-linking and timeline sync.\n\n- Snippet props on Timeline: `label` (custom entity-label content), `loading`,\n  and `empty`. Overlays sit over the stage so the canvas/ResizeObserver/rAF\n  wiring is never torn down; `empty` is driven by a UI-scale hasData flag set\n  when a query resolves, off the render hot path.\n\n- Entity label channel: optional DataSource.trackLabels() (in-memory + worker),\n  surfaced as TimelineContext.labelFor(id). The gutter now shows human labels\n  (falling back to the id) instead of raw ids.\n\n- Reduced-motion-aware Ping: a reactive prefersReducedMotion() singleton (one\n  matchMedia listener, no Svelte version bump) feeds a `reduced` flag into the\n  PingFrame; the renderer draws a steady highlight ring instead of an animated\n  pulse for users who prefer less motion.\n\nAlso fixes the documented demo smell (WorkerDataSource creation moved from\n$derived.by into $state + $effect) and showcases the loading/empty snippets.\nAdds tests for setRange, trackLabels, and the reduced-motion default; updates\nREADME and ARCHITECTURE. check + 48 tests + build all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN6Bkhmi\n5zLNeVPpe7Es0YXvW/Mt1BMWIugQfVUf8LiCIRj8lIxPK92Bt52ibCeQycubLxu3mOw+YrZqaE44\nbgE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T07:29:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/f193f44cb0dcfd1c5614a52b1ea2d02c694e64c0","node_id":"C_kwDOTHLAetoAKGYxOTNmNDRjYjBkY2ZkMWM1NjE0YTUyYjFlYTJkMDJjNjk0ZTY0YzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commit/e56ee073459474f644199a0561fedeb64f9901fe","sha":"e56ee073459474f644199a0561fedeb64f9901fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/e56ee073459474f644199a0561fedeb64f9901fe"}],"sha":"f193f44cb0dcfd1c5614a52b1ea2d02c694e64c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/f193f44cb0dcfd1c5614a52b1ea2d02c694e64c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/commits/e56ee073459474f644199a0561fedeb64f9901fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T06:46:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T06:46:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Remove KronoGraph references and apply DeepCivic branding to the demo\n\nDrop all references to the commercial KronoGraph product across the docs\n(README, ARCHITECTURE), package description, and source comments, replacing\nthem with neutral level-of-detail timeline language while preserving the\ntechnical meaning.\n\nRebrand the example/demo to DeepCivic''s visual identity:\n- Public Sans font, warm off-white (#f5f0e6) page background, warm-brown\n  (#7a6a5a) accents and dark warm ink (#1e1a17) for the canvas stage.\n- Align the kit''s default component palette (Timeline, Lens, toolbar,\n  annotation layer, time axis) to the DeepCivic tokens so the showcase\n  reads on-brand, with focus-visible outlines for keyboard users.\n- Add a DeepCivic wordmark to the demo header and relabel the synthetic\n  example entities with Australian open-government sources.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV","tree":{"sha":"197d7893fe1363283b548af670b2607b712ecbc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/trees/197d7893fe1363283b548af670b2607b712ecbc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/johntooth/svelte-spatial/git/commits/e56ee073459474f644199a0561fedeb64f9901fe","verification":{"payload":"tree 197d7893fe1363283b548af670b2607b712ecbc7\nparent 0d7a12a6807cbc63e2db196b34b52e45aa55c888\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782715601 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782715601 +0000\n\nRemove KronoGraph references and apply DeepCivic branding to the demo\n\nDrop all references to the commercial KronoGraph product across the docs\n(README, ARCHITECTURE), package description, and source comments, replacing\nthem with neutral level-of-detail timeline language while preserving the\ntechnical meaning.\n\nRebrand the example/demo to DeepCivic''s visual identity:\n- Public Sans font, warm off-white (#f5f0e6) page background, warm-brown\n  (#7a6a5a) accents and dark warm ink (#1e1a17) for the canvas stage.\n- Align the kit''s default component palette (Timeline, Lens, toolbar,\n  annotation layer, time axis) to the DeepCivic tokens so the showcase\n  reads on-brand, with focus-visible outlines for keyboard users.\n- Add a DeepCivic wordmark to the demo header and relabel the synthetic\n  example entities with Australian open-government sources.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Va334KKtijAFFqdxvFUezV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBXU7wdU\nr2aVKRxIYcU7X0OH/kZateii/V5eR1lBQDo4GbFudG/zwU12O8PmLkFpo9OqVvfk1mWDKlcfYPIS\ntgQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-29T06:46:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://