API client via `installAuthRefresh()` (from\nAuthProvider). apiFetch now retries an authenticated request once through a\nsilent refresh when it returns 401; on refresh failure it clears tokens so the\nroute guard redirects to /login. Add client + service tests and README docs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"345f536a39a5377292cc4e78a0a00dbcfa5db269","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramadhinzaid/mini-erp-web/git/trees/345f536a39a5377292cc4e78a0a00dbcfa5db269"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramadhinzaid/mini-erp-web/git/commits/b508032fbbce70e18d1e859fc725fcc54454cad0","verification":{"payload":"tree 345f536a39a5377292cc4e78a0a00dbcfa5db269\nparent 5f18ec12b8072e20793f94e26fb6533fb475cc11\nauthor ramadhinzaid <ramadhinzaid@gmail.com> 1782975362 +0700\ncommitter ramadhinzaid <ramadhinzaid@gmail.com> 1782975362 +0700\n\nfeat(auth): silent token refresh on 401\n\nWire the refresh token into the frontend. Add auth.service `refresh()`\n(POST /auth/refresh, persists the new pair) and a deduped `handleAuthRefresh`\nhandler registered with the API client via `installAuthRefresh()` (from\nAuthProvider). apiFetch now retries an authenticated request once through a\nsilent refresh when it returns 401; on refresh failure it clears tokens so the\nroute guard redirects to /login. Add client + service tests and README docs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVqf2JuTiwdGd3AkwNUjUuLI2Jn\nKdey+NXdt0TZZooNwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCG/z3rmcw3y605iVbPlRcJ2XQyLYyGXtjegimoMp23dWXo/jpNtvLe2FJG1t8pfcF\npYzDPjUiMY0WqoVZNNgwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61625805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramadhinzaid/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://ap