iaa30/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maiiaa30/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maiiaa30/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maiiaa30/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maiiaa30","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Maiiaa30/ReconDashboard/commits/5d4e5f9f2f6d5ce6b01c06187b049cdf3c982e03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:44:40Z","email":"diogomaia2003@gmail.com","name":"Maia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:44:40Z","email":"diogomaia2003@gmail.com","name":"Maia"},"message":"feat(ai): suggest-only assists - intruder explain, payload mutate, secret triage, chain narrate\n\nNew src/ai/assists.ts with four fail-soft, read-only assists (reuse util/llm;\nthe model never touches the wire, never mutates a finding, never enqueues a\nscan):\n\n- explainIntruderRow: given a run''s baseline + an interesting row (with the\n  T19 body excerpt), explain why it deviates and whether it looks exploitable.\n- suggestPayloadMutation: on a blocked payload, return ENCODER-CHAIN names\n  (validated against the deterministic TRANSFORM registry, so applyChain can\n  run them) - not new payloads.\n- suggestSecretTriage: classify the FP-heavy jsrecon/secret findings as\n  likely_real vs likely_placeholder (suggestion only).\n- narrateChain: deterministic Task-9 chain structure + LLM prose.\n\nRoutes under /api (session-authed, not scan-gated) each degrade to\n{ enabled:false, note } with no LLM. The Intruder interesting-rows table\ngains an inline \"explain\" action. Unit-tested: fail-soft-when-disabled for\nall four, encoder-chain validation drops unknown transform names, and the\nexplain happy/missing-job paths (llm mocked).","tree":{"sha":"696e67816c7e38fe78f25baa9b7a64ccd78aca7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Maiiaa30/ReconDashboard/git/trees/696e67816c7e38fe78f25baa9b7a64ccd78ac