ers/Maiiaa30/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maiiaa30/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maiiaa30/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maiiaa30","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Maiiaa30/ReconDashboard/commits/fbe4686325c3213b09d486ba9ac25ba1d71b53b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:32:12Z","email":"diogomaia2003@gmail.com","name":"Maia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:32:12Z","email":"diogomaia2003@gmail.com","name":"Maia"},"message":"feat(owasp): CORS Vary:Origin cacheable flag + suffix-escape origin\n\nA per-origin-reflected ACAO with no `Vary: Origin` can be cached by a shared\ncache / CDN and served to other users (CORS cache poisoning). corsVerdict\nnow takes the Vary header and threads a `cacheable` flag that bumps a\nnon-credentialed reflection from medium to high. Also add the suffix-escape\nprobe origin (https://<host>evil.example.org - the host directly\nconcatenated) which defeats a naive startsWith(host) allowlist. The CORS\nfinding notes \"no Vary: Origin - poisonable via shared caches\". Verdict logic\nunit-tested for cacheable vs non-cacheable and the suffix-escape reflection.","tree":{"sha":"1dfe15e0adbb8f30f883109c0dcb384e3e8312fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Maiiaa30/ReconDashboard/git/trees/1dfe15e0adbb8f30f883109c0dcb384e3e8312fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Maiiaa30/ReconDashboard/git/commits/fbe4686325c3213b09d486ba9ac25ba1d71b53b2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46065883?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maiiaa30/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maiiaa30/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maiiaa30/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https